390 1072 #uuid "1c3c2591-89b8-5e94-a7b0-e02f5b424693" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399390 1074 "To apply the ratio test, we define ${a}_{n}=\\frac{(x+5)^{n}}{n(n+1)}.$ Then, we calculate the ratio of two successive terms and take the limit as $n\\to \\infty :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{(x+5)^{n+1}}{(n+1)(n+2)}\\cdot \\frac{n(n+1)}{(x+5)^{n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{n(x+5)}{n+2}| \\\\  & =|x+5|{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{n}{n+2} \\\\  & =|x+5|{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }(\\frac{1}{(1+\\frac{2}{n})}) \\\\  & =|x+5|\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =|x+5|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe series converges if $L<1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|x+5| & <1 \\\\ -1<x+5 & <1 \\\\ -6<x & <-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the radius of convergence is $R=1,$ and the series converges for any $x$ that lies in the open interval $(-6,-4).$\n\nThe ratio test gives no conclusion about the convergence of the series when $L=1.$ So, when $|x+5|=1,$ we do not know if the series converges. This means that the endpoints $x=-6$ and $x=-4$ need to be investigated separately using another test for convergence.\n\n- When $x=-6$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(x+5)^{n}}{n(n+1)} & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-6+5)^{n}}{n(n+1)} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}+n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is convergent by the alternating series test.\n\n- When $x=-4$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(x+5)^{n}}{n(n+1)} & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-4+5)^{n}}{n(n+1)} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{1}^{n}}{{n}^{2}+n} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{2}+n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the above series with  ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{2}},$\nwe see that the series is convergent by the comparison test.\n\nSo the interval of convergence is $I=[-6,-4].$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399391 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399392 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399391 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399393 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399391 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399394 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399391 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399395 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399391 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399396 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399391 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399391 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399391 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399394 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399391 1080 #uuid "f3aed52a-be07-5913-ae72-4601a0fc9425" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399392 1081 "$R=5$ and $I=[-1,1]$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399392 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399392 1084 #uuid "ae1e039d-033d-5fb2-afe2-058a41532346" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399393 1081 "$R=1$ and $I=(-6,-4)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399393 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399393 1084 #uuid "b5518e7e-ad19-5fdf-b048-f6f07aa85005" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399394 1081 "$R=1$ and $I=[-6,-4]$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399394 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399394 1084 #uuid "a777899f-4fb2-599e-8bac-fd1080f27455" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399395 1081 "$R=5$ and $I=(-1,1)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399395 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399395 1084 #uuid "730ca820-682a-52b2-87ed-4d379934e772" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399396 1081 "$R=1$ and $I=[-6,-4)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399396 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399396 1084 #uuid "89a3a902-db89-527e-ac98-aebc7e8b5c3b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399397 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399398 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399397 1069 "q-103781" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399397 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399397 1071 "A hot air balloon that is launched vertically is observed by a child located on the ground $4\\,\\text{km}$ from the launch site. What is the vertical speed of the balloon at the instant when its distance from the child is $5\\,\\text{km}$ and this distance is increasing at a rate of $12\\,\\text{km/h}?$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399397 1072 #uuid "861245ce-e152-550e-a0d5-a98fa38203e9" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399397 1074 "We start by drawing a diagram of the problem.\n\n![](images/40/40957ce27304474263d1d231a3a0df93193ac0461d8a7444cde3b12047d1a214.png)\n\nIn the diagram,\n\n- $x$ is the distance between the child and the launch site,\n\n- $y$ is the distance between the launch site and the balloon,\n\n- $z$ is the distance between the child and the balloon.\n\nAs shown in the diagram, $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ form a right triangle with $z$ as the hypotenuse. We wish to find the rate of change of $y,$ which is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}.$ \n\nWe know that $z=5\\,\\text{km}$ and $x=4\\,\\text{km}.$ We can find $y$ using the Pythagorean Theorem, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ {4}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={5}^{2} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =9 \\\\ y & =3\\,\\text{km}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that:\n\n- $\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}=12\\,\\text{km}/\\text{h},$\n\n- the distance between the child and the launch site ($x$) remains the same, so $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=0.$\n\nFinally, we differentiate both sides of ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={z}^{2}$ with respect to $t$ and then substitute in the known values, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({z}^{2}) \\\\ 2x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =2z\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ 2(4)(0)+2(3)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =2(5)(12) \\\\ 6\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =120 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{120}{6} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertical speed of the hot air balloon is $20\\,\\text{km}/\\text{h}.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399398 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399399 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399398 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399400 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399398 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399401 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399398 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399402 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399398 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399403 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399398 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399398 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399398 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399399 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399398 1080 #uuid "9d3c6cce-0af7-56ae-b62a-c1633c9bc4d4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399399 1081 "20\\,\\text{km/h}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399399 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399399 1084 #uuid "d1a38a30-8bac-5468-8fc8-e062c24e84e9" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399400 1081 "12\\,\\text{km/h}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399400 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399400 1084 #uuid "2ee69ac9-d35a-5e97-8f90-c9134043ab2e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399401 1081 "22\\,\\text{km/h}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399401 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399401 1084 #uuid "e1875e6f-6a69-5440-9e5d-70da4eede3b6" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399402 1081 "18\\,\\text{km/h}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399402 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399402 1084 #uuid "9b355bd5-cbe7-5ac4-861e-9679d2919c24" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399403 1081 "21\\,\\text{km/h}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399403 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399403 1084 #uuid "9ac6560e-0780-5b4e-8401-cff5e6d38baa" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399404 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399405 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399404 1069 "q-103812" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399404 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399404 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$\n\nI. The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1].$\nII. $y=-1$ is the maximum value of the function.\nIII. $x=15\\pi $ is in the domain." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399404 1072 #uuid "4383ecaa-1c57-5705-8853-cba2341fc9fa" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399404 1074 "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ),$ therefore the function doesn't have a maximum value. Hence, statements I and II are both false.\n\n- The function's domain is all real numbers except the integer multiples of $\\pi $, such as $0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,….$ Hence, statement III is false." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399405 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399406 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399405 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399407 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399405 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399408 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399405 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399409 1319413953347