17592186399488 1074 "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2{x}^{2}-x+2 \\\\  & 3x-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{6{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+7x+4\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,3{x}^{2}+7x+4 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,3{x}^{2}+\\,\\,x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6x+4 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6x-2}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are \n\n$\\,$ $2{x}^{2}-x+2\\,$ and $\\,-3{x}^{2}+x.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399489 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399490 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399489 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399491 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399489 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399492 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399489 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399489 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399494 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399489 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399489 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399489 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399492 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399489 1080 #uuid "c64ca425-bacd-5a4c-ad53-32525c95cc75" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399490 1081 "$2{x}^{2}-2x+1\\,$ and $\\,-3{x}^{2}+x$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399490 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399490 1084 #uuid "9ed9271b-c279-5a55-948c-92d0d1f3cb4f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399491 1081 "$2{x}^{2}+x+2\\,$ and $\\,+3{x}^{2}-x$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399491 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399491 1084 #uuid "8998fe59-12df-54be-b54d-ca8f0f8a155a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399492 1081 "$2{x}^{2}-x+2\\,$ and $\\,-3{x}^{2}+x$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399492 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399492 1084 #uuid "8c584647-74c7-50d8-b7b4-101a4b15dae4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399493 1081 "$2{x}^{2}+2x+1\\,$ and $\\,6{x}^{2}+x$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399493 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399493 1084 #uuid "84021088-abb5-5ad2-8756-f12c652e2c35" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399494 1081 "$2{x}^{2}-2x+2\\,$ and $\\,-6{x}^{2}+x$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399494 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399494 1084 #uuid "f1db7d2c-8cf3-5b19-8259-5193b46ec41d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399495 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399496 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399495 1069 "q-105701" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399495 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399495 1071 "The function $g(x)$ is continuous over $x\\in [2,7].$ Some values of $g(x)$ are given in the table below. \n\n| $x$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(x)$ | $-2$ | $1$ | $-3$ | $1$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n\nWhat is the smallest possible number of solutions to the equation $g(x)=-1?$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399495 1072 #uuid "07c30a16-0504-5c16-ba6b-3435983938c4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399495 1074 "Since $g$ is a continuous function on $[2,7]$, we can apply the intermediate value theorem (IVT) in any subinterval of $[2,7].$\n\nSo, we will go through each subinterval of $[2,7]$ and check if the IVT guarantees a solution to the equation $g(x)=-1.$\n\n- On the subinterval $[2,3],$ we have $g(2)=-2$ and $g(3)=1.$ Since $-1\\in [-2,1],$  the IVT *does * guarantee a solution to the equation $g(x)=-1$ on this subinterval.\n\n- On the subinterval $[3,4],$ we have $g(3)=1$ and $g(4)=-3.$ Since $-1\\in [-3,1],$ the IVT *does* guarantee a solution to the equation $g(x)=-1$ on this subinterval.\n\n- On the subinterval $[4,5],$ we have $g(4)=-3$ and $g(5)=1.$ Since $-1\\in [-3,1],$ the IVT *does * guarantee a solution to the equation $g(x)=-1$ on this subinterval.\n\n- On the subinterval $[5,6],$ we have $g(5)=1$ and $g(6)=0.$ Since $-1\\notin [0,1],$ the IVT does *not* guarantee a solution to the equation $g(x)=-1$ on this subinterval.\n\n- On the subinterval $[6,7],$ we have $g(6)=0$ and $g(7)=2.$ Since $-1\\notin [0,2],$ the IVT does *not* guarantee a solution to the equation $g(x)=-1$ on this subinterval.\n\nThe IVT guarantees solutions to $g(x)=-1$ on the subintervals $[2,3],$ $[3,4]$  and $[4,5].$ Therefore, $g(x)=-1$ has at least three solutions on $[2,7].$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399496 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399497 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399496 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399498 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399496 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399496 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399496 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399501 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399496 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399496 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399496 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399497 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399496 1080 #uuid "5d82b2e4-6f95-5829-98a0-f3c805de2c17" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399497 1081 "3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399497 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399497 1084 #uuid "8858bd6f-a8b4-5fe8-a1a9-895135df061c" 13194139533478