9 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399518 1084 #uuid "11d35582-3a44-5c08-8455-d2f9e84525d5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399519 1081 "x=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399519 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399519 1084 #uuid "aba5b46d-91ae-5e56-a685-c83b09b8b31b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399520 1081 "x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399520 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399520 1084 #uuid "d7d5554c-9aa3-5296-9ebc-642d7ab8668d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399521 1081 "x=36\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=9\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399521 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399521 1084 #uuid "21ab22a6-9eb5-5460-a37a-51dabf9c5da8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399522 1081 "x=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399522 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399522 1084 #uuid "a8369c3d-7d61-5b31-87ce-5b1b018ff986" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399523 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399524 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399523 1069 "q-106585" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399523 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399523 1071 "Find the points that satisfy the mean value theorem for $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}-{z}^{3}$ on the line segment $\\overset{―}{AB},$ where the position vectors of $A$ and $B$ are $a=⟨-1,0,1⟩$ and $b=⟨0,1,0⟩,$ respectively." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399523 1072 #uuid "6a0cb1f4-667e-57bd-8d19-2b32f34f6a8a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399523 1074 "The mean value theorem states that if $f(x,y,z)$ is differentiable at each point on the line segment $\\overset{―}{AB},$ then there exists a point $C\\in \\overset{―}{AB}$ with position vector $c$ such that\n\n$$\nf(b)-f(a)=∇f(c)·(b-a).\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}-{z}^{3}$ is differentiable at each point on the line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ So, we can apply the mean value theorem.\n\nSubstituting $a=⟨-1,0,1⟩$ and $b=⟨0,1,0⟩$ into the above expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,1,0)-f(-1,0,1) & =∇f(c)\\cdot (⟨0,1,0⟩-⟨-1,0,1⟩) \\\\ 0-0 & =∇f(c)\\cdot ⟨1,1,-1⟩ \\\\ 0 & =∇f(c)\\cdot ⟨1,1,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $∇f$ and evaluating at $c=⟨{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}⟩,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨2x,0,-3{z}^{2}⟩ \\\\ ∇f(c) & =⟨2{c}_{1},0,-3{c}_{3}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =∇f(c)\\cdot ⟨1,1,-1⟩ \\\\ 0 & =⟨2{c}_{1},0,-3{c}_{3}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨1,1,-1⟩ \\\\ 0 & =2{c}_{1}+3{c}_{3}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $C$ lies on $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ So, let's first find the equation of the line.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-(-1)}{1} & =\\frac{y-0}{1}=\\frac{z-1}{(-1)} \\\\ x+1 & =y=1-z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nParametrizing the line, we get\n\n$$\nx=t-1\\,\\,y=t,\\,z=1-t,\\,0\\le t\\le 1.\n$$\n\nSince $c=⟨{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}⟩$ satisfies the equation of the line, we have\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=t-1\\,\\,{c}_{2}=t,\\,{c}_{3}=1-t.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above in the equation $2{c}_{1}+3{c}_{3}^{2}=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(t-1)+3(1-t)^{2} & =0 \\\\ (t-1)[2+3(t-1)] & =0 \\\\ (t-1)(3t-1) & =0 \\\\ t & =\\frac{1}{3},\\,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we proceed to find the coordinates of the points that satisfy the mean value theorem.\n\n- For $t=\\frac{1}{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{3}-1=-\\frac{2}{3}, \\\\ {c}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{3}, \\\\ {c}_{3} & =1-\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the coordinates of the first point $C$ are $(-\\frac{2}{3},\\frac{1}{3},\\frac{2}{3}).$\n\n- For $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} & =1-1=0, \\\\ {c}_{2} & =1, \\\\ {c}_{3} & =1-1=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the coordinates of the second point $C$ are $(0,1,0).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399524 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399525 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399524 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399526 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399524 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399527 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399524 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399528 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399524 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399529 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399524 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399524 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399524 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399527 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399524 1080 #uuid "b7e2b45d-5b9d-5091-9941-06bd82a064b8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399525 1081 "$(-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{2}{3},\\frac{1}{2})$ and $(-\\frac{2}{3},\\frac{1}{3},\\frac{2}{3})$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399525 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399525 1084 #uuid "b63ab9ff-56cc-569e-a2eb-37c7b01b50d4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399526 1081 "$(-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{2}{3},\\frac{1}{2})$ and $(0,1,0)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399526 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399526 1084 #uuid "ccb712d9-a5c5-5d8c-831a-ab2ad2eb58be" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399527 1081 "$(-\\frac{2}{3},\\frac{1}{3},\\frac{2}{3})$ and $(0,1,0)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399527 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399527 1084 #uuid "c0e7b9b8-1b51-5d9a-a752-82b801722063" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399528 1081 "$(-1,0,1)$ and $(-\\frac{1}{3},