\\frac{7}{3}.$ To find the velocity at this moment, we substitute this back into $v(t)$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(\\frac{7}{3}) & =14(\\frac{7}{3})-3{(\\frac{7}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{98}{3}-\\frac{49}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{49}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399678 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399679 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399678 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399680 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399678 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399681 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399678 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399682 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399678 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399683 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399678 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399678 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399678 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399681 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399678 1080 #uuid "1669c4fe-448a-5ecd-96c2-60941d083824" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399679 1081 "t=\\frac{3}{2},\\,v=-\\frac{9}{2}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399679 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399679 1084 #uuid "e1f8e3ed-64ac-534b-9097-97dd33f2545d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399680 1081 "t=2,\\,v=-4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399680 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399680 1084 #uuid "106f9321-de03-58f4-8540-f31885a755c3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399681 1081 "t=\\frac{7}{3},\\,v=\\frac{49}{3}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399681 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399681 1084 #uuid "084bda93-d0d6-514b-b8c7-73ce821b2053" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399682 1081 "t=2,\\,v=6" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399682 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399682 1084 #uuid "367c159c-f8cf-54ab-9cdc-cfddc4ed2a5b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399683 1081 "t=\\frac{7}{3},\\,v=\\frac{15}{6}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399683 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399683 1084 #uuid "212ea060-615f-5258-8e09-ac350ea1ca59" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399684 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399685 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399684 1069 "q-109639" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399684 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399684 1071 "The second-order initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-4{e}^{t}{y}^{′}+5y=0,\\,y(0)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-1\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{1}(0)=p \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}=f(t),\\, & {x}_{2}(0)=q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{′}(t),$ and $p$ and $q$ are constants. Calculate  $(p-q)\\cdot f(t).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399684 1072 #uuid "ebf9231a-650d-5b8c-8818-efc1d0c42664" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399684 1074 "First, we make the following change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =y \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={y}^{′}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also convert the initial conditions, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & ={x}_{1}(0)=2 \\\\ {y}^{′}(0) & ={x}_{2}(0)=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equations with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{″}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={y}^{″}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt this point, we're almost done. We just need to write the right-hand side of the last equation in terms of ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}.$\n\nSolving our original differential equation for the highest-order derivative $({y}^{″}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=4{e}^{t}{y}^{′}-5y.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=4{e}^{t}{x}_{2}-5{x}_{1}.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{1}(0)=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}=-5{x}_{1}+4{e}^{t}{x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{2}(0)=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $p=2,q=-1,f(t)=-5{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2},$ and \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(p-q)\\cdot f(t) & =(2-(-1))(-5{x}_{1}+4{e}^{t}{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =3(-5{x}_{1}+4{e}^{t}{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =-15{x}_{1}+12{e}^{t}{x}_{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399685 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399686 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399685 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399687 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399685 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399688 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399685 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399689 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399685 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399690 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399685 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399685 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399685 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399686 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399685 1080 #uuid "8605a456-8f74-549b-ba68-da660540b8c0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399686 1081 "-15{x}_{1}+12{e}^{t}{x}_{2}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399686 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399686 1084 #uuid "af7079ea-861b-500c-9d7f-1e6deedf2499" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399687 1081 "15{e}^{t}{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399687 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399687 1084 #uuid "6b240488-157e-59e5-bed1-15811d8bfd83" 13194139533478 1759