 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399801 1071 "Determine the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}-9}{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+6x-12}.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399801 1072 #uuid "046b8096-a4b3-5639-81fd-05cfaf3fcc14" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399801 1074 "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-9}{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+6x-12} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+3)(x-3)}{{x}^{2}(x-2)+6(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+3)(x-3)}{({x}^{2}+6)(x-2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the denominator equal to zero. This gives\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+6)(x-2)=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve the above equation using the zero product property:\n\n- Solving $x-2=0$ gives the solution $x=2.$\n\n- The equation ${x}^{2}+6=0$ has no real solutions.\n\nTherefore, the only vertical asymptote is $x=2.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399802 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399803 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399802 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399804 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399802 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399805 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399802 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399806 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399802 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399807 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399802 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399802 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399802 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399805 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399802 1080 #uuid "9de2cff7-92c8-5c70-9102-18ed3f31a5ce" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399803 1081 "$x=0$ and $x=2$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399803 10