045585 true] [17592186399819 1084 #uuid "f8d8695e-5196-5de3-8a7b-43fe3997211b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399820 1081 "$4{x}^{2}+10x+45\\,$ and $\\,11{x}^{2}-x-5$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399820 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399820 1084 #uuid "07b0d23d-ec2d-59ef-9ff0-7ee1b6fd0027" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399821 1081 "$4{x}^{2}-11x+45\\,$ and $\\,11{x}^{2}-2x-5$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399821 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399821 1084 #uuid "27453f3a-03ff-59ee-9447-15e61177956e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399822 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399823 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399822 1069 "q-113767" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399822 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399822 1071 "Given the function $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{{e}^{x}},$ which of the following statements are true?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399822 1072 #uuid "5d605cec-3072-5304-adcf-70f0f4b40d1d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399822 1074 "First, we find the stationary points. Differentiating $f(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{2x{e}^{x}-({x}^{2}+1){e}^{x}}{{e}^{2x}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{x}^{2}-2x+1}{{e}^{x}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{{e}^{x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{{e}^{x}}\\,⟹\\,x=1.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the fact that ${e}^{x}>0$ for all values of $x.$\n\nSo, $x=1$ is the only stationary point of $f(x).$ Next, to determine whether this point is a local maximum or minimum, we use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's choose the test points $x=0,2$ and evaluate the first derivative at these points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(0) & =-\\frac{(0-1)^{2}}{{e}^{0}}=-1<0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & =-\\frac{(2-1)^{2}}{{e}^{2}}=-{e}^{-2}<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe summarize the information in a table, shown below.\n\n| $x$ | $(-\\infty ,1)$ | $1$ | $(1,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Test Point | $0$ |  | $2$ |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $-$ | $0$ | $-$ |\n| $f$ | $↘$ |  | $↘$ |\n\nThe first derivative does not change sign at $x=1.$ Therefore, we conclude that $x=1$ is neither a minimum nor a maximum.\n\nTherefore, the first derivative test shows that the function has no local extrema." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399823 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399824 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399823 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399825 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399823 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399826 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399823 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399827 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399823 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399828 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399823 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399823 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399823 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399826 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399823 1080 #uuid "9f06b88a-0b3e-517c-8884-684e65abf6f2" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399824 1081 "There is a local minimum at $x=-1$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399824 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399824 1084 #uuid "4d2b2d3d-bc75-52df-bb2c-abdcbe9305ba" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399825 1081 "There is a local minimum at $x=1$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399825 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399825 1084 #uuid "4b4bfed4-7246-5315-9221-f89dd61376e7" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399826 1081 "The function $f(x)$ has no local extrema" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399826 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399826 1084 #uuid "a324b8bd-f18d-5775-a6a5-02c9e56e4b3b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399827 1081 "There is a local maximum at $x=-1$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399827 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399827 1084 #uuid "d961280f-42a3-5c74-8167-a78423307df5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399828 1081 "There is a local maximum at $x=1$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399828 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399828 1084 #uuid "2b36fc7f-e874-5627-a39c-c2930cf8cca1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399829 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399830 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399829 1069 "q-114262" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399829 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399829 1071 "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & x-6\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{2}+0x-4} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{2}-36x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{36x-216}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,212\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399829 1072 #uuid "3536c096-9c19-5ecb-8cd6-bf3a33c8475e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399829 1074 "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x$-term. So, we write it using a zero coefficient, as follows: \n\n$$\n6{x}^{2}+0x-4\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6x+36 \\\\  & x-6\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{2}+0x-4} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{2}-36x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,36x-4 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{36x-216}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,212\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\,$ $6x+36\\,$ and $\\,36x-4.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399830 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399831 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399830 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399832 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399830 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399833 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399830 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399834 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399830 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399835 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399830 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399830 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399830 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399835 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399830 1080 #uuid "aeb0dafe-c8dd-5892-9eb8-f305e87ca008" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399831 1081 "$6x+48\\,$ and $\\,48x-8$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399831 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399831 1084 #uuid "e6409232-2d31-593b-90bb-8a5813883aaa" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399832 1081 "$6x-24\\,$ and $\\,24x-4$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399832 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399832 1084 #uuid "8add39dc-99a4-5ff4-9055-09c5f3363d40" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399833 1081 "$6x+30\\,$ and $\\,30x-6$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399833 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399833 1084 #uuid "aa8cd1cd-1378-56d5-a7ab-7daa3b9b05fe" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399834 1081 "$6x-36\\,$ and $\\,48x-4$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399834 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399834 1084 #uuid "29edcf41-1ad2-52f3-ab8d-9b28e983225b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399835 1081 "$6x+36\\,$ and $\\,36x-4$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399835 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399835 1084 #uuid "f2683559-249d-5d23-9f72-d0c8764dba6c" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399836 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399837 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399836 1069 "q-114399" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399836 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399836 1071 "![](images/8f/8f20b09e85ce71a1001e7c701ebfafa3e6ac6c8adb29e8dfd47f256f37a29f5f.png)\n\nThe function $h(x)$ is continuous and twice-differentiable for all $x$ in $(-4,1.5)$ The graph $y={h}^{″}(x)$ is shown above. At what value(s) of $x$ does $h(x)$ have a point of inflection?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399836 1072 #uuid "959a29f9-94e3-5ec3-bf75-8100c4fac3c4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399836 1074 "First, notice that since $h(x)$ is twice-differentiable, the tangent line to the graph exists for all real $x.$\n\nInflection points occur when a graph changes concavity. In order for the graph to change concavity, the value of the second derivative ${h}^{″}(x)$ must switch signs. So, we are looking for points where the graph of ${h}^{″}(x)$ crosses the $x$-axis.\n\nWe can see that the graph $y={h}^{″}(x)$ crosses the $x$-axis at $x=-1$ and $x=1.$ \n\nTherefore, $h(x)$ has points of inflection at $x=-1$ and $x=1.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399837 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399838 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399837 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399839 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399837 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399840 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399837 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399841 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399837 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399842 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399837 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399837 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399837 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399842 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399837 1080 #uuid "04b865a5-78da-5138-9a6e-a4f61421c384" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399838 1081 "$x=-3$ and $x=-1$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399838 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399838 1084 #uuid "60d399bd-315a-5c25-b63b-0a7391724a1e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399839 1081 "$x=-3$ and $x=1$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399839 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399839 1084 #uuid "920e6436-61f2-5a55-8fd8-6326ab8c0807" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399840 1081 "$x=-1$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399840 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399840 1084 #uuid "d4e096b7-2688-5afd-8241-00c938c02da0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399841 1081 "$x=-3,$ $x=-1$ and $x=1$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399841 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399841 1084 #uuid "596b5a75-fa8d-518b-b2eb-9eb7b3a09dac" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399842 1081 "$x=-1$ and $x=1$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399842 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399842 1084 #uuid "c210c0cc-3f26-5461-99d3-ddbe6f537e73" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399843 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399844 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399843 1069 "q-114402" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399843 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399843 1071 "![](images/20/20b6532fc5d99c74a26bd752e19aa2a6451ea26a79d2a129e4c0203bc9133354.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is continuous and twice-differentiable for all $x$ in $(-4,4).$ The graph $y={f}^{″}(x)$ is shown above. At what value(s) of $x$ does $f(x)$ have a point of inflection?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399843 1072 #uuid "444031a3-3309-59e7-a714-c81365022d27" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399843 1074 "First, notice that since $f(x)$ is twice-differentiable, the tangent line to the graph exists for all real $x.$\n\nInflection points occur when a graph changes concavity. In order for the graph to change concavity, the value of the second derivative ${f}^{″}(x)$ must switch signs. So, we are looking for points where the graph of ${f}^{″}(x)$ crosses the $x$-axis.\n\nWe can see that the graph $y={f}^{″}(x)$ crosses the $x$-axis at $x=-2,$ $x=1,$ and $x=3.$ \n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has points of inflection at $x=-2,$ $x=1,$ and $x=3.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399844 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399845 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399844 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399846 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399844 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399847 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399844 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399848 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399844 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399849 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399844 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399844 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399844 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399848 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399844 1080 #uuid "989f84dd-5950-58e9-b6c6-2ad30ae07799" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399845 1081 "$x=-2$ and $x=1$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399845 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399845 1084 #uuid "13fdeb0d-d904-56f6-8b96-e74fb1d0181b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399846 1081 "$x=0$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399846 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399846 1084 #uuid "837da0ae-38ee-520a-bb45-9843ff8b7fee" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399847 1081 "$x=1$ and $x=3$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399847 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 