ef 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399853 1084 #uuid "98942d10-5093-5b9e-b56e-6cb0c197d275" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399854 1081 "$x=-1$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399854 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399854 1084 #uuid "94d7a6b5-dc7f-5665-8396-f95fbd37d4d2" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399855 1081 "$g(x)$ has no inflection points" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399855 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399855 1084 #uuid "1d987e38-5562-5ec2-8fa2-95ef362d9640" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399856 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399857 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399856 1069 "q-115134" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399856 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399856 1071 "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{49}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}=1?$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399856 1072 #uuid "3113828e-6ca6-530b-804d-2cdc91aade73" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399856 1074 "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=49$ and ${b}^{2}=36.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=49,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{49}=7.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=36,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{36}=6.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $a=7,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=6.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 7=14,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 6=12.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399857 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399858 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [175921