045585 true] [17592186399870 1074 "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=-6$ and $k=-4,$ so the center is located at $(-6,-4).$\n\nIn the given equation, we also have ${a}^{2}=5$ and ${b}^{2}=9.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=5,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{5}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=9,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{9}=3.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=3,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=\\sqrt{5}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 3=6,$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\sqrt{5}=2\\sqrt{5}.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399871 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399872 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399871 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399873 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399871 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399874 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399871 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399875 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399871 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399876 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399871 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399871 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399871 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399876 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399871 1080 #uuid "1872eebc-f1ce-56c5-86dd-93ce7b60f7ed" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399872 1081 "$9$ and $5$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399872 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399872 1084 #uuid "ff3dd05f-a366-554a-ba55-c8784fb9b96f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399873 1081 "$4.5$ and $2.5$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399873 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [1759218