 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399892 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399891 1069 "q-115364" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399891 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399891 1071 "![](images/3a/3af3101fd7a103e8382755177ca1ebab9bc1cdf48aebd34af8ac7cc92991387c.png)\n\nGiven that the points $(-1,2)$ and $(1,4)$ lie on a diameter of a circle, what are the center and radius of the circle?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399891 1072 #uuid "a02e3599-0d24-591c-985f-c45e9f652ee9" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399891 1074 "The center of the circle is located at the midpoint of the diameter. So, we can calculate the coordinates of the center using the midpoint formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(h,k) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{-1+1}{2},\\frac{2+4}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{0}{2},\\frac{6}{2}) \\\\  & =(0,3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe radius can be found by calculating the distance between the center $(0,3)$ and a point on the circle, such as $(-1,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{{({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})}^{2}+{({y}_{1}-{y}_{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(-1-0)}^{2}+{(2-3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399892 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399893 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399892 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399894 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399892 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399895 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399892 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399896 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399892 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399897 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399892 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399892 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399892 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399897 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399892 1080 #uuid "