68 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399973 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399968 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399968 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399968 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399972 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399968 1080 #uuid "564afc56-93e1-5116-bc1b-3a39fadf5bbd" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399969 1081 "113" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399969 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399969 1084 #uuid "1e208d2b-dec6-562a-a378-e1098ccc8637" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399970 1081 "80" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399970 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399970 1084 #uuid "95086ebb-7581-57b3-a760-1b80ee3581dd" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399971 1081 "72.5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399971 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399971 1084 #uuid "d51ba212-184c-5759-8461-dffee9f36c0d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399972 1081 "84.5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399972 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399972 1084 #uuid "6365eea9-1bba-56eb-bc53-b9734f86d4ad" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399973 1081 "169" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399973 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399973 1084 #uuid "d5f4da11-8df3-5c32-9ef0-645590937087" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399974 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399975 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399974 1069 "q-117369" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399974 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399974 1071 "Which of the following points lies on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x?$\n\nI. $(-1,-\\frac{\\pi }{4})$\nII. $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3})$\nIII. $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},1)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399974 1072 #uuid "d42d29a1-7ec6-555e-8ef7-3216eb563375" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399974 1074 "In order for a point $(a,b)$ to lie on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ the following conditions must hold:\n\n- The reflected point $(b,a)$ must lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$\n\n- The $y$-value of the point must lie in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ which is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of the points. \n\n- First,  we consider the point $(-1,-\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(-\\frac{\\pi }{4},-1)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(-1,-\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n- Next, we consider the point $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\sqrt{3})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, we consider the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},1).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(1,\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$  $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},1)$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399975 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399976 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399975 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399977 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399975 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399978 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399975 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399979 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399975 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399980 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399975 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399975 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399975 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399980 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399975 1080 #uuid "f2f8be92-1eeb-51f2-9522-8aecb4bbebb3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399976 1081 "I, II, and III" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399976 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399976 1084 #uuid "fa719b7d-d1ee-5649-b870-8f8a3d1177c4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399977 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399977 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399977 1084 #uuid "18dee54a-fce8-5dc3-a798-772a50cd8901" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399978 1081 "I only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399978 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399978 1084 #uuid "730c0a62-4f76-5705-9e0b-4a00253a74f7" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399979 1081 "III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399979 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399979 1084 #uuid "11d81d17-4b55-5d20-91dc-2a09540e3557" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399980 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399980 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399980 1084 #uuid "5bafb7b5-e251-5b4a-b330-592196d2fd1c" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399981 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399982 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399981 1069 "q-117737" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399981 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399981 1071 "Find the $x$-coordinates of the points where the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1$ intersects the line $x+2y=4$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399981 1072 #uuid "61ffdc01-8414-55ad-b1b4-42608bbe9957" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399981 1074 "First, we rearrange the equation $x+2y=4,$ as follows:\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{2}x+2\n$$\n\nTo find $x$-coordinates of the intersection points, we need to substitute $y=-\\frac{1}{2}x+2$ into the equation of the circle and solve the resulting equation for $x,$ if possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{(-\\frac{1}{2}x+2)}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-2x+4 & =1 \\\\ \\frac{5{x}^{2}}{4}-2x+3 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we compute the discriminant $D$ of the above quadratic equation, then we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={2}^{2}-4\\cdot \\frac{5}{4}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =4-15 \\\\  & =-11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $D=-11<0$, there are no real solutions to the equation $\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{4}-2x+3=0.$\n\nHence, we conclude that the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1$ does not intersect the line $x+2y=4$ at any point.\n\nThe corresponding diagram is shown below.\n\n![](images/40/400b997f9f1e83d6d2dd6c34b68a01ad4de5b352e40de2401eb516ca181f3163.png)" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399982 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399983 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399982 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399984 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399982 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399985 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399982 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399986 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399982 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399987 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399982 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399982 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399982 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399986 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399982 1080 #uuid "d47ad7cb-b24b-5fa1-931d-75679414940e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399983 1081 "$1$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399983 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399983 1084 #uuid "1712079f-0724-55c4-bcf9-4a641811e473" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399984 1081 "$2$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399984 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399984 1084 #uuid "964eca01-2ae2-551e-a658-79835ac5c947" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399985 1081 "$-1$ and $3$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399985 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399985 1084 #uuid "784750f3-6750-5c52-9edd-ecd848bdea7f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399986 1081 "The circle and the line do not intersect" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399986 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399986 1084 #uuid "c7cac279-8da9-592d-88fb-73f8fe0b7a5d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399987 1081 "$-2$ and $4$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399987 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399987 1084 #uuid "83bfd300-7ebf-55e8-b278-1ff27d7a64f7" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399988 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399989 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399988 1069 "q-118389" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399988 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399988 1071 "![](images/37/37434a61262f829160fc2b19fcadb67745a024d589cd1ce318ca4ab90d6ab2d9.png)\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the point $P$ on the curve $y=\\frac{x+1}{\\sqrt{x}}$ that is closest to the point $(2,0)$ satisfies the equation\n\n$$\n2x-3-\\boxed{\\phantom{AAAAAA}}=0.\n$$\n\n \nWhat is the missing expression?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399988 1072 #uuid "f0024a60-f6e5-5b56-9272-60dda6ebe058" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399988 1074 "Let's consider the *squared* distance $S$ between $(2,0)$ and a general point $P(x,y):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(x,y) & =(x-2)^{2}+(y-0)^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-4x+4+{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe require that the point $P$ lies on the curve $y=\\frac{x+1}{\\sqrt{x}}.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & ={x}^{2}-4x+4+{y}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-4x+4+{(\\frac{x+1}{\\sqrt{x}})}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-4x+4+\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{x} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-4x+4+\\frac{{x}^{2}+2x+1}{x} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-4x+4+x+2+\\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-3x+\\frac{1}{x}+6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the minimum distance, we take the first derivative of $S(x)$ and equate it to zero. This gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}^{′}(x)=2x-3-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399989 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399990 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399989 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399991 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399989 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399992 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399989 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399993 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399989 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399994 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399989 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399989 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399989 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399991 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399989 1080 #uuid "e83f0ff3-bc35-5721-8d0b-7a1f7fc531ac" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399990 1081 "\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399990 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399990 1084 #uuid "87a1b81f-6a01-51e3-8077-b35d6d3c965e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399991 1081 "\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399991 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399991 1084 #uuid "121d4c99-f9fd-560e-b8d1-8cf12f76ef01" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399992 1081 "\\frac{1}{x}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399992 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399992 1084 #uuid "37c5a8a6-835d-5948-a4e4-bc4371e503af" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399993 1081 "\\frac{1}{2x}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399993 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399993 1084 #uuid "ed218258-9b28-520e-b77f-948add6059b7" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399994 1081 "\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399994 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399994 1084 #uuid "1a5f6dc5-0cb2-55ae-b3d1-11c8ecd253e5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399995 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399996 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399995 1069 "q-119037" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399995 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399995 1071 "Find the general solution to the differential equation  ${f}^{′}(x)-6{e}^{-3x}=1.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399995 1072 #uuid "8e422fe9-fc97-5df0-b6a5-ce1fd6f9f5cf" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399995 1074 "First, we rearrange the equation to isolate the derivative term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =1+6{e}^{-3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (1+6{e}^{-3x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\text{d}x+6\\int {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x+6(-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-3x}) \\\\  & =x-2{e}^{-3x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [1759