/ref 17592186400063 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400058 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400058 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400058 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400063 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400058 1080 #uuid "72a057d8-e342-52dd-a1fb-abc1e06dc5c1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400059 1081 "| $-$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $+$ |" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400059 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400059 1084 #uuid "89a56145-d991-5f19-9125-7dfeb8c19018" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400060 1081 "| $-$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $+$ |" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400060 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400060 1084 #uuid "06d8b15d-ffbd-5909-a889-264a17e6ec09" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400061 1081 "| $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $+$ |" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400061 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400061 1084 #uuid "ff298d2d-031a-50d5-a2e0-d484276129ef" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400062 1081 "| $+$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $-$ |" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400062 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400062 1084 #uuid "bc19913c-5667-515a-bb6f-f55140f312eb" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400063 1081 "| $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $-$ |" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400063 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400063 1084 #uuid "af5764ad-7d4d-52f1-b5b0-d4fb0b6a16fc" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400064 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400065 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400064 1069 "q-122351" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400064 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400064 1071 "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis in the direction of increasing $x.$ When the displacement of $P$ from the origin $O$ is $x\\,\\text{m},$ its acceleration is $\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x+1}}\\,{m/s}^{2}.$ Initially, $P$ is at the origin $O$ and has velocity $v=4\\,m/s.$ Find $x$ as a function of time $t.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400064 1072 #uuid "528f1204-b150-5ae3-b3f2-1df94a35f90d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400064 1074 "![](images/ee/ee516744d915553bf962b498af522cf0006d42c5d0e0e2a003e6f385dd069e4a.png)\n\nSince the acceleration of the particle $P$ is $\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x+1}}\\,{m/s}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x+1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2})\n$$\n\nwe can rewrite our equation as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2})=\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x+1}}.\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides of the above equation with respect to $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x+1}}\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the general solution\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2} & =8\\sqrt{x+1}+K.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $x=0\\,\\text{m}$ when $v=4\\,\\text{m/s},$ we can find the value of the constant $K,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2} & =8\\sqrt{x+1}+K \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}(4)^{2} & =8\\sqrt{0+1}+K \\\\ 8 & =8+K \\\\ K & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2} & =8\\sqrt{x+1} \\\\ {v}^{2} & =16\\sqrt{x+1} \\\\ v & =\\pm 4\\sqrt[4]{x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the particle is moving in the direction of increasing  $x,$ we have that $v(x)>0,$ so we can discard the negative square root. Therefore,\n\n$$\nv(x)=4\\sqrt[4]{x+1}.\n$$\n\nNow, we know that $v=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}.$ Therefore, we have the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=4\\sqrt[4]{x+1}.\n$$\n\nSeparating the variables and integrating both sides with respect to $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =4\\sqrt[4]{x+1} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt[4]{x+1}}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =4 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt[4]{x+1}}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int 4\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}(x+1)^{3/4} & =4t+{C}_{1} \\\\ (x+1)^{3/4} & =3t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=\\frac{3{C}_{1}}{4}.$ \n\nWe're given that $x=0$ when $t=0.$ Therefore, $C=1,$ and the particular solution is\n\n$$\n(x+1)^{3/4}=3t+1.\n$$\n\nFinally, writing $x$ in terms of $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{3/4} & =3t+1 \\\\ x+1 & =(3t+1)^{4/3} \\\\ x & =(3t+1)^{4/3}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400065 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400066 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400065 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400067 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400065 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400068 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400065 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400069 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400065 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400070 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400065 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400065 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400065 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400067 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400065 1080 #uuid "56af02a6-0883-5dcb-9c23-0114fa511fa6" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400066 1081 "x(t)=(3t+1)^{4}-1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400066 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400066 1084 #uuid "cb841386-1180-59be-8b8f-ef4a3bdf4bae" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400067 1081 "x(t)=(3t+1)^{4/3}-1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400067 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400067 1084 #uuid "e0471f0f-25c1-5626-b98b-3b2fe326dc7c" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400068 1081 "x(t)=(4t+1)^{3}-1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400068 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400068 1084 #uuid "6ed50d71-47ef-504d-b078-392fbb23bb85" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400069 1081 "x(t)=(t+2)^{2/3}-1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400069 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400069 1084 #uuid "303677bb-cada-51a9-b7bf-74bbee38a830" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400070 1081 "x(t)=(t+2)^{4/3}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400070 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400070 1084 #uuid "2ddf2ba5-5cf7-5f47-befa-2cacf9a12596" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400071 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400072 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400071 1069 "q-122931" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400071 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400071 1071 "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx={e}^{t},\\,y=2t{e}^{t}-2{e}^{t},\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty .\n$$\n\nLet $C$ be the point that corresponds to $t=1$ on the curve. Find the equation of the normal to the curve at $C.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400071 1072 #uuid "138e1f42-3fb6-5013-87c6-eb59c3a912d0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400071 1074 "First, we find the coordinates of the point $C$ by substituting $t=1$ into the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =e, \\\\ y & =2(1){e}^{1}-2{e}^{1}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we're looking to find the equation of the tangent line to the curve at the point $(e,0).$  For this, we need to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ which means we first need to find the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)={e}^{t},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=2t{e}^{t}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2t{e}^{t}}{{e}^{t}} \\\\  & =2t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=1,$ the slope of the tangent line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={\\frac{dy}{dx}|}_{t=1} & =2(1)=2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope ${m}_{n}$ of the normal line, we take the negative reciprocal of $m$:\n\n$$\n{m}_{n}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{\\,2\\,}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the equation of the normal, we use point-slope form with the point $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(e,0)$ and the slope ${m}_{n}=-\\frac{1}{2}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-0 & =(-\\frac{1}{2})(x-e) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{e}{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400072 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400073 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400072 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400074 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400072 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400075 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400072 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400076 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400072 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400077 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400072 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400072 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400072 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400074 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400072 1080 #uuid "b6e41e50-ea1d-54b4-8438-62f4c2b9fa61" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400073 1081 "y=\\frac{x}{3}+\\frac{e}{4}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400073 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400073 1084 #uuid "ac6379c3-3e1c-5a08-ae54-d99f43489aa3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400074 1081 "y=-\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{e}{2}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400074 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400074 1084 #uuid "359d0ac8-26db-56f1-98c6-ec3481c97cb5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400075 1081 "y=-\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{2e}{3}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400075 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400075 1084 #uuid "dfc9efa8-1c48-5867-a1e9-734559b5450d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400076 1081 "y=\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{e}{4}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400076 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400076 1084 #uuid "f85a9aab-60c9-5ec0-8bc2-0588e38d3687" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400077 1081 "y=\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{2}{e}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400077 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400077 1084 #uuid "aa8e29ac-c571-528d-b8c7-bb6ee10f19df" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400078 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400079 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400078 1069 "q-123020" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400078 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400078 1071 "![](images/ae/ae210abc4028440aa9c822510d68f0ab0b8ba4b9f5806dd299149e953ccd1b21.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x={t}^{3}-4,\\,y=2t$\nfrom $t=-2$ to $t=0$ (shown above)?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400078 1072 #uuid "ce632c36-0a89-59ca-a425-8c378bad7972" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400078 1074 "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-4)=3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\sqrt{(3{t}^{2})^{2}+(2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+4}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400079 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400080 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400079 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400081 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400079 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400082 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400079 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400083 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400079 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400084 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400079 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400079 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400079 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400081 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400079 1080 #uuid "d769d84c-e8c5-56e0-8e28-ef7348f0bb6a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400080 1081 "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\sqrt{{t}^{4}+t}\\,\\text{d}t" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400080 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400080 1084 #uuid "71b63c40-4166-58be-98ca-c4f5edc13748" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400081 1081 "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+4}\\,\\text{d}t" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400081 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400081 1084 #uuid "e8a8ab40-ccbb-5118-b2d9-f78348093f93" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400082 1081 "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+3}\\,\\text{d}t" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400082 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400082 1084 #uuid "