 \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{(2-\\frac{1}{{n}^{5}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe limit exists, so the sequence converges.\n\n- In sequence II, the dominant term in the denominator is $-{n}^{4},$ so we divide the numerator and the denominator by ${n}^{4}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n} & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{n-{n}^{5}}{2-{n}^{4}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{n}{{n}^{4}}-\\frac{{n}^{5}}{{n}^{4}})}{(\\frac{2}{{n}^{4}}-\\frac{{n}^{4}}{{n}^{4}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{1}{{n}^{3}}-n)}{(\\frac{2}{{n}^{4}}-1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{0-n}{0-1} \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe limit does not exist, so the sequence diverges.\n\n- In sequence III,  the limit is\n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n}={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{5}{{n}^{6}}=0.\n$$\n\nThe limit exists, so the sequence converges.\n\nIn conclusion, sequence II diverges." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400100 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400101 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400100 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400102 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400100 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400103 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400100 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400104 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400100 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400105 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400100 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400100 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400100 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400105 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400100 1080 #uuid "3fa5013e-ecbb-5612-b808-2ece59956c79" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400101 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400101 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400101 1084 #uuid "ecdf47cc-f0cb-56b3-84ca-bee8e2b8bfe4" 131941395