\\frac{4}{3})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is convergent because $|r|<1.$\n\n- For the geometric series $0.1+0.11+0.121+0.133\\,1+⋯$  the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} & =\\frac{0.11}{0.1} \\\\  & =1.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is divergent  because $|r|\\ge 1.$\n\nIn conclusion, only series II converges." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400156 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400157 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400156 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400158 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400156 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400159 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400156 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400160 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400156 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400161 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400156 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400156 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400156 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400161 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400156 1080 #uuid "7478616a-dd06-5aea-b75a-b73c688ab5fc" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400157 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400157 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400157 1084 #uuid "e3c60d79-86b9-50cc-9f64-560ea2cecec3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400158 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400158 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400158 1084 #uuid "04fc169e-d7b2-5fb6-aaaa-03529f82ef7a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400159 1081 "I only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400159 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400159 1084 #uuid "c64b1ae1-73f4-50e4-83d1-af39cac88db8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400160 1081 "III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400160 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400160 1084 #uuid "c0007124-207e-55b6-82bb-cf42de7dce86" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400161 1081 "II only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400161 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400161 1084 #uuid "8d3720ee-33a3-5bc3-abd0-5c477d7133fe" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400162 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400163 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400162 1069 "q-124965" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400162 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400162 1071 "![](images/cd/cd41c969aee2e7c04c9034106978d8522d6a715733098bfde87abbdb861da7a8.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the unit circle. Given that $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{4},$ what is the value of $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta ?$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400162 1072 #uuid "6bb1887b-828c-58c3-9b10-3c0e7dc6d40b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400162 1074 "![](images/49/4942cec8983dd2bddddd0ba2f8f9332b1b82f3999a44adb138b905457d39c633.png)\n\nWe can use the Pythagorean identity to find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{4}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{1}{16}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{15}{16}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe select the negative answer since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ is negative in the second quadrant. So, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4}.$\n\nFinally, knowing that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{4})}{(-\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4})}=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{15}}=-\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{15}.\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400163 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400164 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400163 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400165 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400163 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400166 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400163 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400167 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400163 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400168 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400163 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400163 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400163 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400168 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400163 1080 #uuid "7ec6cfae-f16c-5f01-8f87-2f00e0b258ca" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400164 1081 "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{15}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400164 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400164 1084 #uuid "1d1e516a-fd02-539c-a55b-1d53b977ac63" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400165 1081 "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{5}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400165 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400165 1084 #uuid "3dd19dff-a905-5735-9496-24d7b4eee41f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400166 1081 "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{5}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400166 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400166 1084 #uuid "7175eeec-eda1-5a92-99be-f76806feffc8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400167 1081 "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400167 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400167 1084 #uuid "14302d62-f56c-5807-8418-d9e29a49a8ab" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400168 1081 "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{15}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400168 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400168 1084 #uuid "df3a9c05-b642-53bc-aee7-47f4b93b0bb0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400169 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400170 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400169 1069 "q-125004" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400169 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400169 1071 "If $sin⁡\\theta =\\frac{7}{8}$ and $\\frac{\\pi }{2}<\\theta <\\pi $ then what is the value of $sec⁡\\theta ?$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400169 1072 #uuid "c006e542-29a2-5102-8308-98f4920ebd17" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400169 1074 "Let's sketch our angle $\\theta $ in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](images/5c/5c98414bbe0e1e373864e9ec1d6b8667bb0032c8824f20bed1e6f9b9079c4d02.png)\n\nWe're given that $sin⁡\\theta =\\frac{7}{8}.$ We can use the Pythagorean identity to find $cos⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ cos⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $sin⁡\\theta =\\frac{7}{8}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cos⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{7}{8})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{49}{64}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{15}{64}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe select the negative answer since $cos⁡\\theta $ is negative in the second quadrant. So, $cos⁡\\theta =-\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{8}.$\n\nFinally, knowing that $sec⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{cos⁡\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\nsec⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{(-\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{8})}=-\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{15}}=-\\frac{8\\sqrt{15}}{15}.\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [175