rue] [17592186400175 1084 #uuid "0944c75f-3871-5029-b2ac-06fe51638caa" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400176 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400177 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400176 1069 "q-125262" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400176 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400176 1071 "Which of the following functions satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[0,e]?$\n\nI. $f(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}$\nII. $g(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$\nIII. $h(x)={e}^{-x/2}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400176 1072 #uuid "0d26c1fd-9972-5992-b3ee-1cc9fed13d91" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400176 1074 "For a function to satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[0,e],$ the function must be continuous on $[0,e]$ and differentiable on $(0,e).$\n\nLet's check each function individually.\n\n- The function $f(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}$ is continuous and differentiable on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ In particular, it  is continuous on $[0,e]$ and differentiable on $(0,e).$ Therefore, $f(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function  $g(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is not defined at $x=0,$ so it is not continuous at $x=0,$ which means it is not continuous on $[0,e].$ Therefore, $g(x)$ does not satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $h(x)={e}^{-x/2}$ is continuous and differentiable on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ In particular, it  is continuous on $[0,e]$ and differentiable on $(0,e).$ Therefore, $h(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\nTherefore, only functions I and III satisfy the conditions for the mean value theorem over the interval $[0,e].$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400177 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400178 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400177 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400179 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400177 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400180 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400177 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400181 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400177 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400182 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400177 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400177 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400177 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400180 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400177 1080 #uuid "2ce3352c-5866-54ec-8397-cf9e37019fd3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400178 1081 "I, II, and III" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400178 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400178 1084 #uuid "95363d69-aef8-5be0-bed6-2e48e831157e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400179 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400179 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400179 1084 #uuid "c811cfee-b520-5024-a08a-7253a95a06d9" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400180 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400180 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400180 1084 #uuid "fb4caf99-22b3-54c0-8115-85030a8148f5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400181 1081 "III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400181 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400181 1084 #uuid "7f361f8f-c150-58fe-9b01-71b7b26b992c" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400182 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400182 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400182 1084 #uuid "f957daf2-0051-5201-9483-2ef71d3af41d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400183 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400184 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400183 1069 "q-125335" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400183 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400183 1071 "Express the Maclaurin series expansion for $x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ given by\n\n$$\nx\\operatorname{sin}⁡x={x}^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{3!}+\\frac{{x}^{6}}{5!}-\\frac{{x}^{8}}{7!}+⋯\n$$\n\nusing sigma notation." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400183 1072 #uuid "66708e85-e31b-5700-a1e3-46ef23b1df08" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400183 1074 "The first four terms of the series are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & ={x}^{2} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{3!} \\\\ {a}_{2} & =\\frac{{x}^{6}}{5!} \\\\ {a}_{3} & =-\\frac{{x}^{8}}{7!}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we can express these terms using a common format, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{(-1)^{0}{x}^{2\\cdot (0+1)}}{(2\\cdot 0+1)!} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =\\frac{(-1)^{1}{x}^{2\\cdot (1+1)}}{(2\\cdot 1+1)!} \\\\ {a}_{2} & =\\frac{(-1)^{2}{x}^{2\\cdot (2+1)}}{(2\\cdot 2+1)!} \\\\ {a}_{3} & =\\frac{(-1)^{3}{x}^{2\\cdot (3+1)}}{(2\\cdot 3+1)!}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe deduce that the general formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{(-1)^{n}{x}^{2(n+1)}}{(2n+1)!}\\,.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & ={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}{x}^{2(n+1)}}{(2n+1)!}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400184 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400185 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400184 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400186 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400184 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400187 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400184 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400188 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400184 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400189 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400184 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400184 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400184 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400186 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [1759218