7592186400330 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400331 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400330 1069 "q-127826" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400330 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400330 1071 "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 15 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400330 1072 #uuid "dd3729c7-43c0-5883-808f-5b63c7f7af84" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400330 1074 "- The matrix $A$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $B$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(B)=-3\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 15=-30.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(B)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $B$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=7\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 4=2.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $C$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ does not have an inverse." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400331 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400332 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400331 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400333 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400331 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400334 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400331 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400335 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400331 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400336 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400331 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400331 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400331 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400333 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400331 1080 #uuid "e2eacdbe-c7ca-5401-a770-a6823a00bee1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400332 1081 "$A$ and $C$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400332 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400332 1084 #uuid "e8d