y one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now check our statements.\n\nNow, since the first part of the invertible matrix theorem is true ($A$ is invertible), all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem, only options I and III give us true statements:\n\n- *If $A$ is invertible, then $det(A)\\ne 0.$* $\\,✓$\n\n- *If $A$ is invertible, then $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$* $\\,✓$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400338 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400339 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400338 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400340 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400338 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400341 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400338 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400342 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400338 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400343 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400338 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400338 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400338 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400342 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400338 1080 #uuid "9e5bc233-a857-5531-b1c0-5d6872ab74e0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400339 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400339 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400339 1084 #uuid "32703bd1-510a-5493-8fea-27ee4c97cf9e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400340 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400340 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400340 1084 #uuid "99ce61c4-029a-53a5-a2e3-716c725f41b9" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400341 1081 "III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400341 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400341 1084 #uuid "f6430495-e643-5b57-a059-f4ae97b5f229" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400342 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400342 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400342 1084 #uuid "b8a6703f-ba79-5105-aa0e-79c1dad1aa0d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400343 1081 "II only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400343 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400343 1084 #uuid "0dd7aae6-48b9-58c3-b530-c8d20775ab70" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400344 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400345 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400344 1069 "q-128461" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400344 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400344 1071 "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨{k}^{2},7,4⟩,$ $b=⟨6,7,4⟩,$ and $c=⟨3,0,2⟩$ are coplanar." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400344 1072 #uuid "41e53fe4-b06e-5150-a976-5badf29f5d4c" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400344 1074 "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}{k}^{2} & 7 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={k}^{2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|-7\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|+4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}6 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={k}^{2}(7\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 4)-7(6\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 4)+4(6\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 7) \\\\  & =14{k}^{2}+0-84 \\\\  & =14{k}^{2}-84 \\\\  & =14({k}^{2}-6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 14({k}^{2}-6) & =0 \\\\ {k}^{2}-6 & =0 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =6 \\\\ k & =\\pm \\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-\\sqrt{6}$ or $k=\\sqrt{6}.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400345 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400346 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400345 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400347 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400345 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400348 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400345 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400349 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400345 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400350 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400345 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400345 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400345 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400349 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400345 1080 #uuid "d47d5cb7-6394-509c-81ff-79c6a1373831" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400346 1081 "$k=\\sqrt{6}$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400346 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400346 1084 #uuid "ce1c52bd-3b80-591c-b1ee-da79ec0a2f5b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400347 1081 "$k=-6$ or $k=6$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400347 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400347 1084 #uuid "0be7aabd-bcca-5a8a-a91e-5d1dfb6c9d3d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400348 1081 "$k=-\\sqrt{6}$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400348 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400348 1084 #uuid "07cf905c-bfd7-597a-b011-0bc724c98f3c" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400349 1081 "$k=-\\sqrt{6}$ or $k=\\sqrt{6}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400349 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400349 1084 #uuid "1c100f4f-e0f0-5fd4-9658-c15b9ace8765" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400350 1081 "$k=-\\sqrt{3}$ or $k=\\sqrt{3}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400350 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400350 1084 #uuid "7316d970-6133-533d-8bfb-659fe822cc85" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400351 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400352 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400351 1069 "q-128478" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400351 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400351 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $F$ given below?\n\nI. $det(F)=-7$\nII. $F$ is **not** a singular matrix\nIII. $det(F)=-2$\n\n$$\nF=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400351 1072 #uuid "af5c321a-ef93-52c0-aab1-818de4211e7b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400351 1074 "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(F) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|-8|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(2-3)-8(-1-5)+3(-3-10) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)-8\\cdot (-6)+3\\cdot (-13) \\\\  & =-2+48-39 \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(F)=7$, the matrix is **not** singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement II is true." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400352 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400353 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400352 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400354 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400352 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400355 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400352 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400356 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400352 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400357 13194139533478 1759218604558