4139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400447 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400447 1084 #uuid "1c6ada89-cdaa-544a-8a21-15e02b79999d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400448 1081 "$A,$ $B,$ and $C$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400448 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400448 1084 #uuid "2a6c5c09-c127-5638-b0a9-423f5bc33f89" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400449 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400450 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400449 1069 "q-130005" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400449 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400449 1071 "Consider the differential equation $x{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}+4{x}^{3}y=0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x$ is a solution to the equation\nII. ${y}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}^{2}$ is a solution to the equation\nIII. The general solution of the equation is $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}^{2}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400449 1072 #uuid "5007768b-5de4-5206-bbd7-b32aa44bd388" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400449 1074 "Let's check each statement:\n\n- To determine whether ${y}_{1}(x)$ is a solution to the differential equation, we substitute ${y}_{1}$ and its derivatives into the equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{′}(x) & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\ {y}_{1}^{″}(x) & =-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{1}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation. We get\n\n$$\nx(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)-(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+4{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=(4{x}^{3}-4x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{1}$ is not a solution to the equation, and therefore statement II is false.\n\n- Similarly, we compute the derivatives of ${y}_{2}$ and substitute to the equation. Computing the derivatives yields\n\nFirst, we find the first and second derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′}(x) & =2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}^{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″}(x) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}^{2}-4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{2}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation. We get\n\n$$\nx(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}^{2}-4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}^{2})-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}^{2}+4{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}^{2}=(2x-2x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}^{2}+(4{x}^{3}-4{x}^{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}^{2}=0.\\,✓\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{2}$ is a solution to the equation, and therefore statement II is true.\n\n- So, ${y}_{2}$ is a solution while ${y}_{1}$ is not a solution of the equation, hence $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}^{2}$  is not the general solution.\n\nTherefore, statement III is false." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400450 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400451 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400450 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400452 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400450 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400453 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400450 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400454 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400450 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400455 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400450 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400450 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400450 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400455 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400450 1080 #uuid "f811653b-c37a-5ec9-b2ba-127c51552176" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400451 1081 "I, II, and III" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400451 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400451 1084 #uuid "e6f79407-a923-589b-a295-638d183f58c4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400452 1081 "I only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400452 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400452 1084 #uuid "ec6f68ed-dc62-52f7-a8a8-25d2b4e2c679" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400453 1081 "None" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400453 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400453 1084 #uuid "304116eb-0764-5f6c-972e-528fb8f92b2d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400454 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400454 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400454 1084 #uuid "e34f4504-4c9a-5234-9156-5bb772e4f0f4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400455 1081 "II only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400455 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400455 1084 #uuid "e64e44b4-9ddb-5053-ab1b-b0b50f74e6de" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400456 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400457 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400456 1069 "q-130217" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400456 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400456 1071 "At which points on the curve ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2y-2x$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $-i+j?$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400456 1072 #uuid "6851bbc7-80d6-5dc9-8a00-f559624fa12f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400456 1074 "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =2y-2x \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2x-2y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2x-2y,$ our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=0.$ \n\nA tangent vector to the level curve can be computed as follows:\n\n$$\nt(x,y)={f}_{y}(x,y)\\,i-{f}_{x}(x,y)\\,j\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y) & ={f}_{y}(x,y)\\,i-{f}_{x}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2x-2y)\\,i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2x-2y)\\,j \\\\  & =(2y-2)\\,i-(2x+2)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince our tangent vector needs to be perpendicular to $-i+j,$ we must have $t\\cdot (-i+j)=0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot (-i+j) & =0 \\\\ ((2y-2)\\,i-(2x+2)\\,j)\\cdot (-i+j) & =0 \\\\ -(2y-2)-(2x+2) & =0 \\\\ -2y-2x & =0 \\\\ y & =-x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $y=-x$ into the equation of our curve gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =2y-2x \\\\ {x}^{2}+(-x)^{2} & =2(-x)-2x \\\\ 2{x}^{2} & =-4x \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+4x & =0 \\\\ 2x(x+2) & =0 \\\\ x & =-2,0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally:\n\n- For $x=-2,$ we get $y=2,$ and the corresponding point is $(-2,2).$\n\n- For $x=0,$ we get $y=0,$ and the corresponding point is $(0,0).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400457 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400458 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400457 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400459 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400457 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400460 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400457 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400461 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400457 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400462 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400457 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400457 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400457 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400459 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400457 1080 #uuid "31717cb2-d9d0-54f4-b700-91183260eebd" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400458 1081 "$(0,0)$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400458 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400458 1084 #uuid "2a3b5cf6-0370-5cde-a9e6-1edabf953fa1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400459 1081 "$(-2,2)$ and $(0,0)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400459 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400459 1084 #uuid "796d0d95-8bf2-5062-97c0-381c6826adbc" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400460 1081 "$(0,2)$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400460 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400460 1084 #uuid "930c85b6-cd1d-5f01-b245-1181988c9afd" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400461 1081 "$(-2,0)$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400461 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400461 1084 #uuid "03b48f4a-4c69-5175-9b51-45915a00e587" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400462 1081 "$(-2,0)$ and $(0,2)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400462 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400462 1084 #uuid "36a2c161-410d-5532-af77-2aaed16bed2f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400463 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400464 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400463 1069 "q-130256" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400463 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400463 1071 "Which of the following are linear differential operators?\n\nI. ${D}_{1}(y)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$\nII. ${D}_{2}(y)=2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$\nIII. ${D}_{3}(y)={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400463 1072 #uuid "3a8a1c12-7f84-5c3b-83f4-8db057221abd" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400463 1074 "For any linear differential operator,\n\n$$\nD(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})=aD({y}_{1})+bD({y}_{2})\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. \n\nLet's check each case in turn.\n\n- The first operator is **not** linear. To see why, we first evaluate the left-hand side of the linearity condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{1}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})+(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =a\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+b\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{a}^{2}{y}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}+{b}^{2}{y}_{2}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}+ab({y}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}+{y}_{2}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is not the same as the right-hand side, because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a{D}_{1}({y}_{1})+b{D}_{1}({y}_{2}) & =a[\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{y}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}]+b[\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{y}_{2}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}] \\\\  & =a\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+b\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+a{y}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}+b{y}_{2}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operator is indeed linear. To see this, we check the above linearity condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{2}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) & =2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})-x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =2a\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2b\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-ax\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}-bx\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =a[2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-x\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}]+b[2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-x\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}] \\\\  & =a{D}_{2}({y}_{1})+b{D}_{2}({y}_{2})\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third operator is also linear. To see this, we check the above linearity condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{3}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) & ={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})+2x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =a{x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+b{x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2ax\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}+2bx\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =a[{x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2x\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}]+b[{x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2x\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}] \\\\  & =a{D}_{3}({y}_{1})+b{D}_{3}({y}_{2})\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400464 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400465 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400464 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400466 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400464 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400467 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400464 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400468 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400464 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400469 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400464 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400464 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400464 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400465 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400464 1080 #uuid "c115e153-7737-5c46-8dab-a27a2878d2ab" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400465 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400465 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400465 1084 #uuid "bd9ec779-6e5b-54f7-8fd9-a5183794b900" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400466 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400466 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400466 1084 #uuid "2f86b6dc-bb9c-5829-8488-ad5ed68bda32" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400467 1081 "I only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400467 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400467 1084 #uuid "ba05598e-f2d4-5884-9220-cb669bdd2471" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400468 1081 "III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400468 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400468 1084 #uuid "6434ae8b-dd11-5d8d-a8cc-6bab51ffb0aa" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400469 1081 "II only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400469 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400469 1084 #uuid "a1f89614-0c4c-5da9-973a-e0bc4c18e8b4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400470 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400471 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400470 1069 "q-130261" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400470 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400470 1071 "Which of the following are linear differential operators?\n\nI. ${D}_{1}(y)=x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2xy$\nII. ${D}_{2}(y)={x}^{3}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}$\nIII. ${D}_{3}(y)=y\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+xy$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400470 1072 #uuid "3d8c3559-a0d3-57b0-8496-a5eb629e4fde" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400470 1074 "For any linear differential operator,\n\n$$\nD(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})=aD({y}_{1})+bD({y}_{2})\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. \n\nLet's check each case in turn.\n\n- The first operator is indeed linear. To see this, we check the above linearity condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{1}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) & =x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})-2x(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =ax\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+bx\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2ax{y}_{1}-2bx{y}_{2} \\\\  & =a[x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2x{y}_{1}]+b[x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2x{y}_{2}] \\\\  & =a{D}_{1}({y}_{1})+b{D}_{1}({y}_{2})\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operator is also linear. To see this, we check the above linearity condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{2}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) & ={x}^{3}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =a{x}^{3}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+b{x}^{3}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =a[{x}^{3}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}]+b[{x}^{3}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}] \\\\  & =a{D}_{2}({y}_{1})+b{D}_{2}({y}_{2})\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third operator is **not** linear.\nTo see why, we first evaluate the left-hand side of the linearity condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{3}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) & =(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})+x(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})(a\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+b\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}})+ax{y}_{1}+bx{y}_{2} \\\\  & ={a}^{2}{y}_{1}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{b}^{2}{y}_{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+ab({y}_{1}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{y}_{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}})+ax{y}_{1}+bx{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is not the same as the right-hand side, because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a{D}_{3}({y}_{1})+b{D}_{3}({y}_{2}) & =a[{y}_{1}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+x{y}_{1}]+b[{y}_{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+x{y}_{2}] \\\\  & =a{y}_{1}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+b{y}_{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+ax{y}_{1}+bx{y}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400471 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400472 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400471 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400473 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400471 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400474 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400471 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400475 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400471 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400476 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400471 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400471 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 tr