^{3}-3{x}^{2}-72x.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400582 1072 #uuid "19a51c3a-961d-51e8-839d-dcbc2e643a8d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400582 1074 "A critical point of $f(x)$ is a point $x=c$ in the domain of $f$ such that either ${f}^{′}(c)=0$ or ${f}^{′}(c)$ does not exist.\n\nDifferentiating $f(x),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-72x) \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}-6x-72.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to find the critical points:\n\n- First, we compute the points where ${f}^{′}(c)=0.$ We set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}-6x-72 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-x-12 & =0 \\\\ (x-4)(x+3) & =0 \\\\ x & =-3,\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has stationary points at $x=-3$ and $x=4.$\n\n- Second, we note that ${f}^{′}(x)$ exists for all values of $x$ in the domain of $f(x).$ So $f(x)$ has no non-stationary critical points.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the critical points of $f(x)$ are $x=-3$ and $x=4.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400583 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400584 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400583 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400585 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400583 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400586 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400583 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400587 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400583 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400588 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400583 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400583 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400583 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400585 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400583 1080 #uuid "40b63710-ca14-5f20-99f5-64eef01983af" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400584 1081 "$x=-6$ and $x=3$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400584 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400584 1