ms of $y$ and $z.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement III is true." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400639 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400640 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400639 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400641 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400639 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400642 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400639 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400643 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400639 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400644 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400639 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400639 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400639 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400642 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400639 1080 #uuid "97478289-921c-5024-949c-f21308c68969" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400640 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400640 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400640 1084 #uuid "461eef6c-aefb-5663-8d03-db54f697d105" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400641 1081 "I only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400641 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400641 1084 #uuid "b3d3c662-b67b-5b81-a307-d2b8efde6388" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400642 1081 "III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400642 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400642 1084 #uuid "fbcd7fd9-5df8-5756-a9f3-48cc31c9e67e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400643 1081 "None" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400643 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400643 1084 #uuid "ec9dcc22-2e73-56c0-825d-9e630c431eb4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400644 1081 "II only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400644 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400644 1084 #uuid "56e99c2d-29cc-5ded-a5f5-80ae572f982d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400645 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400646 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400645 1069 "q-131721" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400645 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400645 1071 "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y=-1 \\\\  & 3x+7y=1 \\\\  & -2x-4y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is consistent independent\nII. The system has no solution\nIII. The system is consistent dependent" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400645 1072 #uuid "b9b47374-5548-52b6-9b51-17d923fcd37b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400645 1074 "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=-1 \\\\ y=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we have $y=4$ and substituting this into the first equation yields $x=-9.$ So,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent. \n\nAs a result, only statement I is true." 131941395