00875 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400875 1084 #uuid "f03dd7eb-af5f-5f22-813b-7f3d5b84651c" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400876 1081 "$|B|$ and $|C|$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400876 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400876 1084 #uuid "ab86d5e2-989c-5d49-9b2d-7a183fd53e17" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400877 1081 "$|C|$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400877 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400877 1084 #uuid "da8626ef-a38f-59a8-a718-2155b988e445" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400878 1081 "$|A|$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400878 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400878 1084 #uuid "c0fe0f31-e9db-50f1-a23b-a66578e23d9f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400879 1081 "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400879 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400879 1084 #uuid "1485ab74-1a6a-53e5-9aaf-e407a69b362d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400880 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400881 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400880 1069 "q-140401" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400880 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400880 1071 "Let $v$ be a non-zero vector from ${R}^{2}$ and let $A$ be the rotation-scaling matrix given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3\\sqrt{2} & -3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{2} & -3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe description of $Av$ in terms of geometric transformations in the plane is given below. What are the missing entries?\n\n*To compute the vector $Av$, we rotate $v$ counterclockwise by an angle of $\\theta =\\text{_____}$ and then scale the result by a factor of $r=\\text{_____}.$*" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400880 1072 #uuid "f2b946dc-503a-51e5-98d7-7e814f7abb9d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400880 1074 "We can find the scale factor using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{det(A)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(3\\sqrt{2})}^{2}+{(3\\sqrt{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18+18} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent $A$ as a product of a rotation and a scaling matrix, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =6[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}r & 0 \\\\ 0 & r\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\theta =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that the missing entries are $\\theta =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ and $r=6.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400881 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400882 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400881 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400883 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400881 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400884 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400881 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400885 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400881 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400886 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400881 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400881 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400881 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400885 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400881 1080 #uuid "c9bcdf0a-7ee5-512b-8b69-1c9ff761e1cb" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400882 1081 "$\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and $5$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400882 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400882 1084 #uuid "d416963d-0812-5442-bfb3-5143f8304cd1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400883 1081 "$\\frac{7\\pi }{4}$ and $9$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400883 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400883 1084 #uuid "25b68c79-4c84-5a8a-b3cb-c873ab4bbeec" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400884 1081 "$\\frac{5\\pi }{4}$ and $9$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400884 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400884 1084 #uuid "399087ad-ae5c-50a9-b3f6-f634f021724e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400885 1081 "$\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ and $6$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400885 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400885 1084 #uuid "abe1e0eb-b3fa-5749-9d80-faecfb2587cc" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400886 1081 "$\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and $6$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400886 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400886 1084 #uuid "e4b9e256-2bbe-5a6c-804a-deec95112ee2" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400887 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400888 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400887 1069 "q-140449" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400887 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400887 1071 "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda $ of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400887 1072 #uuid "f772a19b-8ab2-5f26-9ef1-47231e01914d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400887 1074 "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 6-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 6-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )(3-\\lambda )(6-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=3,$ $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=4,$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=6.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are always the entries on the main diagonal." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400888 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400889 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400888 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400890 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400888 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400891 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400888 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400892 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400888 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400893 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400888 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400888 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400888 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400892 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400888 1080 #uuid "8ed14d3f-a85e-59d0-a5e0-cd86b0195649" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400889 1081 "\\lambda \\in {3,0,6}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400889 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400889 1084 #uuid "7c340906-07d4-57b0-9046-295287f1840f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400890 1081 "\\lambda \\in {3,4,9}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400890 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400890 1084 #uuid "735c9554-2122-554a-9c6d-88f5c542af17" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400891 1081 "\\lambda \\in {3,-2,6}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400891 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400891 1084 #uuid "cf676211-b439-541c-a870-387de50e341e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400892 1081 "\\lambda \\in {3,4,6}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400892 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400892 1084 #uuid "5f97e983-0e63-57dd-acda-842c7a7cfb12" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400893 1081 "\\lambda \\in {-3,4,6}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400893 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400893 1084 #uuid "812db70d-b4af-5153-8bf4-a315c5a42142" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400894 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400895 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400894 1069 "q-140555" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400894 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400894 1071 "What type of quadratic curve is defined by the following equation?\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=-7\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400894 1072 #uuid "e9992e79-a8b1-5b6c-bb33-ddbd38d4ce02" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400894 1074 "First, we complete the squares for the variables ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} & =-7 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}({x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1})+({x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}) & =-7 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}({x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}+4-4)+({x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}+1-1) & =-7 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}({x}_{1}+2)^{2}+({x}_{2}-1)^{2}-4 & =-7 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}({x}_{1}+2)^{2}+({x}_{2}-1)^{2} & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, performing the change of variables\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}={x}_{1}+2, \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}{y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2} & =-3 \\\\ \\frac{{y}_{1}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}_{2}^{2}}{3} & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich defines an empty set. Notice that the equation is equivalent to $\\frac{{y}_{1}^{2}}{(2\\text{i})^{2}}+\\frac{{y}_{2}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3}\\text{i})^{2}}=1,$ which has imaginary solutions, so we can interpret this as an imaginary ellipse with semiaxes $2\\text{i}$ and $\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400895 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400896 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400895 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400897 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400895 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400898 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400895 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400899 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400895 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400900 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400895 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400895 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400895 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400897 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400895 1080 #uuid "8d7df124-dbc5-56d7-8581-3302e8d894bc" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400896 1081 "A hyperbola with semiaxes $2$ and $\\sqrt{3}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400896 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400896 1084 #uuid "74b0f0ad-077e-5490-8903-2b75e6400fb3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400897 1081 "An imaginary ellipse" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400897 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400897 1084 #uuid "c9962984-13d2-5e7a-a101-99ffb98df884" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400898 1081 "A hyperbola with semiaxes $4$ and $3$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400898 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400898 1084 #uuid "c26a296a-362d-571b-bc2a-b4d7be4f7f68" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400899 1081 "An ellipse with semiaxes $2$ and $\\sqrt{3}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400899 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400899 1084 #uuid "5b9951ca-7918-51ae-8e54-71674985b355" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400900 1081 "An ellipse with semiaxes $4$ and $3$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400900 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400900 1084 #uuid "70050e40-2d4d-5f43-8504-d04583bd8a31" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400901 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400902 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400901 1069 "q-140822" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400901 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400901 1071 "Scientists are observing a colony of bugs. The population $P(t)$ of the colony is given by the function\n\n$$\nP(t)=27+{\\int }_{0}^{t}(3{x}^{2}-12)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere $P$ is the number of bugs, and $t>0$ is the time (in days) since the observation started. \n\nAt what time is the population of the colony a minimum, and what is the number of bugs at this time?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400901 1072 #uuid "3cbfc231-381e-525d-b699-91d7448dd5be" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400901 1074 "To find when the population is a minimum, we need to solve $\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=0.$ First, we differentiate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(27+{\\int }_{0}^{t}(3{x}^{2}-12)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(27)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({\\int }_{0}^{t}(3{x}^{2}-12)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{\\int }_{0}^{t}(3{x}^{2}-12)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve $\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=0$ for $t>0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{2}-12 & =0 \\\\ 3({t}^{2}-4) & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2} & =4 \\\\ t & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo there are two candidates for global extrema, $t=0$ and $t=2.$\nTo find the number of bugs when $t=2,$ we figure out $P(2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2) & =27+{\\int }_{0}^{2}(3{x}^{2}-12)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =27+[{x}^{3}-12x]{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =27+[(8-24)-(0)] \\\\  & =27-16 \\\\  & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $11<27$, we conclude that the minimum population is $11$ bugs, and this happens after $2$ days." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400902 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400903 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400902 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400904 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400902 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400905 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400902 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400906 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400902 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400907 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400902 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400902 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400902 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400907 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400902 1080 #uuid "5e151de4-60bd-5c74-b6e4-910b2f3a14f4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400903 1081 "The minimum is $8$ bugs after $4$ days" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400903 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400903 1084 #uuid "abcdf400-bcb6-5e0b-9ec6-dab2bf54761d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400904 1081 "The minimum is $27$ bugs after $5$ days" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400904 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400904 1084 #uuid "ab9c13c6-09fb-581a-8fa8-e20695647309" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400905 1081 "The minimum is $15$ bugs after $4$ days" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400905 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400905 1084 #uuid "7235e376-c628-51f5-8028-177047d2588a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400906 1081 "The minimum is $16$ bugs after $2$ days" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400906 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400906 1084 #uuid "5f2d7c8e-9f10-5045-82f9-c14578f74b9e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400907 1081 "The minimum is $11$ bugs after $2$ days" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400907 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400907 1084 #uuid "6f60dfcf-9cc7-5683-856d-afa629682956" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400908 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400909 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400908 1069 "q-140997" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400908 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400908 1071 "Given the quadratic form $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+5{x}_{2}^{2},$ find its canonical (diagonal) form ${y}^{T}\\,Dy$ and an orthogonal matrix $P$ such that $x=Py$ defines the corresponding change of variables." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400908 1072 #uuid "2172cdc2-fb35-5393-84ba-3c3dbc3c7926" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400908 1074 "First, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nEvery quadratic form can be reduced to its canonical (diagonal) form using orthogonal transformations.\n\nTo find the coefficients of the canonical form, we need to calculate the eigenvalues of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-7\\lambda +6 & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =6,\\,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we need to find an eigenvector basis of $A.$ \n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=6,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-6I & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]-6[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-6I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Dividing ${v}_{2}$ by its norm $‖{v}_{2}‖=\\sqrt{5},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-1I & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]-1[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-1I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Dividing ${v}_{1}$ by its norm $‖{v}_{1}‖=\\sqrt{5},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the diagonal matrix $D$ (writing the eigenvalues in descending order) and the orthogonal matrix $P$ in the usual way, and this gives us the following:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400909 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400910 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400909 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400911 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400909 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400912 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400909 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400913 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400909 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400914 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400909 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400909 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400909 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400912 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400909 1080 #uuid "b9d3fb41-4434-5c99-a083-41daf1b7f0a5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400910 1081 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400910 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400910 1084 #uuid "8b279401-b2e9-52e3-8e8a-5ed7f4ab0fc4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400911 1081 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $P=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}}\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400911 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400911 1084 #uuid "2e9a7c28-297a-59f1-8324-969697fcb145" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400912 1081 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $P=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400912 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400912 1084 #uuid "6872e2bc-f5d0-5fd1-8dae-d3fd4d09b23b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400913 1081 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $P=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400913 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400913 1084 #uuid "432384f9-da06-525e-baa9-7350f4251ed1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400914 1081 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $P=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400914 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400914 1084 #uuid "67ba60db-8cbf-553b-b63c-195669a23aa3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400915 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400916 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400915 1069 "q-141140" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400915 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400915 1071 "![](images/b3/b362831ba2248e03537551c412ae7537646dcd09f0d00a598905f0d52a258da9.png)\n\nA part of the graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is given above. Which of the following statements is true?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400915 1072 #uuid "6ab70a1a-e04b-524f-9866-e86f88144126" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400915 1074 "| Multiplicity | Sketch | Sketch |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ \n\n (Simple Root) | ![](images/5a/5a0221f93c65a1eeb4503604a558a6da81c4c7af81c2c52cc35ecf3d189fe99f.png) | ![](images/d5/d556b4edf39181eebb7ec87c344d6f657a6875ecd2745405eaf5351ccaff6f96.png) |\n| $>1$ \n\n (Multiple Root) \n\n Even | ![](images/9d/9d14c2588da2ee9c9f5bbc32a70791146bed609ea0d6d5912aeaa2edab02e2d7.png) | ![](images/28/28ad9248a9a509e3a44937d0438fb2366f550a22360d01b9b6a29bcac41357e8.png) |\n| $>1$ \n\n (Multiple Root) \n\n Odd | ![](images/3a/3ae81378cb3c918dd5b7730519eb5a91e949f88eef9f03f4910f4ab8fb3cd5a9.png) | ![](images/95/9506a7ce4031f1f6244c0110c3235f66ea5652bb53548a032732869cf21f5997.png) |\n\nIt's possible to determine information regarding the multiplicities of the roots of a polynomial from its graph.\n\n- If the graph intersects the $x$-axis but is *not* tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ we have a *simple* root $x=a.$\n\n- If the graph is *tangent* to the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ we have a *multiple* root $x=a.$ Furthermore:\n\n- If the graph touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at $x=a,$ the multiplicity of a root $x=a$ is *even*.\n\n- If the graph crosses the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ the multiplicity of a root $x=a$ is *odd*.\n\nIn our case, the graph is *not* tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=-3.$ Therefore, $x=-3$ is a *simple* root." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400916 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400917 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400916 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400918 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400916 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400919 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400916 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400920 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400916 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400921 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400916 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400916 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400916 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400921 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400916 1080 #uuid "5806f142-c711-5da8-b1d4-68c8001a3f1f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400917 1081 "$x=-3$ is a multiple root of odd multiplicity" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400917 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400917 1084 #uuid "3559bdb9-c007-500b-83db-63f2d91cd407" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400918 1081 "$x=-3$ is a multiple root of even multiplicity" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400918 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400918 1084 #uuid "f1984a87-93e4-523e-80b4-a37c28b7dc5b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400919 1081 "$x=-3$ is a simple root of even multiplicity" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400919 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400919 1084 #uuid "3f15fef9-83c3-50e8-980b-72c67ab596d8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400920 1081 "$x=-3$ is not a root of $p(x)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400920 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400920 1084 #uuid "f52c0001-2df6-56e0-ae3c-2dca7d79a58b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400921 1081 "$x=-3$ is a simple root" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400921 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400921 1084 #uuid "d7950f6f-fd87-5dac-ba8c-650fe8a19888" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400922 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400923 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400922 1069 "q-141187" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400922 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400922 1071 "![](images/46/46edcf2265f41b8fac7931802875e1b9849006834b3509a186ffc7acb510959f.png)\n\nGiven the graph above, solve the inequality $(-x-5)(x+1)<0.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400922 1072 #uuid "66cebf22-0b82-5cf0-a87d-5c8eaa25290f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400922 1074 "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\n(-x-5)(x+1)<0,\n$$\n\nis a \"*less than*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola  \n\n$$\ny=(-x-5)(x+1)\n$$\n\n  \n\nis *below* the $x$-axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/e8/e830af773829b1712c6a87955e74411b6ad9921ae1aea58029ca968ab354c0f1.png)\n\n \n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x<-5$ or    $x>-1.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400923 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400924 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400923 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400925 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400923 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400926 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400923 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400927 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400923 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400928 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400923 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400923 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400923 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400925 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400923 1080 #uuid "7f3297c0-8b61-583d-8e5e-b17352fc3208" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400924 1081 "-5<x<1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400924 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400924 1084 #uuid "c694a7cb-1273-5aef-bab1-b00405cb06a8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400925 1081 "$x<-5$ or    $x>-1$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400925 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400925 1084 #uuid "19263d22-de7b-5ef3-9798-b98080320005" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400926 1081 "x>5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400926 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400926 1084 #uuid "ee071af0-120e-5c4a-b72d-0c54e26d3687" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400927 1081 "$x<-1$ or    $x>5$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400927 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400927 1084 #uuid "395b066b-730c-5a11-889e-cc63987fd8a1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400928 1081 "-1<x<5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400928 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400928 1084 #uuid "3271e9c8-ddaf-5be7-852f-5b3fd22e072b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400929 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400930 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400929 1069 "q-141310" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400929 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400929 1071 "Does the sequence ${a}_{n}=\\frac{3{(4)}^{n}}{{(-6)}^{n}}$ for $n\\ge 1$ converge or diverge? If it converges, what is its limit?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400929 1072 #uuid "7c5b5131-1801-5dfb-aff8-f50ca940df15" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400929 1074 "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nFirst, we rewrite the sequence in the form ${a}_{n}=a\\cdot {r}^{n},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =\\frac{3{(4)}^{n}}{{(-6)}^{n}} \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{{(4)}^{n}}{{(-6)}^{n}} \\\\  & =3{(-\\frac{4}{6})}^{n} \\\\  & =3{(-\\frac{2}{3})}^{n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now see that this is the geometric sequence with $r=-\\frac{2}{3}.$ \n\nSince $|r|<1,$ the sequence converges to $0.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400930 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400931 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400930 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400932 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400930 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400933 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400930 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400934 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400930 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400935 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400930 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400930 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400930 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400931 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400930 1080 #uuid "a83cb541-9ba7-558c-804e-5b78b4a327b4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400931 1081 "Converges to $0$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400931 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400931 1084 #uuid "d912e9d9-60dd-53f8-84b5-6a01262be9b8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400932 1081 "Converges to $3$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400932 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400932 1084 #uuid "5e69372e-e868-57ad-81a9-235542604c47" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400933 1081 "Converges to $\\frac{2}{3}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400933 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400933 1084 #uuid "ad3cf5dc-1a5e-5ca5-bb04-89cb5648d292" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400934 1081 "Converges to $-\\frac{2}{3}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400934 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400934 1084 #uuid "a6f4c2df-fdff-5c81-86c1-ed79a5590ca1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400935 1081 "The sequence diverges" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400935 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400935 1084 #uuid "ee524a7c-b00b-54ff-b0db-1379d3f0eb87" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400936 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400937 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400936 1069 "q-141539" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400936 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400936 1071 "If the expression ${x}^{2}+6x+14$ is written as $(x+p{)}^{2}+q,$ then what are the values of $p$ and $q?$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400936 1072 #uuid "bd1c73ef-6818-5b51-baee-cca065c2f0da" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400936 1074 "First, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3x+14\n$$\n\nNow, here's the trick. We *add* and *then subtract* ${3}^{2},$ writing the constant term $14$ last:\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3x+{3}^{2}}_{⏟}-\\,{3}^{2}+14\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(x+3{)}^{2}-{3}^{2}+14\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(x+3{)}^{2}+5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=3$ and $q=5.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400937 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400938 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400937 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400939 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400937 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400940 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400937 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400941 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400937 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400942 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400937 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400937 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400937 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400940 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400937 1080 #uuid "95bbc964-13ea-55a0-9065-a7c49f46fb65" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400938 1081 "p=6,\\,q=8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400938 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400938 1084 #uuid "c4bc4897-6558-52b5-bb24-657fa38a810c" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400939 1081 "p=3,\\,q=-5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400939 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400939 1084 #uuid "62f6fb47-ecea-56a8-9070-83fc55e7254f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400940 1081 "p=3,\\,q=5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400940 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400940 1084 #uuid "3d43940b-e27a-5dff-9dca-bf6857baf92f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400941 1081 "p=6,\\,q=7" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400941 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400941 1084 #uuid "bdeaea36-9352-52ca-8483-6b276a77d472" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400942 1081 "p=3,\\,q=-4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400942 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400942 1084 #uuid "bfc66d56-1a8c-5626-b30a-e9774929570d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400943 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400944 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400943 1069 "q-141622" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400943 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400943 1071 "If the expression ${y}^{2}-10y+30$ is written as $(y+p{)}^{2}+q,$ then what are the values of $p$ and $q?$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400943 1072 #uuid "a81398bc-73ed-504a-b8b3-ef512650d7f6" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400943 1074 "First, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}-2\\cdot 5y+30\n$$\n\nNow, here's the trick. We *add* and *then subtract* ${5}^{2},$ writing the constant term $30$ last:\n\n$$\n{{y}^{2}-2\\cdot 5y+{5}^{2}}_{⏟}-\\,{5}^{2}+30\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(y-5{)}^{2}-{5}^{2}+30\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(y-5{)}^{2}+5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=-5$ and $q=5.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400944 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400945 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400944 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400946 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400944 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400947 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400944 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400948 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400944 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400949 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400944 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400944 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400944 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400948 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400944 1080 #uuid "c559c184-d951-52c2-ae9b-1fd6b5cd4853" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400945 1081 "p=-5,\\text{ }q=10" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400945 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400945 1084 #uuid "7d53fe67-7a37-5135-9bda-59dc26da7eba" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400946 1081 "p=5,\\t