94139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400960 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400960 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400960 1084 #uuid "1e18716e-efdf-5322-a98c-f7741d67d8d8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400961 1081 "III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400961 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400961 1084 #uuid "028c6bbc-5127-5736-b3ba-9f94a0f28ed4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400962 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400962 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400962 1084 #uuid "3daa75bf-f787-56ff-9dca-1b80759e9c6c" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400963 1081 "II only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400963 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400963 1084 #uuid "d4912560-949d-5a8e-9911-c20ce554555e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400964 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400965 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400964 1069 "q-142315" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400964 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400964 1071 "Find the solution of $-{x}^{2}+6x-5\\le 0.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400964 1072 #uuid "f59dad02-8b17-598a-a754-71bfff242018" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400964 1074 "To solve the inequality \n\n$$\n-{x}^{2}+6x-5\\le 0,\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny=-{x}^{2}+6x-5\n$$\n\nlies *below* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}+6x-5 & =0 \\\\ -({x}^{2}-6x+5) & =0 \\\\ -(x-1)(x-5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=1$ and $x=5,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](images/7c/7cfa66b5aa6a3f29e7154e329926a47bbbb0eb45dce3251148986785f09ee383.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *below* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x\\le 1$ or $x\\ge 5.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400965 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400966 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400965 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400967 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400965 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400968 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400965 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400969 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400965 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400970 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400965 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400965 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400965 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400968 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400965 1080 #uuid "8b2ce6b8-4640-53b8-b17b-3464a0fe587d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400966 1081 "-1\\le x\\le 5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400966 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400966 1084 #uuid "bb10726b-626d-526b-b3f9-de6bad9f3f38" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400967 1081 "$x\\le -6$ or $x\\ge 1$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400967 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400967 1084 #uuid "a7f8c3f4-5711-584d-9263-fed31acf6c29" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400968 1081 "$x\\le 1$ or $x\\ge 5$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400968 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400968 1084 #uuid "bce75758-abe3-5789-8de5-5d18996c87a5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400969 1081 "-5\\le x\\le -1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400969 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400969 1084 #uuid "cf8d0e9c-0806-580a-b031-8a01a725abe9" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400970 1081 "$x\\le -5$ or $x\\ge 1$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400970 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400970 1084 #uuid "a4a43c47-c698-531e-a0a3-0b2da98a2630" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400971 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400972 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400971 1069 "q-142915" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400971 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400971 1071 "| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.25$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.3$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.2$ | $0$ |\n\nFind the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400971 1072 #uuid "0a2eced6-9cd5-5469-b3dc-6168e1ec698d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400971 1074 "The conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=P(X=x\\,|\\,Y=y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we're required to compute the following set of conditional probabilities:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)=P(X=x\\,|\\,Y=4)\n$$\n\nBy the multiplication law for conditional probability, we have\n\n$$\nP(X=x\\,|\\,Y=4)=\\frac{P(X=x,Y=4)}{P(Y=1)}=\\frac{f(x,4)}{{f}_{Y}(4)}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal distribution of $Y.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distributions for $X$ and $Y$ correspond to the row and column totals, respectively. So, let's compute these:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.25$ | $0.1$ | $0.35$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.3$ | $0.15$ | $0.45$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.2$ | $0$ | $0.2$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.75$ | $0.25$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore, for $x\\in {0,1,2},$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=0\\,|\\,Y=4) & =\\frac{f(0,4)}{{f}_{Y}(4)}=\\frac{0.1}{0.25}=0.4 \\\\ P(X=1\\,|\\,Y=4) & =\\frac{f(1,4)}{{f}_{Y}(4)}=\\frac{0.15}{0.25}=0.6 \\\\ P(X=2\\,|\\,Y=4) & =\\frac{f(2,4)}{{f}_{Y}(4)}=\\frac{0}{0.25}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the conditional probability mass function can be represented by the following table:   \n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | $0$ |" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400972 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400973 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400972 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400974 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400972 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400975 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400972 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400976 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400972 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400977 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400972 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400972 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400972 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400973 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400972 1080 #uuid "2e2d2d25-c810-5851-af0b-d59a08144e7f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400973 1081 "| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | $0$ |" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400973 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400973 1084 #uuid "c4bfd97b-bea2-5ab6-9084-e9f94b5ae836" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400974 1081 "| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)$ | $0.25$ | $0.35$ | $0.4$ |" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400974 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400974 1084 #uuid "b14388b2-8f17-5b6d-bd37-dce823b24383" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400975 1081 "| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)$ | $0.2$ | $0.5$ | $0.3$ |" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400975 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400975 1084 #uuid "e285d986-7f75-5785-9aea-c3e63564aefe" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400976 1081 "| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)$ | $0.5$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ |" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400976 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400976 1084 #uuid "e4fd822c-1f8c-5028-b56a-da7d3e74b8f1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400977 1081 "| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)$ | $0.4$ | $0.2$ | $0.4$ |" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400977 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400977 1084 #uuid "1632a6d2-71a6-5531-bc91-795371f646d4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400978 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400979 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400978 1069 "q-142928" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400978 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400978 1071 "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.3$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ |\n\nFind the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,0)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400978 1072 #uuid "d63f5e38-dd7f-5597-b7d6-4c39a2fe3945" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400978 1074 "The conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=P(Y=y\\,|\\,X=x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we're required to compute the following set of conditional probabilities:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,0)=P(Y=y\\,|\\,X=0)\n$$\n\nBy the multiplication law for conditional probability, we have\n\n$$\nP(Y=y\\,|\\,X=0)=\\frac{P(X=0,Y=y)}{P(X=0)}=\\frac{f(0,y)}{{f}_{X}(0)}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal distribution of $X.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distributions for $X$ and $Y$ correspond to the row and column totals, respectively. So, let's compute these:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.5$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.3$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.5$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.5$ | $0.15$ | $0.35$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore, for $y\\in {0,2,4},$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=0\\,|\\,Y=0) & =\\frac{f(0,0)}{{f}_{X}(0)}=\\frac{0.2}{0.5}=0.4 \\\\ P(X=0\\,|\\,Y=2) & =\\frac{f(0,2)}{{f}_{X}(0)}=\\frac{0.1}{0.5}=0.2 \\\\ P(X=0\\,|\\,Y=4) & =\\frac{f(0,4)}{{f}_{X}(0)}=\\frac{0.2}{0.5}=0.4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the conditional probability mass function can be represented by the following table:   \n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,0)$ | $0.4$ | $0.2$ | $0.4$ |" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400979 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400980 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400979 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400981 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400979 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400982 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400979 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400983 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400979 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400984 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400979 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400979 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400979 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400984 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400979 1080 #uuid "232c8a87-8c1b-58ee-be3e-6552e315bf0f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400980 1081 "| $y$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,0)$ | $0.6$ | $0.2$ | $0.6$ |" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400980 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400980 1084 #uuid "24afd0b0-d6de-56bf-ae8f-4be3381c967b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400981 1081 "| $y$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,0)$ | $0.25$ | $0.25$ | $0.5$ |" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400981 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400981 1084 #uuid "f992bbff-d9b3-5a36-9c82-3cc33ed8858f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400982 1081 "| $y$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,0)$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.5$ |" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400982 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400982 1084 #uuid "c365283b-bc38-5d73-b350-7938e68cf363" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400983 1081 "| $y$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,0)$ | $0.2$ | $0.5$ | $0.3$ |" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400983 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400983 1084 #uuid "29ea203b-ba7b-591f-b3f5-324bd7be1407" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400984 1081 "| $y$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,0)$ | $0.4$ | $0.2$ | $0.4$ |" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400984 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400984 1084 #uuid "98bfc8a2-c396-5e52-ace3-f6d5e9d34641" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400985 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400986 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400985 1069 "q-143034" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400985 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400985 1071 "The value $V$ of a particular art object increases with time. The rate of change of the object's value is proportional to the square of the value. What differential equation describes the change of the value at time $t?$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400985 1072 #uuid "b30d46be-646e-5361-a604-5fb66c710b5b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400985 1074 "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **value** $V$ of a particular art object **increases** with time. The **rate** of change of the object's value is **proportional** to the **square of the value**.  *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *value* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *value squared.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}∝{V}^{2}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the value *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=k{V}^{2}.\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400986 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400987 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400986 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400988 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400986 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400989 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400986 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400990 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400986 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400991 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400986 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400986 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400986 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400990 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400986 1080 #uuid "4527b519-e235-578b-ba4e-e12b67a2bec9" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400987 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=-k\\sqrt{V},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400987 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400987 1084 #uuid "d1888cd0-9005-51e4-8f23-a9c29cc22081" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400988 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=k\\sqrt{V},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400988 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400988 1084 #uuid "f928b778-da6a-5b79-9658-dc18dc898f6b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400989 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=-k{V}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400989 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400989 1084 #uuid "143789ed-0846-5adc-8244-a09df213d77e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400990 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=k{V}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400990 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400990 1084 #uuid "3941f316-7785-5f8b-8014-322641f53352" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400991 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{V},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400991 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400991 1084 #uuid "ef8de928-580b-5d72-8ae9-f3db96bd744c" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400992 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400993 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400992 1069 "q-143037" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400992 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400992 1071 "Construction waste stored in a large pile is taken to a landfill. The height $H$ of the pile decreases with time. The rate of change of the pile's height is proportional to the square of the height. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the height at time $t?$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400992 1072 #uuid "ae491dc9-9063-5d70-aa00-00c9f3a98d29" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400992 1074 "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **height** $H$ of the pile **decreases** with time. The **rate** of change of the pile's height is **proportional** to the **square of the height**.  *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *height* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *height squared.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}∝{H}^{2}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the height *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=-k{H}^{2}.\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400993 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400994 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400993 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400995 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400993 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400996 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400993 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400997 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400993 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400998 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400993 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400993 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400993 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400998 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400993 1080 #uuid "5afc3f62-82b2-5ca2-8452-04ff173cc875" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400994 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=-k\\sqrt{H},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400994 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400994 1084 #uuid "e3609cc0-6b67-5266-9b4a-2f29d8232471" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400995 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=k{H}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400995 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400995 1084 #uuid "ef6cd918-68d8-52d0-9155-4d41f4fd2598" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400996 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{H}^{2}},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400996 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400996 1084 #uuid "add74caf-c6d7-5a05-a30c-9b03f535871e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400997 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=-kH,\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400997 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400997 1084 #uuid "e048b22c-334e-593c-a1bb-448f1e70ae12" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400998 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=-k{H}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400998 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400998 1084 #uuid "1b08abf8-2a85-5a9c-9728-5bed51d13ad2" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400999 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401000 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400999 1069 "q-149548" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400999 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400999 1071 "Consider the function $f(x,y)=(1-x)(y+2)^{2}.$ What are the missing entries in the following sign table of $f(x,y)?$\n\n| $y>-2$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<-2$ |  |  |\n|  | $x<1$ | $x>1$ |" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400999 1072 #uuid "8fb709d8-90a5-57a1-95a3-b0285559ae32" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186400999 1074 "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=1$ and $y=-2.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, a