}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ $a=1,$ and $b=2.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\sqrt{1+{[{f}^{′}(x)]}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\sqrt{\\frac{1+{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401062 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401063 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401062 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401064 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401062 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401065 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401062 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401066 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401062 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401067 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401062 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401062 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401062 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401067 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401062 1080 #uuid "b3dd9699-b980-5dfd-8981-2e277c08e891" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401063 1081 "{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡x}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401063 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401063 1084 #uuid "606fd559-6309-5ad0-9d39-b14bac651a0e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401064 1081 "{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{ln}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401064 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401064 1084 #uuid "9b7d81c0-3670-53fa-96c1-92db4f5667c5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401065 1081 "{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401065 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401065 1084 #uuid "b70dd52d-4f80-5155-8124-3b4a4b1be40d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401066 1081 "{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{\\sqrt{1+x}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401066 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401066 1084 #uuid "0d34d36a-3d69-5d6d-803b-25c205cff3c0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401067 1081 "{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401067 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401067 1084 #uuid "f6c20d18-1824-50eb-b1e3-665bfefc7f00" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401068 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401069 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401068 1069 "q-15465" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401068 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401068 1071 "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,y=t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,0\\le t<2\\pi ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401068 1072 #uuid "16fc9f31-33f6-5972-9529-3afa5f1e1dc8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401068 1074 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-1}{1+0} \\\\  & =0\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401069 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401070 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401069 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401071 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401069 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401072 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401069 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401073 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401069 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401074 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401069 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401069 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401069 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401074 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401069 1080 #uuid "4182a726-9587-5280-b0ae-9a47c4e9e265" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401070 1081 "\\sqrt{2}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401070 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401070 1084 #uuid "bead1cb0-40bc-5682-8aea-b1306552b221" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401071 1081 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401071 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401071 1084 #uuid "86056585-0e06-5b86-b0c0-36b6f0375c43" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401072 1081 "1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401072 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401072 1084 #uuid "7c15ff06-b974-57e0-9d0d-91476444df9d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401073 1081 "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401073 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401073 1084 #uuid "552b9d8c-6c80-5fa5-9717-bf514c6bbbca" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401074 1081 "0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401074 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401074 1084 #uuid "65a93180-72f9-5046-97f5-9cb178f53496" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401075 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401076 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401075 1069 "q-15469" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401075 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401075 1071 "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=2{t}^{3}+1,\\,y={t}^{4}+2{t}^{2},\\,0\\le t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=1.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401075 1072 #uuid "7f9e0331-ffe6-5489-b436-faf1f0bea590" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401075 1074 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=6{t}^{2},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=4t({t}^{2}+1).\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{4t({t}^{2}+1)}{6{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2({t}^{2}+1)}{3t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=1,$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{2((1)^{2}+1)}{3\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401076 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401077 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401076 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401078 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401076 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401079 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401076 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401080 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401076 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401081 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401076 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401076 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401076 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401079 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401076 1080 #uuid "afbc7c1c-c03b-5382-bd6b-5a9beec491d4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401077 1081 "\\fra