ith linearly independent columns, and the expression above gives the least-squares solution of $Ax=b.$ From left to right, what are the missing parts of the equation?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401103 1072 #uuid "d32f936e-03bc-5f70-a00c-2926fd51fe56" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401103 1074 "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the normal equation\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nThen, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $R$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by ${R}^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{-1}\\cdot Rx & ={R}^{-1}\\cdot {Q}^{T}b \\\\ x & =\\,\\,\\,{R}^{-1}\\,\\,{Q}^{T}\\,b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing parts of the equation are ${R}^{-1}$ and ${Q}^{T}.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401104 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401105 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401104 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401106 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401104 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401107 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401104 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401108 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401104 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401109 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401104 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401104 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401104 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401105 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401104 1080 #uuid "3d1a3359-653b-5fbe-99d8-82db0139d073" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401105 1081 "${R}