um solutions of a differential equation, we must find all values of $c$ such that $f(c)=0.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $f(y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2,$ so we attempt solve the equation $f(c)=0,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡c+2 & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡c & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, note that $|\\operatorname{sin}⁡c|\\le 1$ for all $c.$ Therefore, the above equation has no (real) solutions.\n\nTherefore, the differential equation has no equilibrium points." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401179 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401180 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401179 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401181 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401179 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401182 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401179 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401183 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401179 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401184 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401179 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401179 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401179 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401180 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401179 1080 #uuid "68ec482b-0fe8-570d-98b4-c811d283be06" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401180 1081 "The equation has no equilibrium solutions" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401180 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401180 1084 #uuid "eafa79bc-674a-58d4-b671-ca48a2d8af37" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401181 1081 "$y(x)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401181 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401181 1084 #uuid "bf12bc70-5702-514d-a81e-85a39e9d74bf" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401182 1081 "$y(x)=0$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401182 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401182 1084 #uuid "a206451d-8757-5268-a092-52b0e62ff345" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401183 1081 "${y}_{1}(x)=-\\pi $ and ${y}_{2}(x)=\\pi $" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401183 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401183 1084 #uuid "1237e62c-9ff7-54ad-b0a2-1816c8134906" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401184 1081 "${y}_{1}(x)=0$ and ${y}_{2}(x)=\\pi $" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401184 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401184 1084 #uuid "65a7f74e-7edd-5a89-8720-8a9b642df82e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401185 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401186 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401185 1069 "q-160465" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401185 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401185 1071 "Find the locations of all of the critical points of $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u+v} \\\\ {u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401185 1072 #uuid "6940edb0-4ff9-5079-afa0-d099bcae85dd" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401185 1074 "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the locations of the critical points of $T,$ we need to solve \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)={e}^{u+v}$ and $y(u,v)={u}^{2}+{v}^{2}.$ \n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & ={e}^{u+v} & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & ={e}^{u+v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =2u & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =2v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u+v} & {e}^{u+v} \\\\ 2u & 2v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={e}^{u+v}\\cdot 2v-{e}^{u+v}\\cdot 2u \\\\  & =2{e}^{u+v}(v-u).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.$ So, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =0 \\\\ 2{e}^{u+v}(v-u) & =0 \\\\ v-u & =0 \\\\ u & =v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $u=v$ defines a line in the $uv$-plane." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401186 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401187 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401186 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401188 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401186 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401189 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401186 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401190 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401186 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401191 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401186 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401186 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401186 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401191 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401186 1080 #uuid "003d00c4-a45e-580b-a2b2-1a8ab41f3386" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401187 1081 "The critical points lie on the line $u=-2v.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401187 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401187 1084 #uuid "dfe7ddf8-1d90-5732-b4e0-9b6cb53cfed7" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401188 1081 "The critical points lie on the line $v=-2u.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401188 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401188 1084 #uuid "6b355cde-9299-54ff-9082-f28b3a088a6e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401189 1081 "The critical points lie on the line $v=2u.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401189 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401189 1084 #uuid "a417c7cf-6062-5b00-9bc3-e0de419c5534" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401190 1081 "The critical points lie on the line $u=-v.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401190 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401190 1084 #uuid "ac39e8c8-f1ca-5eec-9d60-f35deacbe886" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401191 1081 "The critical points lie on the line $u=v.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401191 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401191 1084 #uuid "0f39009f-2aaf-5fb6-b951-14bb531af992" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401192 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401193 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401192 1069 "q-160473" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401192 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401192 1071 "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}3{u}^{2}+2{v}^{2} \\\\ u+v\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401192 1072 #uuid "f05de000-4a38-5b78-b8b6-ab15cb5a35af" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401192 1074 "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the locations of the critical points of $T,$ we need to solve \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)=3{u}^{2}+2{v}^{2}$ and $y(u,v)=u+v.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =6u & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =4v \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}6u & 4v \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =6u\\cdot 1-4v\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =6u-4v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =0 \\\\ 6u-4v & =0 \\\\ v & =\\frac{3}{2}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $v=\\frac{3}{2}u$ defines a line in the $uv$-plane." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401193 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401194 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401193 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401195 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401193 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401196 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401193 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401197 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401193 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401198 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401193 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401193 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401193 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401198 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401193 1080 #uuid "753118cd-0a71-5bb3-aaee-283497ceb3e4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401194 1081 "The critical points lie on the line $v=6u.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401194 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401194 1084 #uuid "879a74f3-cdb2-5fc9-83e0-82f1953090a1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401195 1081 "The critical points lie on the hyperbola $2{v}^{2}-3{u}^{2}=1.$" 13194