6045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401225 1071 "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with unit normal vector $n,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨{z}^{2},\\,x,\\,y-{z}^{2}⟩\\,,\\,n(x,y,z)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨2,\\,-1,\\,2⟩\\,.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S=\\frac{1}{3}{∬}_{S}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401225 1072 #uuid "dd68aee4-128c-55a1-8849-b847e40933c1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401225 1074 "If $S$ is an oriented surface with unit normal vector $n,$ and $F$ is continuous vector field, then the flux of $F$ across $S$ measured with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S.\n$$\n\nCalculating the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F\\cdot n & =⟨{z}^{2},\\,x,\\,y-{z}^{2}⟩\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}⟨2,\\,-1,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨{z}^{2},\\,x,\\,y-{z}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨2,\\,-1,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(2{z}^{2}-x+2(y-{z}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{2y-x}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the flux can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}\\frac{2y-x}{3}\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{∬}_{S}2y-x\\,\\text{d}S.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401226 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401227 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401226 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401228 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401226 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401229 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401226 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401230 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401226 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401231 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401226 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401226 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401226 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401230 1319413953