6401239 1074 "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=g(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFor the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2})=-2x,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2})=-2y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(-2x)}^{2}+{(-2y)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,{x}^{2}{y}^{2}(-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\sqrt{1+4{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,(-{x}^{4}{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}{y}^{4})\\sqrt{1+4{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401240 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401241 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401240 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401242 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401240 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401243 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401240 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401244 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401240 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401245 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401240 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401240 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401240 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401243 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401240 1080 #uuid "63dd6eb1-0216-5ca0-946f-dc8a7cfe578a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401241 1081 "({x}^{2}{y}^{2}-{x}^{4}{y}^{4})\\sqrt{1+2{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401241 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401241 1084 #uuid "fef4addc-f714-5c73-ba79-b8bbf