of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<2,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401274 1072 #uuid "9cae3814-ea99-54e9-86e7-c0bc019bdf37" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401274 1074 "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/0a/0a0b92621d83d6395926a75b5cae34f479a8b9e64dfe82711094c3724b3b3220.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/3d/3ddef68bf4b4284c1b68896920fddb8d7fb0e70eba15dee103cdbc0134a9ed20.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<2,\\,-x<y<x}.\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401275 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401276 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401275 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401277 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401275 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401278 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401275 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401279 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401275 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401280 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401275 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401275 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401275 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401279 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401275 1080 #uuid "41473911-1989-5683-9728-285b3c146754" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401276 1081 "0<y\\le x" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401276 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401276 1084 #uuid "388d2b25-435c-5296-9aa6-b2d86268ab07" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401277 1081 "-x\\le y\\le x" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401277 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401277 1084 #uuid "f7697d7e-3437-54cb-8f6c-2a92ca54ced0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401278 1081 "-x\\le y<x" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401278 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401278 1084 #uuid "715a11d5-48d4-58bf-b2c8-7bc968bb12ef" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401279 1081 "-x<y<x" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401279 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401279 1084 #uuid "6585c463-6545-5cb0-b223-cfd5eb13f4f3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401280 1081 "0<y<x" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401280 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401280 1084 #uuid "2bc09c1e-549e-5605-9dc7-40a23cf11591" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401281 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401282 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401281 1069 "q-161814" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401281 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401281 1071 "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u+2w \\\\ v-u \\\\ uw\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401281 1072 #uuid "d8752c18-2285-5bd2-a3b2-ba4d0420bd04" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401281 1074 "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=u+2w,\\,y(u,v,w)=v-u,\\,z(u,v,w)=uw.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =-1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =w & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ w & 0 & u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & u\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ w & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(u-0)+2(0-w) \\\\  & =u-2w.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ u-2w & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $u-2w=0$ defines the plane $u=2w.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401282 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401283 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401282 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401284 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401282 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401285 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401282 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401286 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401282 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401287 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401282 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401282 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401282 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401287 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401282 1080 #uuid "65676948-b2fa-585d-8619-ca89f50c6f34" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401283 1081 "The critical points lie on the plane $u+v-2w=0.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401283 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401283 1084 #uuid "53f14d31-90ea-5326-97dc-45022d0835ee" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401284 1081 "The critical points lie on the elliptic cylinder ${u}^{2}+2{w}^{2}=1.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401284 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401284 1084 #uuid "b740b568-485c-5311-a423-33ea2f3eeffb" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401285 1081 "The critical points lie on the parabolic cylinder $v={u}^{2}.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401285 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401285 1084 #uuid "a6795027-5482-5bff-8214-2dd2cc097fe2" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401286 1081 "The critical points lie on the $vw-$ plane." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401286 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401286 1084 #uuid "5adbc1f1-362c-537c-bb50-2cdecc09b123" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401287 1081 "The critical points lie on the plane $u=2w.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401287 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401287 1084 #uuid "f3a89ced-7070-57be-88cf-4d4b894bd3f7" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401288 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401289 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401288 1069 "q-161816" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401288 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401288 1071 "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u} \\\\ {e}^{u+w} \\\\ uv+w\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401288 1072 #uuid "fc380b3f-d92e-5c45-8651-fac240787b92" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401288 1074 "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)={e}^{u},\\,y(u,v,w)={e}^{u+w},\\,z(u,v,w)=uv+w.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & ={e}^{u} & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & ={e}^{u+w} & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & ={e}^{u+w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =v & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =u & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u} & 0 & 0 \\\\ {e}^{u+w} & 0 & {e}^{u+w} \\\\ v & u & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={e}^{u}|\\begin{aligned}0 & {e}^{u+w} \\\\ u & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={e}^{u}(0-u{e}^{u+w}) \\\\  & =-u{e}^{2u+w}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ -u{e}^{2u+w} & =0 \\\\ u & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $u=0$ defines the plane $u=0,$ i.e., $vw$-plane." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401289 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401290 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401289 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401291 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401289 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401292 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401289 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401293 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401289 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401294 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401289 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 1319413