186401302 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401301 1069 "q-161827" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401301 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401301 1071 "![](images/9f/9f7ed51c1273b73243beb574535686f4ce3498b28c84cbe76833a3096674792c.png)\n\nThe solid enclosed by the quarter-sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=9$ for $x\\ge 0$ and $y\\le 0,$ shown above, can be described in spherical polar coordinates as" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401301 1072 #uuid "a0831acd-ddeb-5e04-811c-4d36ad3d1496" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401301 1074 "We write the position of a point (vector) in spherical polar coordinates as $(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ),$ where \n\n- $\\rho \\ge 0$ is the distance from the point to the origin,\n\n- $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi )$ is the angle between the point and the positive $x$-axis, and\n\n- $ϕ\\in [0,\\pi ]$ is the angle the corresponding vector makes with the positive $z$-axis.\n\n![](images/d3/d338181a6631c513330ef2dd3899cfb9b01cb6f4c4ff7d9cd65038b381e7fec4.png)\n\n  \n\nNotice that inside our region, the spherical polar coordinates vary withing the following domains:\n\n- $\\rho \\in [0,3]$\n\n- $\\theta \\in [\\frac{3\\pi }{2},2\\pi ]$\n\n- $ϕ\\in [0,\\pi ]$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le 3,\\,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi ,\\,0\\le ϕ\\le \\pi }.\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401302 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401303 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401302 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401304 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401302 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401305 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401302 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401306 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401302 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401307 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401302 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401302 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401302 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401304 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401302 1080 #uuid "07b9fac4-36f4-5471-8875-46834f232265" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401303 1081 "{(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le 9,\\,3\\pi /2\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi ,\\,0\\le ϕ\\le 2\\pi }" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401303 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401303 1084 #uuid "fdff4620-93ff-550e-afdc-c665cb0060db" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401304 1081 "{(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le 3,\\,3\\pi /2\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi ,\\,0\\le ϕ\\le \\pi }" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401304 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401304 1084 #uuid "6fa29027-2d4f-5367-917f-52c169af3941" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401305 1081 "{(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le \\sqrt{3},\\,3\\pi /2\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi ,\\,0\\le ϕ\\le \\pi }" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401305 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401305 1084 #uuid "9a681f25-a3d3-54aa-8220-4047401f3201" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401306 1081 "{(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le 9,\\,3\\pi /2\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi ,\\,0\\le ϕ\\le \\pi /2}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401306 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401306 1084 #uuid "ebb3ebdb-8986-5120-bc0e-293da834f2da" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401307 1081 "{(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le 3,\\,\\pi /2\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,\\,0\\le ϕ\\le \\pi }" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401307 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401307 1084 #uuid "ec03a2a0-b115-5ed7-a6b0-20a8edc98e96" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401308 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401309 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401308 1069 "q-161879" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401308 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401308 1071 "Consider the finite region $R$ in the $xyz$-space, given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x+3y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le z-3y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le z\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nGiven the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x+3y,\\,v=z-3y,\\,w=z,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the missing part of the expression below?\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}{cos}^{2}⁡(x+z)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(z-3y)\\,dV={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,dw\\,dv\\,du\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401308 1072 #uuid "4004275e-59e4-54d2-bbaa-29203ac29308" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401308 1074 "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo find the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x+3y,\\,v=z-3y,\\,w=z\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & ={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le v\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le w\\le 2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} & \\frac{∂u}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y} & \\frac{∂v}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & \\frac{∂w}{∂z}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(-3-0) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)})}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}{cos}^{2}⁡(x+z)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(z-3y)\\,dV & ={∭}_{Δ}{cos}^{2}⁡(u+v)\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\cdot |\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}{cos}^{2}⁡(u+v)\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\cdot |-\\frac{1}{3}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\frac{1}{3}{cos}^{2}⁡(u+v)\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\,\\,dw\\,dv\\,du\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401309 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401310 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401309 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401311 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401309 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401312 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401309 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401313 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401309 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401314 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401309 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401309 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [175921