z=3\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-9$ and the plane $z=y-x.$ Let $D$ be the projection of $S$ onto the $xy$-plane. The flux of $F$ across $S$ can be expressed in terms of a double integral as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∬}_{D}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be the missing expression?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401315 1072 #uuid "f21c0998-8903-5ed2-945d-a8c8324dedb7" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401315 1074 "Since we have a closed surface, the positive orientation is outward-pointing by convention. So,\n\n- the upper surface ${S}_{1}:z=g(x,y)=y-x$ is oriented upward, and\n\n- the lower surface ${S}_{2}:z=h(x,y)=3\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-9$ is oriented downward.\n\nNow, we write down the flux across each of the surfaces separately.\n\n- Consider the upper plane ${S}_{1}.$\n\nWe compute the partial derivatives of $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y-x)=-1 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y-x)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we denote $F=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩,$ then\n\n$$\nP=0,\\,Q=y,\\,R=-x.\n$$\n\n \n\nAs a result, since the positive orientation is upward, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-0\\cdot (-1)-y\\cdot 1+(-x))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-y-x)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Consider lower cone ${S}_{2}.$ \n\nWe compute the partial derivatives of $z=h(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-9)=\\frac{3x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\ \\frac{∂h}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-9)=\\frac{3y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we denote $F=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩,$ then\n\n$$\nP=0,\\,Q=y,\\,R=-x.\n$$\n\n \n\nAs a result, since the positive orientation is upward, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & =-{∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∬}_{D}(-0\\cdot \\frac{3x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}-y\\cdot \\frac{3y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}+(-x))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∬}_{D}(-\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}-x)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}+x)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the flux across the entire surface is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S+{∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-y-x)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}(\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}+x)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}-y\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401316 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401317 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401316 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401318 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401316 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401319 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401316 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401320 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401316 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401321 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401316 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401316 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401316 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401320 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401316 1080 #uuid "531e02f0-754c-57e9-98aa-5097314bafb8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401317 1081 "\\frac{xy}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}-y" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401317 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401317 1084 #uuid "6df4d06f-b85b-5df3-8dc8-2bb8f495582f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401318 1081 "y-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401318 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401318 1084 #uuid "1a198055-107c-5684-9d14-e7c623094522" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401319 1081 "1-\\frac{xy}{\\sqrt{