474c35e1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401396 1081 "$A$ and $D$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401396 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401396 1084 #uuid "0d45bd81-d2af-5d91-9d5a-2b641a8316e0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401397 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401398 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401397 1069 "q-162811" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401397 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401397 1071 "Suppose we would like to find the maximum value of the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}z$ on the intersection of the surfaces ${x}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1$ and ${y}^{2}+z=9$ using the method of Lagrange multipliers. Then, the corresponding Lagrange multipliers $\\lambda $ and $\\mu $ satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}⟨2x,\\,2yz,\\,{y}^{2}⟩=\\lambda ⟨\\boxed{}\\,, \\,0,\\,2z⟩+\\mu ⟨0,\\boxed{}\\,,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {x}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1 \\\\ {y}^{2}+z=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing expressions?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401397 1072 #uuid "8afa6e7b-08b3-5fd6-b960-921c9d4bc534" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401397 1074 "We need to find the maximum value of \n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}z\n$$\n\n \n\nsubject to the constraints \n\n$$\ng(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1,\\,h(x,y,z)={y}^{2}+z=9.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the method of Lagrange multipliers, we must solve the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z)=\\lambda ∇g(x,y,z)+\\mu ∇h(x,y,z) \\\\ g(x,y,z)=1 \\\\ h(x,y,z)=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now expand the first equation of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\lambda ∇g(x,y,z)+\\mu ∇h(x,y,z) \\\\ ⟨{f}_{x},{f}_{y},{f}_{z}⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨{g}_{x},{g}_{y},{g}_{z}⟩+\\mu ⟨{h}_{x},{h}_{y},{h}_{z}⟩ \\\\ ⟨2x,\\,2yz,\\,{y}^{2}⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨2x,\\,0,\\,2z⟩+\\mu ⟨0,\\,2y,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401398 1