92186401404 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401405 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401404 1069 "q-162812" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401404 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401404 1071 "Suppose we would like to find the minimum value of the function $f(x,y,z)=xy+{z}^{2}$ on the intersection of the surfaces $y-x=0$ and ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=4$ using the method of Lagrange multipliers. Then, the corresponding Lagrange multipliers $\\lambda $ and $\\mu $ satisfy the following system: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}⟨y,\\,x,\\,2z⟩=\\lambda ⟨-1,\\boxed{}\\,, \\,0⟩+\\mu ⟨2x,\\,2y,\\boxed{}\\,⟩ \\\\ y-x=0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing expressions?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401404 1072 #uuid "5a114a88-7824-55e2-8ac4-08f991d5f004" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401404 1074 "We need to find the minimum value of \n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=xy+{z}^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nsubject to the constraints \n\n$$\ng(x,y,z)=y-x=0,\\,h(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the method of Lagrange multipliers, we must solve the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z)=\\lambda ∇g(x,y,z)+\\mu ∇h(x,y,z) \\\\ g(x,y,z)=0 \\\\ h(x,y,z)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now expand the first equation of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\lambda ∇g(x,y,z)+\\mu ∇h(x,y,z) \\\\ ⟨{f}_{x},{f}_{y},{f}_{z}⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨{g}_{x},{g}_{y},{g}_{z}⟩+\\mu ⟨{h}_{x},{h}_{y},{h}_{z}⟩ \\\\ ⟨y,\\,x,\\,2z⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨-1,\\,1,\\,0⟩+\\mu ⟨2x,\\,2y,\\,2z⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401405 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401406 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401405 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401407 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401405 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401408 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401405 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401409 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401405 1075 #e