)=[\\begin{aligned}xy \\\\ {x}^{2}-y \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe total derivative ${f}^{′}$ is given by \n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}y & \\boxed{} \\\\ \\boxed{} & -1 \\\\ \\boxed{} & x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom, what are the missing entries?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401411 1072 #uuid "e019c258-2f09-55a3-ab9c-d440f05baea0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401411 1074 "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)=y,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy)=x, \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-y)=2x,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-y)=-1, \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy))=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy),\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy))=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}y & x \\\\ 2x & -1 \\\\ y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy) & x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThus, the missing entries are $x,\\,$ $2x,\\,$ and $y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401412 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401413 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401412 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401414 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401412 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401415 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401412 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401416 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401412 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401417 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401412 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401412 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401412 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401416 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401412 1080 #uuid "5bc9a4e2-1d70-54d1-8a2a-b5a3fd7bf284" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401413 1081 "$x,\\,$ $2x,\\,$ and $x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401413 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401413 1084 #uuid "0982cdc8-9442-57fe-b7fa-346753e57354" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401414 1081 "$x,\\,$ $2x,\\,$ and $y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401414 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401414 1084 #uuid "d02b2ee1-2d41-522a-96b3-adfd227f36c3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401415 1081 "$x,\\,$ $x,\\,$ and $y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401415 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401415 1084 #uuid "9b952bee-251b-539e-8f7d-67e73938f6f8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401416 1081 "$x,\\,$ $2x,\\,$ and $y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401416 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401416 1084 #uuid "03a4583d-e5ff-5e79-9be7-41b39f117fc3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401417 1081 "$x,\\,$ $x,\\,$ and $x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401417 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401417 1084 #uuid "71423d40-798c-5652-a081-532957655dd8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401418 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401419 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401418 1069 "q-163100" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401418 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401418 1071 "For the transformation $f:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{xyz} \\\\ x+yz\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe total derivative ${f}^{′}$ is given by \n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{} & xz{e}^{xyz} & xy{e}^{xyz} \\\\ 1 & \\boxed{} & \\boxed{}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing entries?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401418 1072 #uuid "e4436f3f-18fe-5775-815d-04fe166d17a2" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401418 1074 "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂z}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{xyz})=yz{e}^{xyz},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{xyz})=xz{e}^{xyz},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({e}^{xyz})=xy{e}^{xyz} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+yz)=1,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x+yz)=z,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x+yz)=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}yz{e}^{xyz} & xz{e}^{xyz} & xy{e}^{xyz} \\\\ 1 & z & y\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401419 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401420 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401419 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401421 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401419 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401422 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401419 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401423 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401419 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401424 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401419 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401419 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401419 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401423 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401419 1080 #uuid "9cbe7815-5a90-5779-9948-27720bbf467a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401420 1081 "$x{e}^{xyz},\\,$ $z,\\,$ and $z$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401420 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401420 1084 #uuid "d959d5d7-cbc1-5318-b797-c37a0afbbf37" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401421 1081 "${e}^{xyz},\\,$ $2x,\\,$ and $y$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401421 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401421 1084 #uuid "b30dc2cc-68a4-5912-8a3e-df5e08613c6e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401422 1081 "$yz{e}^{yz},\\,$ $0,\\,$ and $y$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401422 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401422 1084 #uuid "3fd45803-73b4-58a2-b054-1d9f41e88d38" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401423 1081 "$yz{e}^{xyz},\\,$ $z,\\,$ and $y$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401423 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401423 1084 #uuid "43123342-28a0-58f0-8627-2ed0371a4ca3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401424 1081 "$z{e}^{xyz},\\,$ $z,\\,$ and $z$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401424 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401424 1084 #uuid "1c151508-a070-5be8-9646-29a3b6c0d0e1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401425 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401426 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401425 1069 "q-163771" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401425 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401425 1071 "The quadratic Taylor approximation of the function $f(x)$ about $x=a\\in {R}^{3}$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈-\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{1}{2}(x-a)^{T}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}](x-a).\n$$\n\nGiven that the eigenvalues of ${f}^{″}(a)$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=1,{\\lambda }_{2}=2,$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=3,$ what type of point is $a?$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401425 1072 #uuid "c9ce8c10-95e8-5421-97ed-611d96bbf7c9" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401425 1074 "The point $a\\in {R}^{n}$ is a critical point of the function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ if ${f}^{′}(a)={0}^{T}.$ In such cases, we can classify $a$ as follows:\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is positive definite, then $a$ is a local minimum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is negative definite, then $a$ is a local maximum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite, then $a$ is a saddle point\n\nThe quadratic Taylor expansion of a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ about $x=a\\in {R}^{n}$ given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{1}{2}(x-a)^{T}{f}^{″}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSince the quadratic Taylor expansion of $f$ has no $(x-a)$ term, we can conclude that ${f}^{′}(a)={0}^{T}.$ Hence, $a$ is a critical point of $f.$\n\nFinally, notice that all the eigenvalues of ${f}^{″}(a)$ are positive:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1} & =1>0 \\\\ {\\lambda }_{2} & =2>0 \\\\ {\\lambda }_{3} & =3>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the matrix is positive definite. Therefore, $a$ is a local minimum of $f.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401426 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401427 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401426 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401428 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401426 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401429 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401426 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401430 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401426 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401431 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401426 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401426 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401426 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401430 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401426 1080 #uuid "c860e53e-f867-5749-aa4f-e7a554c597fa" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401427 1081 "local maximum" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401427 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401427 1084 #uuid "5a1cab09-af4c-5681-b572-7073c44cadd1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401428 1081 "inconclusive" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401428 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401428 1084 #uuid "79bc2964-acb4-51b0-b007-9d90d00e18e8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401429 1081 "not a critical point" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401429 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401429 1084 #uuid "17c52ede-9d07-5f7f-8b20-6215a7509689" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401430 1081 "local minimum" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401430 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401430 1084 #uuid "869eb4f4-f69e-53fa-8018-2d9ffbf80a5f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401431 1081 "saddle point" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401431 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401431 1084 #uuid "e113570c-5c60-57ef-a5c6-a06bf8ad264a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401432 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401433 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401432 1069 "q-163834" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401432 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401432 1071 "![](images/21/215b322e06280dd01e5858df9a17cd56673b5cdec69521decca205e03771ac21.png)\n\nThe graph $z=f(x,y)$ is shown above. What are the global maximum points of the function?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401432 1072 #uuid "8c163c8c-12fc-59a2-9e1d-9f264f8ad03a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401432 1074 "First, we recall the following definitions:\n\n- The global maximum of a function is the largest value it attains on its domain. There can only be (at most) one global maximum.\n\n- A global maximum point is a point $(x,y,z)$ where a function reaches a global maximum. There can be zero, one, or many global maximum points.\n\nFor our function, the maximum value reached by the function is $f(x,y)=3.$ Therefore, the global maximum is $3.$ The function reaches this value when $(x,y)=(-2,1),$ so the global maximum point is $(-2,1,3).$\n\n![](images/d5/d5f948483a80f37257b285d48cd1e6bbf1d8a6ba9b66d1fea5edd865c787711a.png)" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401433 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401434 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401433 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401435 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401433 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401436 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401433 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401437 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401433 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401438 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401433 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401433 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401433 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401437 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401433 1080 #uuid "32d7053b-a2c6-58ee-8efc-3a03178f6bd3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401434 1081 "$(1,0,-2)$ and $(2,3,0)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401434 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401434 1084 #uuid "d12bfd22-9e9d-5d37-bbd0-35e563e5e30a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401435 1081 "$(0,-2,1.2)$  only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401435 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401435 1084 #uuid "99f7cc57-ad3a-5493-ba20-b02d01c3c072" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401436 1081 "$(2,3,0)$  only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401436 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401436 1084 #uuid "7d4d1de4-cb9d-5b3a-b919-1ee28c961db6" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401437 1081 "$(-2,1,3)$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401437 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401437 1084 #uuid "27f2d2ad-7cab-5c68-bfaf-a31ab980901d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401438 1081 "$(0,-2,1.2)$ and $(-2,1,3)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401438 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401438 1084 #uuid "d947cbda-24ab-58ef-b437-c399ba283d13" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401439 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401440 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401439 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401441 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401439 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401442 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401439 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401443 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401439 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401444 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401439 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401439 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401439 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401440 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401439 1080 #uuid "ef647b19-79e2-5b54-b8df-1bf5fe9db9b4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401440 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)y=\\frac{1+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401440 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401440 1084 #uuid "c4bcf009-6fca-5110-8ae8-643678b3cb9e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401441 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)y=1+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401441 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401441 1084 #uuid "eb82a4b2-58af-556c-a366-f92624768704" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401442 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)y=1+\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401442 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401442 1084 #uuid "f4a26a57-987c-5668-b531-e2f3db2b75bc" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401443 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)y=1+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401443 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401443 1084 #uuid "b6972414-a235-5987-855e-567ba571b605" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401444 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}=(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)y" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401444 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401444 1084 #uuid "e08cc03c-cea4-583d-b68b-e5c8622f76e1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401445 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401446 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401445 1069 "q-164152" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401445 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401445 1071 "![](images/c4/c460920f6b2516ac8603852e12d15840cca051736555ea43cf15a278ef9e0155.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $z=f(x,y)$ is shown above. Which of the points shown are local maximum points?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401445 1072 #uuid "2740d2d6-bc06-5779-9308-da4a9d560214" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401445 1074 "A function $f(x,y)$ has a local maximum point at $(a,b)$ if $f(x,y)\\le f(a,b)$ for all points $(x,y)$ in a neighborhood of $(a,b).$ \n\nIn other words, we can take a neighborhood of $(x,y)$-values such that the point $(x,y,f(x,y))$ is the highest point on the graph in the neighborhood.\n\nSuch neighborhoods exist for the points $C$ and $D.$ Hence $C$ and $D$ are local maxima.\n\n![](images/cc/cc526bb1cf73fb5b5579966e91077ccd096aea475a4cf13196166bd65ac88d7b.png)" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401446 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401447 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401446 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401448 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401446 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401449 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401446 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401450 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401446 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401451 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401446 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401446 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401446 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401451 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401446 1080 #uuid "b8d87059-ea13-55bb-b541-23109862b322" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401447 1081 "The function does not have local maxima" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401447 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401447 1084 #uuid "475ce117-63c5-5ee4-b359-fc20c9c51651" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401448 1081 "$D$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401448 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401448 1084 #uuid "cc880a4e-5176-5965-abb2-4d59cb691ec9" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401449 1081 "$A$ and $B$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401449 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401449 1084 #uuid "e2bd567a-a4c4-543c-81f0-2381cab6d5e8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401450 1081 "$C$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401450 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401450 1084 #uuid "56368805-72a8-566e-a53d-bb48170c39e2" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401451 1081 "$C$ and $D$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401451 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401451 1084 #uuid "41a0973a-78e5-5b21-83f7-bcf5f3ddb6d3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401452 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401453 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401452 1069 "q-164267" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401452 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401452 1071 "Given the ellipsoid $\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(z-2)^{2}}{16}=1$, find its intercepts with the $y$-axis." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401452 1072 #uuid "50783562-e3df-58d6-82c6-67c9daca87a3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401452 1074 "To find the $y$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(0+2)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{4}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =1 \\\\ y & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $y=-1$ and $y=1.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $y$-axis are $(0,-1,0)$ and $(0,1,0).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401453 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401454 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401453 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401455 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401453 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401456 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401453 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401457 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401453 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401458 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401453 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401453 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401453 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401456 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401453 1080 #uuid "de275abf-f996-5e86-903d-b371c046139e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401454 1081 "$(0,-\\frac{1}{2},0)$ and $(0,1,0)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401454 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401454 1084 #uuid "bd89ecad-0fc0-5ba5-a620-05712d3a1b08" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401455 1081 "$(0,0,0)$ and $(0,\\frac{1}{2},0)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401455 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401455 1084 #uuid "d50858b8-1fd8-5038-a72e-57fc3037d5e2" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401456 1081 "$(0,-1,0)$ and $(0,1,0)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401456 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401456 1084 #uuid "0fd95cab-9721-51ba-b9c4-0bf0be760265" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401457 1081 "$(0,-1,0)$ and $(0,\\frac{1}{2},0)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401457 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401457 1084 #uuid "99d03f44-97f1-5754-9f11-086ea13d97fe" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401458 1081 "$(0,-\\frac{1}{2},0)$ and $(0,\\frac{1}{2},0)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401458 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401458 1084 #uuid "4408e820-21f8-5788-8399-5558cbe467ac" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401459 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401460 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401459 1069 "q-164272" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401459 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401459 1071 "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets ${x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{4}=-1,$ find its $z$-intercepts." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401459 1072 #uuid "b589cdc8-22e6-5881-b7f2-9fb3725db0fb" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401459 1074 "To find the $z$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $y=0$ into the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{0}^{2}+\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{4} & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{4} & =-1 \\\\ (z+1)^{2} & =4 \\\\ z+1 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ z & =-1\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $z=-3$ and $z=1.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $z$-axis are $(0,0,-3)$ and $(0,0,1).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401460 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401461 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401460 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401462 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401460 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401463 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401460 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401464 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401460 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401465 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401460 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401460 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401460 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401462 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401460 1080 #uuid "2c38e30b-5bcd-54ca-8ea6-28e179828a4c" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401461 1081 "$(0,0,-3)$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401461 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401461 1084 #uuid "4bb29e98-356d-5e90-ac97-d29d6178c40e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401462 1081 "$(0,0,-3)$ and $(0,0,1)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401462 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401462 1084 #uuid "6a12cd1c-6682-5df8-923c-6c5944da1e21" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401463 1081 "$(0,0,-2)$ and $(0,0,2)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401463 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401463 1084 #uuid "6dea4a01-2c2d-5563-9522-56b73624cc0d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401464 1081 "$(0,0,-1)$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401464 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401464 1084 #uuid "9addb0b5-d438-50d6-917d-38fb314ead17" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401465 1081 "The hyperboloid does not intersect the $z$-axis" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401465 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401465 1084 #uuid "5e7a3e71-8adf-5c96-a5b6-a2346b9e5122" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401466 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401467 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401466 1069 "q-164311" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401466 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401466 1071 "Given the sphere $(x-3)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}+(z-2)^{2}=9,$ what is the domain of $z=z(x,y)?$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401466 1072 #uuid "3e6a384d-7ca2-5551-9c7a-30830f5ff58a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401466 1074 "From the equation of the sphere, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}+(z-2)^{2} & =9 \\\\ (z-2)^{2} & =9-((x-3)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}) \\\\ z-2 & =\\pm \\sqrt{9-((x-3)^{2}+(y-1)^{2})} \\\\ z & =2\\pm \\sqrt{9-((x-3)^{2}+(y-1)^{2})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the square root is defined only for non-negative arguments, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9-((x-3)^{2}+(y-1)^{2})\\ge 0 \\\\ (x-3)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}\\le 9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis inequality describes the interior and boundary of the circle \n\n$$\n(x-3)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=9\n$$\n\nwhich is a circle of radius $3$ centered at $(3,1)$ in the $xy$-plane." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401467 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401468 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401467 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401469 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401467 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401470 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401467 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401471 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401467 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401472 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401467 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401467 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401467 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401468 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401467 1080 #uuid "182e0ed3-43fe-59b0-b733-03b03b4eb82f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401468 1081 "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $3$ centered at $(3,1)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401468 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401468 1084 #uuid "9e71a948-a9c5-5faf-b47c-17e50a3f8324" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401469 1081 "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $3$ centered at $(1,-3)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401469 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401469 1084 #uuid "1e85c958-d38e-5452-bf22-85abbc7a75bf" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401470 1081 "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $\\sqrt{3}$ centered at $(-3,1)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401470 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401470 1084 #uuid "df3c0953-d686-59f3-a7d7-fe00ebde4e1d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401471 1081 "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $\\sqrt{3}$ centered at $(3,2)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401471 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401471 1084 #uuid "c7c4b9ff-1b21-54cc-b53e-7eb6f046091b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401472 1081 "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $\\sqrt{3}$ centered at $(1,3)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401472 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401472 1084 #uuid "598580ec-0b00-5ab0-a4fe-2e46a90d75e6" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401473 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401474 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401473 1069 "q-164400" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401473 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401473 1071 "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the parabolic cylinder $(x+3)^{2}=6y?$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401473 1072 #uuid "7c06a8e8-6e3d-50f3-ae2e-200f38471a76" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401473 1074 "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the cylinder, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0+3)^{2} & =6y \\\\ 9 & =6y \\\\ y & =\\frac{9}{6} \\\\ y & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a line in the $yz$-plane." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401474 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401475 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401474 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401476 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401474 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401477 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401474 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401478 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401474 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401479 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401474 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401474 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401474 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401478 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401474 1080 #uuid "770068c0-e321-5534-9c7a-f0ff2132d3c7" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401475 1081 "The parabola $(x+3)^{2}=6z$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401475 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401475 1084 #uuid "ff45c2a2-3a41-5311-99ca-5e68d6a5cab4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401476 1081 "The line $y=3$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401476 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401476 1084 #uuid "de23290b-1126-571c-a0e8-9a9fda87468d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401477 1081 "The parabola ${x}^{2}=6(z-3)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401477 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401477 1084 #uuid "86e5f373-6dc5-578d-9dab-a014632c2480" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401478 1081 "The line $y=\\frac{3}{2}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401478 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401478 1084 #uuid "017e8e93-5da0-5960-ba95-563c27bee3c1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401479 1081 "The lines $y=-3$ and $y=15$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401479 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401479 1084 #uuid "defd7bf9-9f21-5237-ad4c-3feffa02e09e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401480 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401481 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401480 1069 "q-164401" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401480 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401480 1071 "What is the trace in the $xz$-plane of the elliptic cylinder $\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{2}=1?$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401480 1072 #uuid "98ad452f-818a-5095-bf60-3f83ccbaae0f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401480 1074 "To find the trace in the $xz$-plane, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the cylinder, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(0-1)^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{1}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{8} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ (x-4)^{2} & =4 \\\\ x-4 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ x & =4\\pm 2 \\\\ x & =2,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of two lines $x=2$ and $x=6$ in the $xz$-plane." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401481 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401482 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401481 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401483 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401481 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401484 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401481 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401481 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401481 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401481 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401481 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401484 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401481 1080 #uuid "53177c21-6f8b-5255-86cb-d89db3a9a51a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401482 1081 "The line $x=4$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401482 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401482 1084 #uuid "ddfe34f7-e006-5620-84fe-1db6fc963651" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401483 1081 "The line $x=6$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401483 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401483 1084 #uuid "b838d302-7461-5223-8e33-c740bbf20ff9" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401484 1081 "The lines $x=2$ and $x=6$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401484 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401484 1084 #uuid "161fe7ca-7c93-5282-b813-a0a45f65d7ac" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401485 1081 "The ellipse $\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}=1$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401485 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401485 1084 #uuid "2cfcfb48-24ef-595a-a479-2f2b1a35f56d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401486 1081 "The hyperbola $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{2}=1$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401486 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401486 1084 #uuid "b309b4aa-316e-5e47-b444-65898ffba0f5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401487 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401488 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401487 1069 "q-164403" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401487 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401487 1071 "Identify the following surface: \n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{7}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}=1\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401487 1072 #uuid "1ef46611-6066-5608-b7b6-cb53d9ef1a50" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401487 1074 "Recall that the equation of an ellipsoid centered at $O$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=1,\n$$\n\nand an ellipsoid centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-{x}_{0})^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-{y}_{0})^{2}}{{b}^{2}}+\\frac{(z-{z}_{0})^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=1,\n$$\n\nThus, our equation is an ellipsoid with the following parameters:\n\n$$\n({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(1,-2,0),\\,a=3,\\,b=\\sqrt{7},\\,c=2.\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401488 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401489 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401488 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401490 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401488 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401491 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401488 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401492 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401488 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401488 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401488 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401488 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401488 1080 #uuid "903d6dd5-4634-519d-8334-fc52eabb5e80" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401489 1081 "A paraboloid" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401489 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401489 1084 #uuid "91eeb41c-1501-568e-81cf-b44bd4f6787f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401490 1081 "A cylinder" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401490 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401490 1084 #uuid "2b39f102-3558-5351-90f8-01a7c7dbb286" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401491 1081 "A hyperboloid" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401491 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500