[17592186401557 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401558 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401557 1069 "q-164555" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401557 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401557 1071 "Identify the surface ${x}^{2}+5{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}-2x+20y+11=0.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401557 1072 #uuid "84fd9eec-1cf5-594c-8917-00bf240277f1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401557 1074 "First, we complete the square in the $x$ and $y$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+5{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}-2x+20y+11 & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2x)+5({y}^{2}+4y)+{z}^{2}+11 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}-1+5([y+2)^{2}-4]+{z}^{2}+11 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}-1+5(y+2)^{2}-20+{z}^{2}+11 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+5(y+2)^{2}+{z}^{2}-10 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}+5(y+2)^{2}+{z}^{2}-10 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+5(y+2)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =10 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{10}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{10} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of an ellipsoid centered at $(1,-2,0).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401558 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401559 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401558 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401560 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401558 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401561 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401558 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401562 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401558 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401563 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401558 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401558 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401558 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401559 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401558 1080 #uuid "f0d3a90f-543b-5602-bf42-4796008282b3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401559 1081 "An ellipsoid centered at $(1,-2,0)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401559 1083 #edb/ref 1759