c{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=-1$ and $k=-3,$ so the center is located at $(-1,-3).$\n\nIn the given equation, we also have ${a}^{2}=5$ and ${b}^{2}=20.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=5,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{5}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=20,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{20}=2\\sqrt{5}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=2\\sqrt{5},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=\\sqrt{5}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{5}=4\\sqrt{5},$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\sqrt{5}=2\\sqrt{5}.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401565 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401566 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401565 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401567 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401565 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401568 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401565 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401569 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401565 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401570 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401565 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401565 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401565 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401569 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401565 1080 #uuid "a9fd9c31-b922-5bc4-b3d4-983574117b6f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401566 1081 "$2\\sqrt{5}$ and $4$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401566 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401566 1084 #uuid "e8434a84-5ef1-505b-a2c7-d42809c26959" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401567 1081 "$2\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\sqrt{5}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401567 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401567 1084 #uuid "386a0708-44f8-5648-9834-907d2d7fef7b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401568 1081 "$4$ and $\\sqrt{5}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401568 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401568 1084 #uuid "f019f459-9c8d-5bca-ac2e-8bf08a5f03f3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401569 1081 "$4\\sqrt{5}$ and $2\\sqrt{5}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401569 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401569 1084 #uuid "1362416b-6b2e-5b41-8cce-b430bb96c908" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401570 1081 "$4\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\sqrt{5}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401570 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401570 1084 #uuid "c489543f-9ba5-563a-8700-e139b5d4d02f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401571 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401572 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401571 1069 "q-16642" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401571 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401571 1071 "Calculate the points where the ellipse $\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{9}=1$ intercepts the $x$-axis." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401571 1072 #uuid "fca3c3f7-188d-5506-9818-be66c0607803" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401571 1074 "To calculate the $x$-intercept, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $x.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{4}{9} & =1 \\\\ 9(x-3)^{2}+16 & =36 \\\\ 9(x-3)^{2} & =20 \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =\\frac{20}{9} \\\\ x-3 & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{20}{9}} \\\\ x & =3\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $x$-axis at the points $(3-\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3},0)$ and $(3+\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3},0).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401572 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401573 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592