is $2.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401621 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401621 1084 #uuid "dfbc4514-da7a-5d32-bb0c-75cb3c1af14e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401622 1081 "There exists no rational number whose triple is $2.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401622 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401622 1084 #uuid "00b16d7a-3879-5b16-a22b-05c9128f9304" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401623 1081 "There exists a rational number whose triple is a multiple of $2.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401623 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401623 1084 #uuid "445c2f89-43cc-540c-a4c7-441ca2f3d468" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401624 1081 "Triple every rational number is not $2.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401624 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401624 1084 #uuid "db52d8b1-5884-5600-886d-f29af9a8111f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401625 1081 "Triple every rational number is $2.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401625 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401625 1084 #uuid "33760338-3c64-54bf-8af4-8c4133bc6f27" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401626 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401627 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401626 1069 "q-171999" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401626 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401626 1071 "$\\,$ $∀x\\in (0,1),\\,x>{x}^{2}$\n\nWhich of the following expresses the statement given above?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401626 1072 #uuid "698421f5-96c5-5307-a8fb-d2ac4a250cc1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401626 1074 "The universal quantifier \"$∀$\" means \"for all.\" So, our quantified statement reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ **For all** $x\\in (0,1),\\,x>{x}^{2}.$\n\nThis can be further simplified as follows:\n\n$\\,$ Every number between $0$ and $1$ is greater than its square.\n\n**Note:** This statement is true." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401627 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401628 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401627 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401629 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401627 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401630 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401627 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401631 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401627 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401632 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401627 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401627 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401627 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401632 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401627 1080 #uuid "e4f005b5-9729-5d5f-b912-f7b0246c77fd" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401628 1081 "There exists a number between $0$ and $1$ that is greater than its square." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401628 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401628 1084 #uuid "0fe9a0e2-c6d2-56ac-b91e-b2347fd649b4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401629 1081 "Consider the square of every number between $0$ and $1.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401629 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401629 1084 #uuid "286a7a4d-b364-5fd1-bc1c-cdcc0f25f9a8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401630 1081 "Every number is greater than its square." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401630 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401630 1084 #uuid "676c24b5-3446-5b45-8adc-2f8128e722d4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401631 1081 "There is a number whose square is between $0$ and $1.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401631 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401631 1084 #uuid "db1e01e2-6988-5261-bb19-4bde540dddf9" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401632 1081 "Every number between $0$ and $1$ is greater than its square." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401632 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401632 1084 #uuid "9830dd3d-604d-5712-a275-601b3e2f9f76" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401633 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401634 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401633 1069 "q-17392" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401633 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401633 1071 "Given that $y=2{x}^{e}-ln⁡x$, find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401633 1072 #uuid "104d7814-9b21-55a2-864d-c61ec56f5c8f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401633 1074 "To find the instantaneous rate of change at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{e}-ln⁡x) \\\\  & =2e{x}^{e-1}-\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(2e{x}^{e-1}-\\frac{1}{x})|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =2e\\cdot {1}^{e-1}-\\frac{1}{1} \\\\  & =2e-1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401634 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401635 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401634 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401636 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401634 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401637 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401634 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401638 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401634 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401639 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401634 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401634 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401634 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401636 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401634 1080 #uuid "5088efea-7f9e-57d5-8f9c-14c688a0e06b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401635 1081 "2e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401635 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401635 1084 #uuid "0beb1ecb-7649-51d5-8923-8085f1d146bc" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401636 1081 "2e-1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401636 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401636 1084 #uuid "aa5ec049-b8d0-5c17-a28c-05813122674f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401637 1081 "2" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401637 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401637 1084 #uuid "c2d87b1b-17a5-523c-a973-f5e0ad287cd3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401638 1081 "2e+1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401638 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401638 1084 #uuid "ea4f4094-0cfd-5ae4-8308-88f0b83b2c27" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401639 1081 "-1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401639 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401639 1084 #uuid "946c0adc-baba-5359-a975-69b7a89f4838" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401640 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401641 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401640 1069 "q-175404" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401640 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401640 1071 "Given that \n\n$$\nP(x):x\\text{ is }\\text{not}\\text{ prime},\n$$\n\n \nwhich of the following represents $¬P(x)?$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401640 1072 #uuid "813f8661-6028-5444-9eb0-c5477e6d2450" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401640 1074 "The symbol \"$¬$\" represents negation. So, our task is to negate the given sentence. \n\nTo negate our plain English sentence, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\n$$\n¬P(x):\\text{It is not true that }x\\text{ is }\\text{not}\\text{ prime},\n$$\n\n \n\nIn other words, $x$ is prime. Therefore, $¬P(x)$ means the following:\n\n$$\n¬P(x):x\\text{ is prime}.\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401641 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401642 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401641 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401643 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401641 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401644 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401641 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401645 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401641 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401646 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401641 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401641 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401641 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401645 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401641 1080 #uuid "e6698acc-7b29-5b47-adfc-142f7b407f15" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401642 1081 "$-x$ is not prime" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401642 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401642 1084 #uuid "1c4342a2-aa37-5d96-b2bd-53d063965b9f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401643 1081 "$1$ is not prime" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401643 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401643 1084 #uuid "15a35b0c-6fdf-55ef-951e-82f3c0ef6382" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401644 1081 "$x$ is not prime" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401644 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401644 1084 #uuid "ed204714-bf39-5405-9311-45ac92c2d622" 13194139533478 17