[17592186401817 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401817 1084 #uuid "cb8e226f-a28c-5b1a-b7df-6f312bfd06a3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401818 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401819 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401818 1069 "q-19299" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401818 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401818 1071 "The position $s(t)$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by \n\n$$\ns(t)=4{e}^{-t}+3{t}^{2}-2t+1,\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity at time $t=2.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401818 1072 #uuid "59ea1544-758d-5928-bf3f-4995dd8b61f1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401818 1074 "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{e}^{-t}+3{t}^{2}-2t+1) \\\\  & =-4{e}^{-t}+6t-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the velocity at $t=2,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the velocity function above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =-4{e}^{-2}+6\\cdot 2-2 \\\\  & =-4{e}^{-2}+10 \\\\  & =9.458\\,658… \\\\  & ≈9.46\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401819 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401820 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401819 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401821 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401819 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401822 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401819 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401823 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401819 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401824 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401819 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401819 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401819 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401820 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401819 1080 #uuid "ab640647-5232-553a-be5a-08e8539221b0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401820 1081 "v=9.46" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401820 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401820 1084 #uuid "e41ae0ea-e83b-581f-a124-c29c127545ab" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401821 1081 "v=4.94" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401821 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401821 1084 #uuid "2ddc81bc-6b74-5b86-9aa6-68b7985e21ee" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401822 1081 "v=10.03" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401822 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401822 1084 #uuid "4c2d52e0-5f90-57ca-a8a9-c0f4aaadbdfb" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401823 1081 "v=9.24" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401823 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401823 1084 #uuid "e34561e5-c74f-5726-99b2-cd744a8924ae" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401824 1081 "v=8.36" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401824 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401824 1084 #uuid "eea394a2-6e5a-5394-a910-d19a50a2530e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401825 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401826 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401825 1069 "q-19302" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401825 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401825 1071 "The position $s(t)$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by \n\n$$\ns(t)={t}^{2}-2t+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity at time $t=3.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401825 1072 #uuid "3df15b1d-5c6a-5a31-88c3-94f27234c33f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401825 1074 "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-2t+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t) \\\\  & =2t-2+\\frac{1}{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the velocity at $t=3,$ we substitute $t=3$ into the velocity function above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(3) & =2(3)-2+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =6-2+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{3} \\\\  & =4.333\\,333… \\\\  & ≈4.33\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401826 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401827 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401826 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401828 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401826 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401829 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401826 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401830 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401826 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401831 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401826 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401826 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401826 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401829 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401826 1080 #uuid "2dc005a4-0a0a-5369-9aa9-e0229fc91626" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401827 1081 "v=6.67" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401827 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401827 1084 #uuid "9733cf69-5d70-514e-a80d-eadad1d41489" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401828 1081 "v=8.05" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401828 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401828 1084 #uuid "85286b89-c2a3-56c9-a420-e9d18189a069" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401829 1081 "v=4.33" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401829 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401829 1084 #uuid "259c571e-8927-56b2-95c0-5bb1688deec4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401830 1081 "v=3.75" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401830 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401830 1084 #uuid "1ebd6114-b8d6-5140-a703-c4dd01c13274" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401831 1081 "v=0.22" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401831 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401831 1084 #uuid "5f2eab8c-d466-5781-91a5-1f6a93c6b3d4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401832 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401833 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401832 1069 "q-19493" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401832 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401832 1071 "Use the first two non-zero terms of the Taylor expansion of ${x}^{1/3}$ about $x=8$ to approximate the value of ${7}^{1/3}.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401832 1072 #uuid "c2001916-7ed2-504f-9a8e-d02fda09253a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401832 1074 "We use Taylor's formula in the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(a)}{2!}(x-a)^{2}+⋯,\n$$\n\nwith $a=8.$ \n\nCalculating the necessary derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={x}^{1/3} \\\\ f(8) & ={8}^{1/3}=2 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{-2/3} \\\\ {f}^{′}(8) & =\\frac{1}{3}(8)^{-2/3}=\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Taylor series is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{1/3} & =2+\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 4}(x-8)+⋯ \\\\  & =2+\\frac{x-8}{12}+⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute $x=7$ into the above to approximate ${7}^{1/3}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{7}^{1/3} & ≈2+\\frac{7-8}{12} \\\\  & =2-\\frac{1}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{23}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401833 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401834 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401833 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401835 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401833 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401836 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401833 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401837 1319413953347