the function $x(t).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401900 1072 #uuid "6706b3e3-ba1f-5e48-a0c6-87c0de600ccd" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401900 1074 "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the side ${S}_{3}.$\n\nFor the side ${S}_{3},$ we have $1\\ge u\\ge 0$ and $v=1.$ Substituting $v=1$ into our transformation equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(v(2-u),\\,u{v}^{3}) \\\\  & =(1(2-u),\\,u(1)^{3}) \\\\  & =(2-u,u).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the image of ${S}_{3}$ can be parametrized by\n\n$$\nx=2-u,\\,y=u,\\,1\\ge u\\ge 0.\n$$\n\n \n\nWriting this in the usual notation, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=2-t,\\,y(t)=t,\\,1\\ge t\\ge 0.\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401901 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401902 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401901 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401903 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401901 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401904 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401901 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401905 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401901 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401906 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401901 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401901 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401901 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401903 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401901 1080 #uuid "618ade45-7715-5c2b-8e23-5edac27f8883" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401902 1081 "2t" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401902 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401902 1084 #uuid "793fda82-4b8f-5357-8355-7eb714c2f363" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401903 1081 "2-t" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401903 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401903 1084 #uuid "b6a3c59d-ed02-5238-a8c6-fd2024482e82" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401904 1081 "t" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401904 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401904 1084 #uuid "f6cd580d-4800-5b0c-92e0-e1600068f58e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401905 1081 "2+t" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401905 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401905 1084 #uuid "b627bbcd-b10a-5d39-a559-125ce37018ed" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401906 1081 "0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401906 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401906 1084 #uuid "ee753101-7bb5-5dbb-a4a6-c54e0820154f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401907 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401908 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401907 1069 "q-225228" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401907 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401907 1071 "![](images/33/33e48fa5bdbb034bcf489e038ccf80fc5f67baabeccacc1b7abd741183ebf05d.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{v-1}{u+1},\\,y=(u+v-1)^{2}+1.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the side ${S}_{4}$ under the action of $T?$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401907 1072 #uuid "5bd99021-9f7b-5102-9e9a-342e79f39167" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401907 1074 "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the side ${S}_{4}.$\n\nFor the side ${S}_{4},$ we have $u=0$ and $1\\ge v\\ge 0.$ Substituting $u=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(\\frac{v-1}{u+1},\\,(u+v-1)^{2}+1) \\\\  & =(\\frac{v-1}{0+1},\\,(0+v-1)^{2}+1) \\\\  & =(v-1,\\,(v-1)^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the image of ${S}_{4}$ can be parametrized by\n\n$$\nx=v-1,\\,y=(v-1)^{2}+1,\\,1\\ge v\\ge 0.\n$$\n\n \n\nWriting this in the usual notation, we have\n\n$$\nx=t-1,\\,y=(t-1)^{2}+1,\\,1\\ge t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nThese are parametric equations of a parabolic arc. Notice that if we eliminate $t$ from the equations, we get\n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}+1\n$$\n\nwhich is an upward-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,1).$\n\nMoreover, the endpoints of ${S}_{4}$ are mapped to the $xy$-plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T:(0,1)\\to (\\frac{1-1}{0+1},(0+1-1)^{2}+1)=(0,1) \\\\  & T:(0,0)\\to (\\frac{0-1}{0+1},(0+0-1)^{2}+1)=(-1,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image of ${S}_{4}$ is an arc of a upward-opening parabola, traversed from $(0,1)$ to $(-1,2).$\n\n![](images/69/69a2a8ab136360c01d1a17a58dc2fc4864ae2089330a551df913b200d923f087.png)" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401908 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401909 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401908 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401910 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401908 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401911 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401908 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401912 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401908 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401913 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401908 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401908 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401908 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401911 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401908 1080 #uuid "47132c57-ee0e-5ec3-b95e-67a15913786d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401909 1081 "An arc of a right-opening parabola, traversed from   $(1,1)$ to $(0,2).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401909 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401909 1084 #uuid "4d42c473-b845-56f6-91ed-2f7569cdadf9" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401910 1081 "An arc of a upward-opening parabola, traversed from $(0,2)$ to $(1,1).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401910 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401910 1084 #uuid "6dd13488-86ae-53ef-94b1-8445c40feae7" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401911 1081 "An arc of an upward-opening parabola, traversed from $(0,1)$ to $(-1,2).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401911 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401911 1084 #uuid "2eaf5793-614c-59c2-8266-69fcc04e0964" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401912 1081 "An arc of a right-opening parabola, traversed from $(0,1)$ to $(-1,2).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401912 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401912 1084 #uuid "1cea9769-6304-556d-88e7-17fabaf6e8d9" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401913 1081 "An arc of an upward-opening parabola, traversed from $(-1,2)$ to $(0,1).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401913 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401913 1084 #uuid "132e7131-949c-5374-87b4-fafc2b9fee75" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401914 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401915 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401914 1069 "q-26223" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401914 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401914 1071 "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0.3x-0.1y=0.6 \\\\ 0.6x+0.8y=0.2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401914 1072 #uuid "3d7c59ff-df86-5863-a05a-c20fb84b2ead" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401914 1074 "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply both equations by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0.3x-0.1y=0.6 & |\\,\\times 10 \\\\ 0.6x+0.8y=0.2 & |\\,\\times 10\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}3x-y=6 \\\\ 6x+8y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that if we divide the second equation by $(-2),$ we will get a $-3x$ term in the second equation that can cancel with the $3x$ term in the first equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x-y=6 &  \\\\ 6x+8y=2 & |\\,÷(-2)\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}3x-y=6 \\\\ -3x-4y=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $x$-variable and allows us to solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{3x}-y & =6 \\\\ -\\cancel{3x}-4y & =-1 \\\\ (-y-4y) & =(6-1) \\\\ -5y & =5 \\\\ y & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $y=-1$ into the equation $3x-y=6$ to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-y & =6 \\\\ 3x-(-1) & =6 \\\\ 3x & =5 \\\\ x & =\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $x=\\frac{5}{3}$ and $y=-1.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401915 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401916 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401915 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401917 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401915 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401918 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401915 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401919 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401915 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401920 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401915 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401915 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401915 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401920 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401915 1080 #uuid "e422abe5-7836-5aa6-bfb2-34896476a4d7" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401916 1081 "$x=\\frac{4}{3},$ $y=-2$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401916 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401916 1084 #uuid "c29c57bf-e265-52a1-bca7-e9f5dad2f3f4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401917 1081 "$x=1,$ $y=-3$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401917 1083 #ed