[17592186401934 1069 "q-29384" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401934 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401934 1071 "![](images/a7/a740aafbb9f74e2681506d3027f848fa92e7eea2bac3e08ccaf3fc7e0acf8fa1.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown in the graph above?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401934 1072 #uuid "5cb8229e-2a6a-582b-a6c3-627b88cf6816" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401934 1074 "Consider the line $y=x+2.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>x+2.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=-x+1.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge -x+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y>x+2 \\\\ y\\ge -x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401935 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401936 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401935 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401937 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401935 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401938 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401935 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401939 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401935 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401940 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401935 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401935 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401935 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401938 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401935 1080 #uuid "210acf01-110f-53da-bf3c-8725abe1a7d8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401936 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le x+2 \\\\ y>-x+1\\end{aligned}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401936 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401936 1084 #uuid "c28cb971-d849-577e-9682-a8890d4ae773" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401937 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge x+2 \\\\ y\\ge -x+1\\end{aligned}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401937 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401937 1084 #uuid "d4c91422-9ef9-5a21-a3cd-6168971db223" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401938 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y>x+2 \\\\ y\\ge -x+1\\end{aligned}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401938 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401938 1084 #uuid "928ea34b-f94c-5914-8894-15d7edbe4d92" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401939 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge x+2 \\\\ y<-x+1\\end{aligned}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401939 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401939 1084 #uuid "129beb51-d7c5-5a45-86b1-53f54c6e7926" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401940 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le x+2 \\\\ y<-x+1\\end{aligned}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401940 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401940 1084 #uuid "1f5ea53c-6d9f-56de-99b0-c8f54f45ac23" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401941 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401942 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401941 1069 "q-2939" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401941 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401941 1071 "![](images/92/9283bcc77ac8e63c1ba00f9a81e659bcbcf41bc98b94a1a0617b02feab71cf0a.png)\n\nCar $B$ is being driven due south toward Caltech at a speed of $60\\,\\text{km/h},$ while car $A$ is being driven due east away from Caltech. When car $B$ is $0.6\\,\\text{km}$ away from Caltech, car $A$ is $0.8\\,\\text{km}$ from Caltech. If the distance between the two vehicles is increasing at a rate of $20\\,\\text{km/h},$ what is the speed of car $A?$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401941 1072 #uuid "507fbe2b-2f95-5bfa-be32-3403810daadf" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401941 1074 "![](images/6e/6e7ef0d4665710a31c1c601048498f20ad6b3099769c1d140320074805964ec7.png)\n\nIn the diagram,\n\n- $x$ is the distance between Caltech and car $A$,\n\n- $y$ is the distance between Caltech and car $B$,\n\n- $z$ is the distance between the two cars.\n\nAs shown in the diagram, $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ form a right triangle with $z$ as the hypotenuse. We wish to find the rate of change of $x,$ which is $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}.$ \n\nWe know that $x=0.8\\,\\text{km}$ and $y=0.6\\,\\text{km}.$ We can find $z$ using the Pythagorean Theorem, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ {0.8}^{2}+{0.6}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ {z}^{2} & =1 \\\\ z & =1\\,\\text{km}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that:\n\n- $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=-60\\,\\text{km}/\\text{h},$\n\n- $\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}=20\\,\\text{km}/\\text{h}.$\n\nFinally, we differentiate both sides of ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={z}^{2}$ with respect to $t$ and then substitute in the known values, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({z}^{2}) \\\\ 2x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =2z\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ 2(0.8)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+2(0.6)(-60) & =2(1)(20) \\\\ 1.6\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =40+72 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{112}{1.6} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =70.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed of the car $A$ is $70\\,\\text{km}/\\text{h}.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401942 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401943 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186401942 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401944 13194139533478 17592186045585 tr