533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402132 1074 "Recall Newton's second law, which states that the resultant force $F$ acting on a body equals the product of its mass $m$ and acceleration $a:$\n\n$$\nF=ma\n$$\n\nIn our case, two forces are acting on the rock:\n\n- The force due to gravity, given by the weight $w$ of the rock, which equals\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w & =mg \\\\  & =2g.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The force due to drag (air resistance) $D,$ which is proportional to the square of the velocity of the rock (and negative since it acts in the negative direction):\n\n$$\nD=-k{v}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality. Note that, since drag, in $\\text{N}=\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m/s}}^{2},$ is the product of the constant $k$ and squared velocity, in $(\\text{m/s})^{2}={\\text{m}}^{2}/{\\text{s}}^{2},$ the units of $k$ are\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{N}}{{\\text{m}}^{2}/{\\text{s}}^{2}}=\\frac{\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m/s}}^{2}}{{\\text{m}}^{2}/{\\text{s}}^{2}}=\\text{kg/m}.\n$$\n\nSumming the forces, the resultant force acting on the rock is\n\n$$\nF=w+D=2g-k{v}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAlso, recall that acceleration is the derivative of velocity: $a=\\frac{dv}{dt}.$\nSubstituting this into Newton's second law, along with our expression for the resultant force on the rock, we get\n\n$$\n2g-k{v}^{2}=2\\,\\frac{dv}{dt}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{dv}{dt}=g-\\frac{k}{2}{v}^{2}.\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402133 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402134 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402133 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402135 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402133 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402136 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402133 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402137 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402133 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402138 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402133 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402133 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402133 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402137 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402133 1080 #uuid "8915c372-42a6-5420-8c91-5f069925b152" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402134 1081 "\\frac{dv}{dt}=2g-kv" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402134 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402134 1084 #uuid "32063b22-d699-5f63-a71d-869c73971f55" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402135 1081 "\\frac{dv}{dt}=2g" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402135 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402135 1084 #uuid "0fc50789-5421-50d2-b60e-67a3bd2e10f6" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402136 1081 "\\frac{dv}{dt}=2g-k{v}^{2}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402136 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402136 1084 #uuid "491ac020-a720-59c1-ba10-c392f69847b9" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402137 1081 "\\frac{dv}{dt}=g-\\frac{k}{2}{v}^{2}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402137 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402137 1084 #uuid "4948e46f-d047-5768-bf2d-e94a4743506f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402138 1081 "\\frac{dv}{dt}=g-\\frac{k}{2}v" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402138 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402138 1084 #uuid "d34ed5ad-0c4e-5b97-a8e7-e19f41dfe4f5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402139 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402140 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402139 1069 "q-335542" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402139 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402139 1071 "A wildlife reserve can support a total of $800$ deer.\nAt the beginning of a disease study in the reserve, a parasitic infection has affected $80$ deer. After $10$ days, the number of deer affected by the parasite increases to $300.$ To the nearest day, how long does it take for the infected deer population to reach $600$ animals?\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the number of deer affected by the parasite, $P(t),$ increases at a rate that obeys an inhibited growth model, where $t\\ge 0$ is the time, in days.*" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402139 1072 #uuid "a4fd0915-73cc-575a-b3cc-4a156a96dd49" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402139 1074 "The rate at which the deer population affected by the parasite, $P(t),$ changes is proportional to the difference between the total deer population and its current population affected. Therefore, we have the inhibited growth equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=k(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the total deer population in the reserve, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, $a=800$ deer, and we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=k(800-P).\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate our differential equation by separating the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dP}{800-P} & =k\\,dt \\\\ \\int \\frac{dP}{800-P} & =\\int k\\,dt \\\\ -\\operatorname{ln}⁡|800-P| & =kt+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this is the solution to an inhibited growth equation, we have $800-P>0$ for all $t\\ge 0.$\nNext, we solve for $P(t),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}800-P & ={e}^{-kt-C} \\\\ 800-P & ={e}^{-C}{e}^{-kt} \\\\ 800-P & =K{e}^{-kt} \\\\ P & =800-K{e}^{-kt}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $K={e}^{-C}$ is a constant of integration. \n\nWe're told that the initial deer population affected by the parasite was $80$ animals. So, we apply the initial condition $P(0)=80,$ and solve for $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0) & =80 \\\\ 800-K{e}^{0} & =80 \\\\ 800-K & =80 \\\\ K & =720\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following expression for $P(t):$\n\n$$\nP(t)=800-720{e}^{-kt}\n$$\n\nWe're also told that, after $10$ days, the deer population affected by the parasite was $300$ animals. So, applying the condition $P(10)=300,$ we can solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(10) & =300 \\\\ 800-720{e}^{-10k} & =300 \\\\ 500 & =720{e}^{-10k} \\\\ {e}^{-10k} & =\\frac{500}{720}=\\frac{25}{36} \\\\ -10k & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{25}{36}) \\\\ k & =-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{25}{36})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let ${t}_{1}$ be the time when $600$ deer are affected by the parasite. Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({t}_{1}) & =600 \\\\ 800-720{e}^{-k{t}_{1}} & =600 \\\\ 200 & =720{e}^{-k{t}_{1}} \\\\ {e}^{-k{t}_{1}} & =\\frac{200}{720}=\\frac{5}{18} \\\\ -k{t}_{1} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{5}{18}) \\\\ {t}_{1} & =-\\frac{1}{k}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{5}{18}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting in our value for $k,$ we conclude that $600$ deer will be affected by the parasite after\n\n$$\n{t}_{1}=\\frac{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{5}{18})}{-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{25}{36})}=35.128…≈35\\,\\text{days},\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest day." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402140 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402141 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402140 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402142 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402140 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402143 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402140 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402144 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402140 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402145 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402140 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402140 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402140 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402141 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402140 1080 #uuid "63531a29-5d3e-5f5f-97ce-ef01b7d03202" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402141 1081 "$35$ days" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402141 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402141 1084 #uuid "088dc229-13bb-525f-97f0-615a3387e9fc" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402142 1081 "$50$ days" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402142 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402142 1084 #uuid "dbe81525-8780-55b2-9e79-394a40fd9a7e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402143 1081 "$40$ days" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402143 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402143 1084 #uuid "0d9dd8e3-5764-58b2-9ff2-4b88c32898f8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402144 1081 "$20$ days" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402144 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402144 1084 #uuid "ac5c6a61-12a4-5352-8fcc-e3319bbc18bd" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402145 1081 "$28$ days" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402145 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402145 1084 #uuid "dbb667f2-6fca-5729-a7fd-9dfe18862602" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402146 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402147 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402146 1069 "q-335590" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402146 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402146 1071 "A small bakery produces loaves of bread. The owner knows that the bakery can produce a maximum of $600$ loaves a day; however, current production is below this maximum. Since she started monitoring, the bakers produced $480$ loaves and $500$ loaves on days $4$ and $8,$ respectively. How many loaves do they produce on day $40?$ Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the bread production $E(t)$ increases at a rate that obeys an inhibited growth model, where $t$ is the time, in days.*" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402146 1072 #uuid "ee0a87d3-d3e9-539a-9074-68a374d85d6b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402146 1074 "The rate at which the bread production $E(t)$ changes is proportional to the difference between the maximum possible bread production and its current bread production. Therefore, we have the inhibited growth equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dE}{dt}=k(a-E),\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the maximum production of the bakery, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, $a=600$ loaves, and we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{dE}{dt}=k(600-E).\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate our differential equation by separating the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dE}{600-E} & =k\\,dt \\\\ \\int \\frac{dE}{600-E} & =\\int k\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ -\\operatorname{ln}⁡|600-E| & =kt+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this is the solution to an inhibited growth equation, we have $600-E>0$ for all $t\\ge 0.$ Next, we solve for $E(t),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}600-E & ={e}^{-kt-C} \\\\ 600-E & ={e}^{-C}{e}^{-kt} \\\\ 600-E & =K{e}^{-kt} \\\\ E & =600-K{e}^{-kt}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $K={e}^{-C}$ is a constant of integration.\n\nWe're told that, on day $4,$ the bread production was $480$ loaves. So, applying the condition $E(4)=480,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E(4) & =480 \\\\ 600-K{e}^{-4k} & =480 \\\\ K{e}^{-4k} & =120.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're also told that, on day $8,$ the bread production was $500$ loaves. So, applying the condition $E(8)=500,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E(8) & =500 \\\\ 600-K{e}^{-8k} & =500 \\\\ K{e}^{-8k} & =100.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, by dividing the result of the first condition by the result of the second, we can solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{K{e}^{-4k}}{K{e}^{-8k}} & =\\frac{120}{100} \\\\ {e}^{4k} & =\\frac{6}{5} \\\\ 4k & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{6}{5}) \\\\ k & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{6}{5})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting back into the result of the first condition, we solve for $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}K{e}^{-4\\cdot (1/4)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6/5)} & =120 \\\\ K & =120{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6/5)} \\\\ K & =144\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following expression for $E(t):$\n\n$$\nE(t)=600-144{e}^{-(t/4)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6/5)}\n$$\n\nFinally, the number of loaves baked on day $t=40$ is\n\n$$\nE(40)=600-144{e}^{-(40/4)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6/5)}≈576.743…≈577\\,\\text{loaves},\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402147 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402148 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402147 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402149 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402147 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402150 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402147 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402151 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402147 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402152 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402147 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402147 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402147 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402150 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402147 1080 #uuid "6e99660a-207e-56cc-af0c-7810e8c04e78" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402148 1081 "$570$ loaves" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402148 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402148 1084 #uuid "a62be6e9-5300-5837-bb21-616f9afabd11" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402149 1081 "$560$ loaves" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402149 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402149 1084 #uuid "52f73195-6ad4-5063-9185-1d0ce506d0fb" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402150 1081 "$577$ loaves" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402150 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402150 1084 #uuid "487b0c65-385a-5896-a74a-7185c8309375" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402151 1081 "$550$ loaves" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402151 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402151 1084 #uuid "cfb7ad78-9e83-5378-a008-fb209e8c0c15" 13194139533478 17592186045585