lection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402214 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402219 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402214 1080 #uuid "acf1e061-7a98-5801-95c8-22217b716f6a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402215 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402215 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402215 1084 #uuid "7fd99f64-1a0e-5d84-8e13-95caae8d936d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402216 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402216 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402216 1084 #uuid "8b10290b-80cb-5b29-9f79-1f195229c212" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402217 1081 "I only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402217 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402217 1084 #uuid "05e09efb-9144-55ca-b467-bbf73a07f532" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402218 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402218 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402218 1084 #uuid "49d1e9f7-e09c-5fb0-9b7e-39e20b2c166e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402219 1081 "II only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402219 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402219 1084 #uuid "9983cf80-2f24-55d7-be17-9eb6b4c84e81" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402220 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402221 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402220 1069 "q-338623" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402220 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402220 1071 "Consider the following boundary value problem.\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)-{y}^{′}(x)+y(x)={x}^{2},\\,y(1)=0,\\,3y(3)+{y}^{′}(3)=6,\\,1\\le x\\le 3\n$$\n\nWhich of the following best classifies the boundary conditions for this problem?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402220 1072 #uuid "dc494029-58f4-51d4-95fe-9c9b2384d2b2" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402220 1074 "For a second-order boundary value problem, \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+P(x){y}^{′}(x)+Q(x)y(x)=f(x),\\,a\\le x\\le b\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x),Q(x)$ and $f(x)$ are all continuous on $[a,b],$ we have the following boundary condition classifications. \n\n- Dirichlet:\n\n$$\ny(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,y(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Neumann:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Robin (mixed):\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}y(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{\\alpha }_{2}y(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Periodic:\n\n$$\ny(a)=y(b),\\,{y}^{′}(a)={y}^{′}(b)\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\gamma }_{i},{\\alpha }_{i},$ and ${\\beta }_{i}$ are real numbers with $({\\alpha }_{i},{\\beta }_{i})\\ne (0,0).$ \n\nIn our case, we have the following boundary conditions, defined on $x=a=1$ and $x=b=3.$\n\n$$\ny(1)=0,\\,3y(3)+{y}^{′}(3)=6\n$$\n\nThese are Robin (mixed) boundary conditions." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402221 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402222 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402221 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402223 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402221 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402224 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402221 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402225 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402221 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402226 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402221 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402221 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402221 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402223 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402221 1080 #uuid "dd10be9b-3b17-5633-861a-6fa42ef0e0d8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402222 1081 "Other" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402222 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402222 1084 #uuid "51963deb-494b-5038-a567-d52bbae853d7" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402223 1081 "Robin" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402223 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402223 1084 #uuid "ca70af21-75b9-54e1-a733-f7fe2f7fa12e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402224 1081 "Neumann" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402224 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402224 1084 #uuid "320aef74-4e39-5907-aac3-4ae1dafcfabd" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402225 1081 "Periodic" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402225 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402225 1084 #uuid "99d38800-e0a0-56b4-b188-2bf47e62f659" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402226 1081 "Dirichlet" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402226 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402226 1084 #uuid "b97382cb-a37a-52dd-8bc5-72cf2224232a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402227 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402228 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402227 1069 "q-339222" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402227 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402227 1071 "The number of subscribers $N(t)$ to an e-learning platform varies according to the differential equation ${N}^{′}(t)=rN(t),$ where $t$ is the time since the platform was launched, measured in weeks, and $r>0.$ It is known that the number of subscribers doubles after the first four weeks. How long does it take for the number of subscribers to triple after the platform is launched? Round your answer to one decimal place." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402227 1072 #uuid "b562af2b-8343-5000-806c-d01887adea11" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402227 1074 "The general solution to the given differential equation is\n\n$$\nN(t)={N}_{0}{e}^{rt},\n$$\n\nwhere ${N}_{0}$ is the number of subscribers when $t=0.$\n\nLet ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the number of subscribers equals $3{N}_{0}.$ Then, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N({t}_{1}) & =3{N}_{0}\\,⇒\\,{N}_{0}{e}^{r{t}_{1}}=3{N}_{0}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation for ${t}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{N}_{0}{e}^{r{t}_{1}} & =3{N}_{0} \\\\ \\cancel{{N}_{0}}{e}^{r{t}_{1}} & =3\\cancel{{N}_{0}} \\\\ {e}^{r{t}_{1}} & =3 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{r{t}_{1}}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3) \\\\ r{t}_{1} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\ {t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{r}\\,\\,(∗)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now need to calculate $r.$ We're told that the number of subscribers doubles after the first four weeks the platform is launched. Therefore,\n\n$$\nN(4)=2{N}_{0}\\,⇒\\,{N}_{0}{e}^{4r}=2{N}_{0}.\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation for $r,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{N}_{0}{e}^{4r} & =2{N}_{0} \\\\ \\cancel{{N}_{0}}{e}^{4r} & =2\\cancel{{N}_{0}} \\\\ {e}^{4r} & =2 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{4r}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ r & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this into $(∗)$ and evaluating, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{r} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & ≈6.3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402228 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402229 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402228 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402230 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402228 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402231 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402228 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402232 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402228 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402233 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402228 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402228 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402228 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402229 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402228 1080 #uuid "b4ae4df5-40ba-5454-aa69-0f62becda821" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402229 1081 "$6.3$ weeks" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402229 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402229 1084 #uuid "386007b3-91ce-5982-8534-d31233322fdb" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402230 1081 "$6$ weeks" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402230 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402230 1084 #uuid "0a01f341-43f3-528c-b811-0f8051a23c3c" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402231 1081 "$6.4$ weeks" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402231 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402231 1084 #uuid "8ac92552-dc2b-5d29-986a-281a4e64330d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402232 1081 "$6.5$ weeks" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402232 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402232 1084 #uuid "c1738319-0cbe-5aa8-beb9-61d8c99fe62b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402233 1081 "$6.2$ weeks" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402233 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402233 1084 #uuid "aa2f0725-683a-50fc-855c-66c7d9ba756f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402234 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402235 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402234 1069 "q-339226" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402234 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402234 1071 "The value $V(t)$ of a tech device varies according to the differential equation ${V}^{′}(t)=-rV(t),$ where $t$ is the time, measured in years, and $r>0.$ It is known that the value reduces by one-half after the first year. How long does it take for the value to reduce to one-fifth of its original value? Round your answer to one decimal place." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402234 1072 #uuid "8375c335-8cf2-5c82-b2c9-770890e7d65a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402234 1074 "The general solution to the given differential equation is\n\n$$\nV(t)={V}_{0}{e}^{-rt},\n$$\n\nwhere ${V}_{0}$ is the value when $t=0.$\n\nLet ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the value equals $\\frac{1}{5}{V}_{0}.$ Then, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V({t}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{5}{V}_{0}\\,⇒\\,{V}_{0}{e}^{-r{t}_{1}}=\\frac{1}{5}{V}_{0}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation for ${t}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}_{0}{e}^{-r{t}_{1}} & =\\frac{1}{5}{V}_{0} \\\\ \\cancel{{V}_{0}}{e}^{-r{t}_{1}} & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cancel{{V}_{0}} \\\\ {e}^{-r{t}_{1}} & =\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-r{t}_{1}}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\ -r{t}_{1} & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 \\\\ {t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{r}\\,\\,(∗)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now need to calculate $r.$ We're told that the value reduces by one-half after the first year. Therefore,\n\n$$\nV(1)=\\frac{1}{2}{V}_{0}\\,⇒\\,{V}_{0}{e}^{-r}=\\frac{1}{2}{V}_{0}.\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation for $r,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}_{0}{e}^{-r} & =\\frac{1}{2}{V}_{0} \\\\ \\cancel{{V}_{0}}{e}^{-r} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cancel{{V}_{0}} \\\\ {e}^{-r} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-r}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ -r & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ r & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this into $(∗)$ and evaluating, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{r} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & ≈2.3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402235 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402236 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402235 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402237 131941395334