2186045585 true] [17592186402241 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402241 1071 "The rate of increase ${E}^{′}(t)$ of the average monthly cost of electricity in a particular region varies according to the differential equation ${E}^{′}(t)=0.02E(t),$ where $t$ is the time, in years, since the year $2017.$ In $2021,$ the average monthly cost was $$124.50.$ What was the average monthly cost of electricity in $2017?$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402241 1072 #uuid "d1d42a16-3984-5dae-bf8b-539545f414f5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402241 1074 "The general solution to the given differential equation is\n\n$$\nE(t)={E}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.02t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${E}_{0}$ is the average monthly cost of electricity in $2017.$\n\nWe are given that the monthly residential electricity cost was $$124.50$ in $2021,$ so after $t=4$ years. Hence, substituting $t=4$ and $E(4)=124.50$ into our general solution and solving for ${E}_{0},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E(4) & ={E}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.02\\cdot 4} \\\\ 124.50 & ={E}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.08} \\\\ {E}_{0} & =\\frac{124.50}{{e}^{0.08}} \\\\  & ≈114.93\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest cent.\n\nTherefore, the average monthly cost in $2017$ was $$114.93.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402242 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402243 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402242 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402244 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402242 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402245 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402242 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402246 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402242 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402247 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402242 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402242 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402242 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402247 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402242 1080 #uuid "b6cbfe2e-3815-5b36-b83f-63a2f