ial equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at the *same* location in the domain of $y,$ then this is an **initial value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is an initial value problem. The differential equation is together with two conditions at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=4$).\n\n- The second system is not an initial value problem. It contains an equation only. No conditions are specified.\n\n- The third system is an initial value problem. The differential equation is together with two conditions at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=2$)." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402249 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402250 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402249 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402251 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402249 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402252 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402249 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402253 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402249 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402254 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402249 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402249 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402249 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402251 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402249 1080 #uuid "de781819-e735-5446-8359-21f70d676ce4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402250 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402250 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402250 1084 #uuid "aababf37-9c33-5d0f-9433-1d0cf555f97b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402251 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402251 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402251 1084 #uuid "3fa28dc5-5323-59c1-89c5-ec291f51cc7d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402252 1081 "III only" 131941395334