8 17592186045585 true] [17592186402694 1071 "Determine the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{x}{(x+3)(x+1)(x-1)}.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402694 1072 #uuid "ca4d349e-c1ee-5a19-a1e0-b0c9e7e02dd8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402694 1074 "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3)(x+1)(x-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the three solutions $x=-3,$ $x=-1$ and $x=1.$ Therefore, the equations of the vertical asymptotes are  $x=-3,\\,$ $x=-1$ and $x=1.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402695 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402696 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402695 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402697 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402695 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402698 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402695 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402699 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402695 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402700 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402695 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402695 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402695 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402698 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402695 1080 #uuid "aba4d313-1d11-58c4-bb5b-3d3a12220a0e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402696 1081 "x=-1,\\,x=1,\\,x=3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402696 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402696 1084 #uuid "ce1c8713-2cf3-5d3e-be72-a3135dfaed78" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402697 1081 "x=-3,\\,x=1,\\,x=3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402697 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592