4-⋯$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402722 1072 #uuid "5d6af0ce-2d7e-5e7e-9759-710fbc03ce1c" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402722 1074 "Let's look at each series in turn.\n\n- For the geometric series $4+3+\\frac{9}{4}+\\frac{27}{16}+⋯$  the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is convergent because $|r|<1.$\n\n- For the geometric series $16-2+\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{32}+⋯$ the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} & =\\frac{-2}{16} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is convergent because $|r|<1.$\n\n- For the geometric series $-8+16-32+64-⋯$  the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} & =\\frac{16}{-8} \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is divergent because $|r|\\ge 1.$\n\nIn conclusion, only series I and II converge." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402723 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402724 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402723 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402725 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402723 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402726 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402723 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402727 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402723 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402728 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402723 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402723 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402723 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402727 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402723 1080 #uuid "6140ca09-668b-5dd3-b823-6e3fa39bae3f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402724 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402724 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402724 1084 #uuid "58761f09-07f7-57a6-ab8e-19cc89659cdf" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402725