 | $16$ | $15$ | $20$ |\n\nFind the line of the form $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x$ that best fits the data above. According to the model, what will be the profit in the $6$th month, assuming the trend continues?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that*\n\n$$\n({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}11 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{X}^{T}y=[\\begin{aligned}78 \\\\ 250\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n*where $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector.*" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402749 1072 #uuid "e98728e8-7708-5748-ae2b-39ed7242bc51" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402749 1074 "The coefficients of the line that best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 16 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector.\n\nPre-multiplying this equation by ${X}^{T},$ we obtain the corresponding normal equation\n\n$$\n{X}^{T}\\,X\\overset{^}{\\beta }={X}^{T}y.\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $X$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${X}^{T}X$ is invertible and \n\n$$\n\\overset{^}{\\beta }=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values of $({X}^{T}X)^{-1}$ and ${X}^{T}y$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{\\beta } & =({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}\\,y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}11 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}78 \\\\ 250\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10.8 \\\\ 1.6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the line $y=10.8+1.6x.$ \n\nFinally, to predict the profit in the $6$th month, we substitute $x=6$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =10.8+1.6(6) \\\\  & =20.4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, according to the model, the profit in the $6$th month will be $$20\\,400.$\n\n**Note**: Since we're extrapolating ($x=6$ is not within the range of the original set of $x$-values), our result *may* be unreliable." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402750 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402751 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402750 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402752 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402750 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402753 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402750 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402754 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402750 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402755 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402750 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402750 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402750 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402753 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402750 1080 #uuid "dd4ac2e5-74a0-528f-8078-d6aa415b8f9a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402751 1081 "$$24\\,600$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402751 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402751 1084 #uuid "3ba73043-ba7f-5144-85cc-553d87d248c5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402752 1081 "$$37\\,300$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402752 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402752 1084 #uuid "1584ef53-01f2-5061-8e58-39b6ee6c83df" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402753 1081 "$$20\\,400$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402753 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402753 1084 #uuid "7cfaef46-165b-54fb-98ec-40334338b6c9" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402754 1081 "$$34\\,000$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402754 1083 #edb/ref 175921860