592186402922 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402922 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402923 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402922 1080 #uuid "a758672a-df89-5c21-bda2-9147f61578a2" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402923 1081 "$x=-3$ and $x=1$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402923 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402923 1084 #uuid "d1761688-95e3-5738-a863-ea6cd4b7c723" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402924 1081 "$x=1$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402924 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402924 1084 #uuid "9bf0bd1f-bbf9-5956-9fdb-4861ff24950e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402925 1081 "$x=0$ and $x=1$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402925 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402925 1084 #uuid "8361182a-8eda-5e46-8218-dd866302f4a4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402926 1081 "$x=-3$, $x=0$ and $x=1$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402926 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402926 1084 #uuid "e4f39b69-994d-5142-951e-f121dd4222ef" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402927 1081 "$x=-3$  only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402927 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402927 1084 #uuid "d4d4fd26-5931-574f-8d88-1d7ff410bd22" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402928 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402929 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402928 1069 "q-48120" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402928 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402928 1071 "Given the functions $\\,f(x),\\,g(x)\\,$ and $\\,h(x)\\,$ below, which of them has a point discontinuity at $x=1?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}-1 & x<1 \\\\ 0, & x=1 \\\\ 2(x-1), & x>1\\end{aligned} \\\\  \\\\ g(x) & ={\\begin{aligned}3x+2, & x<1 \\\\ 4, & x=1 \\\\ -3x+8, & x>1\\end{aligned} \\\\  \\\\ h(x) & ={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x-1}, & x\\le 1 \\\\ 1, & x>1\\end{aligned}\\text{ }\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402928 1072 #uuid "f08cee0d-f749-5e56-a39d-99fa204b19b2" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402928 1074 "Let's check each function, in turn:\n\nLet's check our continuity conditions for $f(x)$ at $x=1:$\n\n- $f(1)=0$ exists $✓$\n\n- The left and right-sided limits are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}f(x) & ={1}^{3}-1=0, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{+}}f(x) & =2(1-1)=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the left and right-sided limits are equal, we conclude\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)=0.\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)=f(1)$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=1.$\n\nNow, let's check our continuity conditions for $g(x)$ at $x=1:$\n\n- $g(1)=4$ exists $✓$\n\n- The left and right-sided limits are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}g(x) & =3(1)+2=5, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{+}}g(x) & =-3(1)+8=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the left and right-sided limits are equal, we conclude\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 1}g(x)=5.\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 1}g(x)\\ne g(1)$ $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the function $g(x)$ is not continuous at $x=1.$ It's the third condition that failed, which tells us that $x=1$ is a point discontinuity. \n\nFinally, let's check our continuity conditions for $h(x)$ at $x=1:$\n\n- $h(1)={e}^{(1-1)}=1$ exists $✓$\n\n- The left and right-sided limits are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}h(x) & ={e}^{(1-1)}=1, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{+}}h(x) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the left and right-sided limits are equal, we conclude\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 1}h(x)=1.\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 1}h(x)=h(1)$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\nSo, the function $h(x)$ is continuous at $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, only $g(x)$ has a point discontinuity at $x=1.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402929 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402930 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402929 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402931 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402929 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402932 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402929 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402933 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402929 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402934 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402929 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402929 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402929 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402933 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402929 1080 #uuid "7dd4af99-c768-578a-80d6-2d40aafbe957" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402930 1081 "$f(x)$ and $g(x)$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402930 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402930 1084 #uuid "793b5398-7a91-594d-bf3e-12774bb4d533" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402931 1081 "$f(x)$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402931 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402931 1084 #uuid "34d69758-08a3-5130-9d02-5a8a139d1d93" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402932 1081 "$g(x)$ and $h(x)$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402932 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402932 1084 #uuid "1de0e64a-faa1-5969-9784-4c9d1f067325" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402933 1081 "$g(x)$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402933 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402933 1084 #uuid "d85ecdec-99fd-5bc8-94bb-2c2db87123cc" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402934 1081 "$h(x)$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402934 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402934 1084 #uuid "da0e9431-8013-5bb5-a002-3fc5d3a10ddf" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402935 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402936 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402935 1069 "q-48144" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402935 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402935 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f(x)$ below?\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}3x-1, & x\\ne -1 \\\\ 4, & x=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nI. It has a removable discontinuity at $x=-1.$\nII. It has a jump discontinuity at $x=-1.$\nIII. It is continuous at $x=-1.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402935 1072 #uuid "022bd345-534b-5a28-b7c0-bb66d9319957" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402935 1074 "For $x=-1,$ let's go through our continuity checklist:\n\n- $f(-1)=4$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Let's now check the left and right limits. We see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}(3x-1)=3(-1)-1=-4, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{+}}(3x-1)=3(-1)-1=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the overall limit exists and ${lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x)=-4.\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Finally, we check that the value of the limit equals the value of the function: \n\n$$\nf(-1)=4\\ne {lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x).\n$$\n\nSo the value of the limit does not equal the value of the function.\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=-1.$\n\nHence, I is true, and II and III are false." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402936 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402937 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402936 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402938 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402936 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402939 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402936 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402940 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402936 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402941 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402936 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 1