t $x=-1.$\nII. It has a removable discontinuity at $x=-1.$\nIII. It is continuous at $x=-1.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402942 1072 #uuid "825ab862-b738-5389-82d3-382684f52334" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402942 1074 "The function has a jump discontinuity at $x=-1.$ Checking our conditions, we see that\n\n- $f(-1)=2$ exists, $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x)$ does not exist $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nSo the second condition failed. It failed because the left and right-sided limits are not equal:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}f(x)=1,\\,\\,{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{+}}f(x)=2.\n$$\n\nThese limits both exist and are finite, yet they are not equal. Therefore, the discontinuity at $x=-1$ is a jump discontinuity.\n\nConsequently, I is true, and II and III are false." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402943 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402944 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402943 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402945 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402943 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402946 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402943 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402947 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402943 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402948 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402943 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402943 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402943 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402945 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402943 1080 #uuid "39e1e51d-430b-5ea5-a049-7e9e7c4fca2e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402944 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402944 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402944 1084 #uuid "7fda113a-7bf7-5eb4-99a5-9b1cb83affd3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402945 1081 "I only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402945 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402945 1084 #uuid 