8 17592186045585 true] [17592186402955 1084 #uuid "7517b44c-4288-5afd-98bb-3306dfffce68" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402956 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402957 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402956 1069 "q-48254" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402956 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402956 1071 "![](images/a5/a50d4de74cb016b44546791985e5e1fdc519a9b5d2d4943ff24f6d492f4fa031.png)\n\nThe sides of a square decrease in length at a rate of $2\\text{ m/s}.$ At what rate is the area of the square decreasing when the sides are $10\\text{ m}$ long?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402956 1072 #uuid "60458af0-4d18-5219-97d4-dbd05ed7e66c" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402956 1074 "Let $x$ and $A$ be the length of the sides and the area of the square, respectively. We want to find\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\nThe area $A$ is related to side length $x$ by the formula\n\n$$\nA={x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating this relationship with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(A) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that each side of the square is decreasing at a rate of $2\\,\\text{m/s},$ so we have $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=-2.$ Also, when the sides are $10\\,\\text{m},$ we have $x=10.$ Substituting this information into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =(-2)\\cdot 2(10)=-40{\\text{ m}}^{2}\\text{/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the square decreases at $40\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}/\\text{s}.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402957 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402958 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402957 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402959 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402957 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402960 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402957 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402961 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402957 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402962 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402957 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402957 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402957 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402960 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402957 1080 #uuid "03aa2a75-a535-5715-a30a-bcc66a0ca916" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402958 1081 "30{\\text{ m}}^{2}\\text{/s}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402958 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402958 1084 #uuid "3d26e347-1ad3-5fde-8910-82d6d192a4c0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402959 1081 "15{\\text{ m}}^{2}\\text{/s}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402959 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402959 1084 #uuid "a6bfe9bb-0d95-596e-9565-5b0937d0dee0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402960 1081 "40{\\text{ m}}^{2}\\text{/s}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402960 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402960 1084 #uuid "e338773b-f299-5166-aa17-b7e7ad137b42" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402961 1081 "80{\\text{ m}}^{2}\\text{/s}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402961 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402961 1084 #uuid "e07cb7aa-0dfe-5028-8d59-44e5386e6298" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402962 1081 "20{\\text{ m}}^{2}\\text{/s}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402962 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402962 1084 #uuid "057ef675-78db-588f-94fd-4a1cdb060767" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402963 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402964 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402963 1069 "q-48404" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402963 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402963 1071 "The graph of the function $y=f(x)$ passes through $(3,-3)$ and is concave down on the interval $(1,4).$ If ${f}^{′}(3)=4,$ estimate the value of $f(3.2)$ using the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $x=3$ and determine whether the approximation is an underestimate or overestimate." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402963 1072 #uuid "23fa4cab-6951-5a21-810d-7733098a8e5c" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402963 1074 "The tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at the point $a=3$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =f(3)+{f}^{′}(3)(x-3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function passes through the point $(3,-3),$ so we have $f(3)=-3.$ Also, we're told that ${f}^{′}(3)=4,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =-3+4(x-3) \\\\  & =-3+4x-12 \\\\  & =4x-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(3.2)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=3.2.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3.2) & ≈L(3.2) \\\\  & =4(3.2)-15 \\\\  & =12.8-15 \\\\  & =-2.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the function is concave down on the interval $(1,4),$ the linear approximation $L(x)$ is above the graph near $x=3,$ and therefore we have an overestimate." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402964 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402965 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402964 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402966 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402964 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402967 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402964 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402968 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402964 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402969 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402964 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402964 1