(x)=(x-2)^{2}$\nIII. $h(x)=\\frac{1}{x-3}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402970 1072 #uuid "83188ea1-87cd-5ad1-b8c9-6226665589eb" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402970 1074 "For a function to satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[1,8],$ the function must be continuous on $[1,8]$ and differentiable on $(1,8).$\n\nLet's check each function individually.\n\n- The function $g(x)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}}$ is continuous on $[1,8]$ and has a cusp only at $x=0,$ which is outside $[1,8],$ hence it is differentiable on $(1,8).$ Therefore, $g(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $s(x)=(x-2)^{2}$ is continuous and differentiable on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ In particular, it  is continuous on $[1,8]$ and differentiable on $(1,8).$ Therefore, $s(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function  $h(x)=\\frac{1}{x-3}$ is not defined at $x=3$, so it is not continuous at $x=3$, which means it is not continuous on $[1,8].$ Therefore, $h(x)$ does not satisfiy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\nTherefore, only functions I and II satisfy the conditions for the mean value theorem over the interval $[1,8].$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402971 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402972 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402971 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402973 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402971 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402974 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402971 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402975 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402971 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402976 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402971 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402971 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402971 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402975 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402971 1080 #uuid "53957ce4-c21c-52c2-8684-73966d29c5a3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402972 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402972 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402972 1084 #uuid "b2ece29a-030c-52d6-afe3-255a447cbc90" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402973 1081 "I only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402973 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402973 1084 #uuid "d4a5b93f-384d-5634-966f-62af2bde686a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402974 1081 "III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402974 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402974 1084 #uuid "c76dfcf6-45e4-58d2-af91-12680d968b35" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402975 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402975 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402975 1084 #uuid "45893f39-bd67-57c7-bea5-5cfcb569788c" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402976 1081 "II only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402976 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402976 1084 #uuid "cbfe1530-2fbe-5ccf-bcac-82fef27ae14f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402977 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402978 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402977 1069 "q-48500" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402977 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402977 1071 "Which of the following functions satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[1,3]?$\n\nI. $g(x)={log}_{2}⁡x$\nII. $s(x)=\\frac{1}{x-2}$\nIII. $h(x)=x-2$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402977 1072 #uuid "0c14a931-93db-572b-92db-617c82f326c6" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402977 1074 "For a function to satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[1,3],$ the function must be continuous on $[1,3]$ and differentiable on $(1,3).$\n\nLet's check each function individually.\n\n- The function $g(x)={log}_{2}⁡x$ is continuous and differentiable on $(0,\\infty ).$ In particular, it  is continuous on $[1,3]$ and differentiable on $(1,3).$ Therefore, $g(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function  $s(x)=\\frac{1}{x-2}$ is not defined at $x=2$, so it is not continuous at $x=2$, which means it is not continuous on $[1,3].$ Therefore, $s(x)$ does not satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $h(x)=x-2$ is continuous and differentiable on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ In particular, it  is continuous on $[1,3]$ and differentiable on $(1,3).$ Therefore, $h(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\nTherefore, only functions I and III satisfy the conditions for the mean value theorem over the interval $[1,3].$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402978 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402979 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402978 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402980 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402978 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402981 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402978 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402982 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402978 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402983 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402978 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402978 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402978 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402980 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402978 1080 #uuid "ad377d0e-2547-5fdc-9116-be744f8e7641" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402979 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402979 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402979 1084 #uuid "ee9d9172-4e9b-532b-805c-8f145a6f6bd8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402980 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186402980 1083 