403056 1084 #uuid "b7ebc338-a51c-54a2-9008-89b303d45e94" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403057 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403058 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403057 1069 "q-54202" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403057 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403057 1071 "What is the center and radius of the circle with the equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=169?$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403057 1072 #uuid "13dc47a1-270d-56c2-8deb-b105337fbddb" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403057 1074 "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the origin is \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, the equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=169$ represents a circle that is centered at the origin, with radius\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{2} & =169 \\\\ r & =\\sqrt{169} \\\\ r & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we disregarded the negative solution for the radius since the radius of a circle must be positive.\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(0,0)$ and its radius is $13.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403058 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403059 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403058 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403060 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403058 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403061 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403058 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403062 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403058 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403063 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403058 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403058 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403058 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403063 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403058 1080 #uuid "aca4e605-47ce-5294-954a-2fe2d10aec36" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403059 1081 "The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius is $169$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403059 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403059 1084 #uuid "fcb5d640-6be6-55e0-9c19-beb9cef25ff6" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403060 1081 "The center is $(1,1)$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{13}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403060 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403060 1084 #uuid "50693ac5-91ac-507a-9bea-2faceed1fd57" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403061 1081 "The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius is $26$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403061 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403061 1084 #uuid "184b7f5f-0cc8-5cea-85cb-9c3c0e38ca1f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403062 1081 "The center is $(1,1)$ and the radius is $9$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403062 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403062 1084 #uuid "3b62671f-e9f6-5c77-a8c0-9cf013f52c90" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403063 1081 "The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius is $13$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403063 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403063 1084 #uuid "152e2df1-5743-5c39-8f54-57e7e1870f14" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403064 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403065 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403064 1069 "q-54242" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403064 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403064 1071 "Find the $x$-coordinates of the points where the circle $(x+1)^{2}+{y}^{2}=5$ intersects the line $y=-x+3.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403064 1072 #uuid "6de12d86-c297-540f-8fcc-949f18bd056f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403064 1074 "To find $x$-coordinates of the intersection points, we need to substitute $y=-x+3$ into the equation of the circle and solve the resulting equation for $x,$ if possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =5 \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+(-x+3)^{2} & =5 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2x+1+{x}^{2}-6x+9 & =5 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-4x+5 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we compute the discriminant $D$ of the above quadratic equation, then we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =(-4)^{2}-4\\cdot 2\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =16-40 \\\\  & =-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $D=-24<0$, there are no real solutions to the equation $2{x}^{2}-4x+5=0.$\n\nHence, we conclude that the circle $(x+1)^{2}+{y}^{2}=5$ does not intersect the line $y=-x+3$ at any point.\n\nThe corresponding diagram is shown below.\n\n![](images/85/85c9bea054f2e246d62864b022e53a6f1d23886b0f0c9f8c80c8e0a5b1be9cd8.png)" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403065 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403066 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403065 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403067 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403065 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403068 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403065 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403069 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403065 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403070 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403065 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403065 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403065 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403068 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403065 1080 #uuid "ea675cb1-71da-58ac-9964-d0086c97dbd9" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403066 1081 "$-3$ and $-1$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403066 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403066 1084 #uuid "da491dad-4f1d-55ca-bfae-d14b2a451b28" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403067 1081 "$1$ and $3$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403067 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403067 1084 #uuid "b6a92487-d3ea-562f-9904-5f62363a5252" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403068 1081 "The circle and the line do not intersect" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403068 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403068 1084 #uuid "521e3958-944c-5902-9f7b-658d7a27ed83" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403069 1081 "$-1$ and $4$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403069 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403069 1084 #uuid "5735b4a8-63cf-532a-a1bc-1c227aacb6c7" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403070 1081 "$-1$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403070 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403070 1084 #uuid "5e53871a-4f10-5856-a7d3-60a65cf5aa04" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403071 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403072 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403071 1069 "q-59711" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403071 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403071 1071 "![](images/40/40143c20622029d70a978310a7d38bc41d7b8411151d3d5f61a3b280e5807841.png)\n\nThe speed-time graph shown above represents the motion of an object. At what times is the object accelerating?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403071 1072 #uuid "cca94ba1-21b2-5b66-81e8-07381d34c86b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403071 1074 "The object is accelerating when its acceleration is positive. In a speed-time graph, the acceleration is given by the slope of the line. So, we need to find the times for which the slope is positive.\n\nWe see from the graph that the slope is positive from $t=0\\,\\text{s}$ to $t=30\\,\\text{s}.$ Therefore, the object is accelerating in this time interval." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403072 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403073 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403072 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403074 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403072 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403075 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403072 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403076 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403072 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403077 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403072 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403072 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403072 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403077 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403072 1080 #uuid "f193901b-aa88-5598-b883-d5711c39904d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403073 1081 "From $70\\,\\text{s}$ to $80\\,\\text{s}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403073 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403073 1084 #uuid "1719b7cb-bb0a-512e-b4d0-2db46619b09d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403074 1081 "From $30\\,\\text{s}$ to $80\\,\\text{s}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403074 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403074 1084 #uuid "538466f6-26ea-5ceb-93d4-bf50e00e92bf" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403075 1081 "From $30\\,\\text{s}$ to $70\\,\\text{s}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403075 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403075 1084 #uuid "0140ed8a-92fd-5826-aecd-2f790dfa3107" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403076 1081 "From $0\\,\\text{s}$ to $70\\,\\text{s}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403076 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403076 1084 #uuid "dfc348c6-96de-5702-89fd-0eab3b40e299" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403077 1081 "From $0\\,\\text{s}$ to $30\\,\\text{s}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403077 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403077 1084 #uuid "3b6efc88-a3cc-5c91-8eab-852285448c53" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403078 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403079 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403078 1069 "q-60145" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403078 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403078 1071 "The equation $-20{x}^{2}+60x-41=0$ can be written in the form $20(x+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $q,$ and solve the equation." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403078 1072 #uuid "a1ac9dcc-ee5b-5438-8680-0a3c7af8b759" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403078 1074 "First, we multiply the equation by $-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)\\cdot (-20{x}^{2}+60x-41) & =(-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\ 20{x}^{2}-60x+41 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we move the constant term to the right-hand side, factor the coefficient of the quadratic term, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20{x}^{2}-60x+41 & =0 \\\\ 20{x}^{2}-60x & =-41 \\\\ 20({x}^{2}-3x) & =-41 \\\\ 20[{x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}x+{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}] & =-41 \\\\ 20[{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{4}] & =-41\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we expand the brackets, and write the equation in the required form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-20\\cdot \\frac{9}{4} & =-41 \\\\ 20{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-45 & =-41 \\\\ 20{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =45-41 \\\\ 20{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $q=4.$ We now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =4 \\\\ {(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{4}{20} \\\\ {(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{5}} \\\\ |x-\\frac{3}{2}| & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{5}} \\\\ x-\\frac{3}{2} & =\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ x-\\frac{3}{2} & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5} \\\\ x & =\\frac{3}{2}\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403079 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403080 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403079 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403081 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403079 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403082 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403079 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403083 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403079 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403084 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403079 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403079 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403079 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403082 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403079 1080 #uuid "838eec31-f001-5f3e-95ff-aee58026f6f2" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403080 1081 "q=4,\\,x=2\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403080 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403080 1084 #uuid "5408298f-7273-5f8e-b08d-eb9052a72e9e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403081 1081 "q=4,\\,x=\\frac{3}{4}\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403081 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403081 1084 #uuid "55c297c3-ce19-541b-8f15-0e1cff269acc" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403082 1081 "q=4,\\,x=\\frac{3}{2}\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403082 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403082 1084 #uuid "18ad6631-816d-504b-86a5-d5fe74a70d5e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403083 1081 "q=2,\\,x=3\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403083 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403083 1084 #uuid "fcc7cd2a-4140-5747-8785-3c2be9dddaf8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403084 1081 "q=2,\\,x=\\frac{3}{2}\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403084 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403084 1084 #uuid "ef782508-1876-5861-8688-45bcea667f16" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403085 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403086 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403085 1069 "q-60356" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403085 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403085 1071 "The equation $-3{x}^{2}-2x+6=0$ can be written in the form $3(x+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $q-p.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403085 1072 #uuid "a7884f70-6bc5-5884-9b9e-474178b4363b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403085 1074 "First, we multiply the equation by $-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)\\cdot (-3{x}^{2}-2x+6) & =(-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}+2x-6 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we move the constant term to the right-hand side, factor the coefficient of the quadratic term, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+2x-6 & =0 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}+2x & =6 \\\\ 3[{x}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}x] & =6 \\\\ 3[{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}x+{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}] & =6 \\\\ 3[{(x+\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{9}] & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{(x+\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{9} & =6 \\\\ 3{(x+\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3} & =6 \\\\ 3{(x+\\frac{1}{3})}^{2} & =6+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 3{(x+\\frac{1}{3})}^{2} & =\\frac{19}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=\\frac{1}{3}$, $q=\\frac{19}{3}.$ Finally,\n\n$$\nq-p=\\frac{19}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{18}{3}=6.\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403086 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403087 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403086 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403088 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403086 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403089 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403086 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403090 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403086 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403091 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403086 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403086 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186