e get an angle that lies in the range $[{0}^{∘},{360}^{∘}).$\n\n- $-{210}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}={150}^{∘}\\,✓$\n\nSo the angle ${150}^{∘}$ is coterminal with $-{210}^{∘}.$ Let's draw this coterminal angle in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](images/78/788edaa48306f8370f9780cdeda956a85c34b76bd6ec5a028d9d38d425cbc5b9.png)\n\nWe see that ${150}^{∘}$ lies in quadrant II. Therefore, $-{210}^{∘}$ also lies in this quadrant." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403158 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403159 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403158 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403160 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403158 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403161 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403158 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403162 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403158 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403163 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403158 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403158 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403158 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403159 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403158 1080 #uuid "8d8f144d-6bde-515d-8710-0773c908d13d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403159 1081 "II" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403159 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403159 1084 #uuid "4e72d2ef-11e7-5363-bac5-671eb90f3369" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403160 1081 "III" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403160 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403160 1084 #uuid "ccaa6bd8-19ca-50f7-afe3-f13abc30ccd2" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403161 1081 "IV" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403161 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403161 1084 #uuid "2c6b6c4f-6ff5-5186-9c43-254f26013671" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403162 1081 "Between quadrants II and III" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403162 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403162 1084 #uuid "b616503f-5c11-5640-98b1-3558d18557b5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403163 1081 "I" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403163 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403163 1084 #uuid "f41f9c75-55f9-59f2-9b27-7b3d50783eb7" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403164 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403165 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403164 1069 "q-64701" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403164 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403164 1071 "Consider the equation ${y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}-15y=0$ where $y=y(t).$ If $y={e}^{\\lambda t}$ is a solution, then $\\lambda =$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403164 1072 #uuid "a341ef36-052b-58a5-8e5a-622fd4d5ea6a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403164 1074 "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda t}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda t},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda t}-2\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda t}-15{e}^{\\lambda t} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda t}({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda -15) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda -15 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda -5)=0,\n$$\n\nand so the solutions of the auxiliary equation  are $\\lambda =-3$ or $\\lambda =5.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403165 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403166 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403165 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403167 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403165 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403168 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403165 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403169 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403165 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403170 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403165 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403165 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403165 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403167 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403165 1080 #uuid "9aa513b8-ca41-5963-9d1c-ec92073b4073" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403166 1081 "$3$ or $-5$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403166 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403166 1084 #uuid "aa7b08f4-fd50-5010-9da5-db54d62d9cfb" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403167 1081 "$-3$ or $5$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403167 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403167 1084 #uuid "4baca1b8-62e7-5f52-af30-1fc3884ec93d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403168 1081 "$-3$ or $1$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403168 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403168 1084 #uuid "989a9e5a-82d4-559e-b64e-15fdf78c6beb" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403169 1081 "$3$ or $4$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403169 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403169 1084 #uuid "fdbdf5da-2897-576f-842c-af25e23e73b3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403170 1081 "$-6$ or $4$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403170 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403170 1084 #uuid "e4a7a515-e8e3-5996-959a-f3908110ac5b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403171 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403172 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403171 1069 "q-64953" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403171 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403171 1071 "Given that ${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{x}$ is a solution to the equation ${y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+y=0,$ use reduction of order to find a second solution ${y}_{2}(x)$ to the equation." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403171 1072 #uuid "f0b4e05c-493c-513f-8d82-76dddaa02634" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403171 1074 "According to the reduction of order method, we let ${y}_{2}=u(x){e}^{x}.$ \n\nDifferentiating the above with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′} & ={u}^{′}{e}^{x}+u{e}^{x}={e}^{x}({u}^{′}+u) \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″} & ={e}^{x}({u}^{″}+2{u}^{′}+u).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}({u}^{″}+2{u}^{′}+u)-2{e}^{x}({u}^{′}+u)+{e}^{x}(u) & =0 \\\\ {e}^{x}({u}^{″}+2{u}^{′}+u-2{u}^{′}-2u+u) & =0 \\\\ {e}^{x}{u}^{″} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${e}^{x}\\ne 0$ we must have\n\n$$\n{u}^{″}=0.\n$$\n\nLet $w={u}^{′}.$ Then our equation becomes\n\n$$\n{w}^{′}=0\\,⟹\\,w={c}_{1}.\n$$\n\nBut since $w={u}^{′},$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}={c}_{1}\\,⟹\\,u={c}_{1}x+{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our expression for ${y}_{2}(x)=u{e}^{x}$ becomes\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(x)={e}^{x}({c}_{1}x+{c}_{2}).\n$$\n\nFinally, setting ${c}_{1}=1$ and ${c}_{2}=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(x)={e}^{x}\\cdot x=x{e}^{x}.\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403172 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403173 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403172 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403174 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403172 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403175 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403172 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403176 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403172 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403177 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403172 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403172 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403172 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403175 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403172 1080 #uuid "ea86f69a-d990-5653-ae40-c11a11e9a