he function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at *different* locations in the domain of $y,$ then this is a **boundary value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is not a boundary value problem. The differential equation is combined with two conditions, but both conditions are given at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$). This is an **initial value problem.**\n\n- The second system is not a boundary value problem. It contains an equation only. No conditions are specified.\n\n- The third system is a boundary value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$ and $x=1$)." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403179 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403180 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403179 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403181 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403179 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403182 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403179 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403183 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403179 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403184 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403179 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403179 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403179 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403183 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403179 1080 #uuid "bee37669-e7fb-516e-95fe-1e5da2a5227f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403180 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403180 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403180 1084 #uuid "bb5fc021-9def-5f26-bdda-dd8981cd9477" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403181 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403181 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403181 1084 #uuid "d4805135-9684-5a00-9f95-f2b36b056956" 1319