139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403192 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403192 1071 "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Find the values of $a$ and $b$, if \n\n$$\n{f}_{x}(x,y)=a{y}^{2}x-3y,\\,{f}_{y}(x,y)=2{x}^{2}y+bx.\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403192 1072 #uuid "ee4afd99-ea98-5301-bd22-e1e65a00ab8b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403192 1074 "First, we find the mixed partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(a{y}^{2}x-3y) \\\\  & =2axy-3 \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}y+bx) \\\\  & =4xy+b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the function and its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. Hence, we have the identity\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2axy-3 & =4xy+b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $xy$ and constant terms, we see that $a=2$ and $b=-3.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403193 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403194 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403193 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403195 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403193 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403196 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403193 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403197 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403193 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403198 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403193 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403193 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403193 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403194 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403193 1080 #uuid "36a84ad8-7e07-5e98-8973-bf508e59e4e4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403194 1081 "$a=2$, $b=-3$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [175921864031