ue] [17592186403653 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the ellipses $(x-1)^{2}+4{y}^{2}=1$ and ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=4?$\n\nI. It is a type I region\nII. It is a type II region\nIII. It's neither a type I nor a type II region" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403653 1072 #uuid "964e90c7-3ddc-59ef-9c19-6cc6da31e561" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403653 1074 "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/21/215dd0c920e700a75896fc54751ec20d197487a2c992cd8910810c66129c14dc.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- The vertical line $x=1$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type I region.\n\n![](images/7e/7e1a0c5dd2b4aadf7efe78d903234b8d00cf4fa92eb7a3b41209a856f2d14b01.png)\n\n- The horizontal line $y=0.25$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](images/a9/a90d7306e3f88a31609e368f9362248d6a12b7922b6a9e8c9f980ab31e7fb140.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403654 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403655 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403654 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403656 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403654 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403657 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403654 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403658 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403654 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403659 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403654 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403654 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403654 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403658 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403654 1080 #uuid "c8f0581f-5142-59ed-84df-f95cc7adf20e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403655 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403655 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17