/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403672 1084 #uuid "fdea791f-9fdb-55f9-aceb-2d7e1234420c" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403673 1081 "$2$nd only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403673 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403673 1084 #uuid "186dbf5e-ae6b-51d6-bcec-ca5ddbec9d8d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403674 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403675 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403674 1069 "q-73612" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403674 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403674 1071 "The row echelon form matrix $B$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 2 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403674 1072 #uuid "701f0d82-dd3a-58b3-b64b-6042ce1e752a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403674 1074 "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $B$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $3$rd and $5$th columns:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 2 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot columns are the $2$nd and $4$th columns." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403675 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403676 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403675 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403677 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403675 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403678 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403675 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403679 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403675 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403680 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403675 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403675 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403675 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403676 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403675 1080 #uuid "bfd951bf-1101-57d3-9237-a2969bb45e55" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403676 1081 "$2$nd and $4$th only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403676 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403676 1084 #uuid "0f5d1b21-d0b9-5d69-8355-827e89736e7b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403677 1081 "$4$th only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403677 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403677 1084 #uuid "ae1f6f68-236b-5baf-b98e-ebb13a837d0c" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403678 1081 "$2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403678 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403678 1084 #uuid "2d838c13-5fd7-5baf-875a-cbdb0a8f06c4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403679 1081 "$2$nd, $4$th, and $5$th only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403679 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403679 1084 #uuid "b50399a2-2bb0-5c2b-b2df-c9a80a6714cb" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403680 1081 "$2$nd only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403680 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403680 1084 #uuid "e320a2ba-1f1d-5701-ac7a-db08a7b45731" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403681 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403682 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403681 1069 "q-73617" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403681 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403681 1071 "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=1-t,\\,\\,\\,y={t}^{2}-4,\\,t\\ge -1,\n$$\n\ndetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403681 1072 #uuid "5fc2dccb-24dd-5003-b2b4-73d21d258e08" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403681 1074 "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ note that $1-t\\le 2$ for all $t\\ge -1.$ Consequently, $x=1-t\\le 2.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ note that ${t}^{2}\\ge 0$ for all $t.$ Consequently, $y={t}^{2}-4\\ge -4.$\n\nTherefore, the ranges are $x\\le 2$ and $y\\ge -4.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403682 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403683 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403682 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403684 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403682 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403685 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403682 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403686 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403682 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403687 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403682 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403682 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403682 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403687 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403682 1080 #uuid "966a4be9-e62e-532a-b5f4-b29c14204104" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403683 1081 "x\\ge -1,\\,y\\ge 0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403683 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403683 1084 #uuid "b9f73d83-c051-5dff-95b7-3c8c97c9edbb" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403684 1081 "x\\ge 0,\\,y\\le -4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403684 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403684 1084 #uuid "ad14150b-a7fa-5e1f-8e26-8118219d8796" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403685 1081 "x\\ge 1,\\,y\\le -4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403685 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403685 1084 #uuid "aa0317e7-34d8-5e8a-a56c-876d04157a55" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403686 1081 "x\\le 4,\\,y\\ge 1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403686 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403686 1084 #uuid "0117c445-1ef3-5ae6-aae5-46c6b2367762" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403687 1081 "x\\le 2,\\,y\\ge -4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403687 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403687 1084 #uuid "a9339c84-b774-56f5-95e7-f320ba73550e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403688 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403689 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403688 1069 "q-73638" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403688 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403688 1071 "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $P,$ given by\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403688 1072 #uuid "8bbb774c-4bbb-58f8-84cb-fd20b0029b02" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403688 1074 "First, we need to convert $P$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & ↔{R}_{4} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $P$ has $4$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th columns." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403689 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403690 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403689 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403691 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403689 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403692 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403689 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403693 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403689 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403694 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403689 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403689 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403689 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403693 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403689 1080 #uuid "6197e392-74ff-5689-be7c-741e44610b04" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403690 1081 "$1$st and $4$th only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403690 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403690 1084 #uuid "62c7b061-ae07-587c-bab0-15049cf99b56" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403691 1081 "$2$nd and $3$rd only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403691 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403691 1084 #uuid "bc30072d-7cf1-5da5-97b9-253a92f7877b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403692 1081 "$1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403692 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403692 1084 #uuid "508efe11-c663-52c3-84b8-ac714fe99937" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403693 1081 "$1$st, $2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403693 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403693 1084 #uuid "8054e257-e2ab-5aa6-b464-152bde3bafb3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403694 1081 "$1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403694 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403694 1084 #uuid "56527d12-3319-58cd-8ff8-f8efdf4d8acf" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403695 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403696 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403695 1069 "q-73740" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403695 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403695 1071 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -10 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403695 1072 #uuid "28d32302-16b0-5cdc-a69e-754fd94318a8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403695 1074 "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -10 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=-1 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+2y=-1.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-1-2y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1-2y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1-2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403696 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403697 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403696 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403698 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403696 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403699 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403696 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403700 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403696 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403701 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403696 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403696 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403696 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403697 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403696 1080 #uuid "0ccee7c5-bc00-583c-adcd-616a8af7768b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403697 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1-2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403697 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403697 1084 #uuid "22cd6aa9-a925-5038-975c-07e44d80e350" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403698 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2+y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403698 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403698 1084 #uuid "0e0364cb-677b-524e-aa38-691178112aba" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403699 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1+2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403699 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403699 1084 #uuid "6274e549-fa07-5abb-bd6c-53630d47a7b8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403700 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403700 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403700 1084 #uuid "11509ba5-2bfa-5670-b24e-690396084002" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403701 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403701 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403701 1084 #uuid "da9d2dd8-4de7-59f6-8ae5-f0b3a20d355b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403702 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403703 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403702 1069 "q-73769" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403702 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403702 1071 "Find the points of intersection of the parabola ${y}^{2}-16x-6y-91=0$ with the $y$-axis." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403702 1072 #uuid "40490cf3-305d-5b56-bda2-cd96ef68cf95" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403702 1074 "When the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we set $x=0$ and solve the resulting equation for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-16(0)-6y-91 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}-6y-91 & =0 \\\\ (y-13)(y+7) & =0 \\\\ y & =13,-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parabola intersects the $y$-axis at $(0,13)$ and $(0,-7).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403703 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403704 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403703 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403705 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403703 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403706 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403703 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403707 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403703 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403708 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403703 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403703 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403703 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403704 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403703 1080 #uuid "a708c3e3-24dc-5816-8cc2-c47d9443150d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403704 1081 "$(0,13)$ and $(0,-7)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403704 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403704 1084 #uuid "ade6b736-21fc-5927-801a-6f95d4712df7" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403705 1081 "$(0,-13)$ and $(0,7)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403705 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403705 1084 #uuid "2cda79e2-68f3-5c41-896a-04084cb1b5f3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403706 1081 "$(0,-13)$ and $(0,-7)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403706 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403706 1084 #uuid "f8befb49-e008-5058-9add-edd4e46f5252" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403707 1081 "$(13,0)$ and $(0,-7)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403707 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403707 1084 #uuid "3a777482-4e1e-57a1-bc18-958db548f36c" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403708 1081 "$(0,13)$ and $(0,7)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403708 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403708 1084 #uuid "2651a385-0c6f-559e-bc57-1a1a3107749a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403709 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403710 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403709 1069 "q-73832" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403709 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403709 1071 "![](images/e7/e79a3a7c2fce5a3e3ec7d838ebe1327dcc5452168f499fad05eea85a08e8f8b0.png)\n\nWhat are the $x$-intercepts of the parabola shown above?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403709 1072 #uuid "166cdda3-01a4-5828-9800-429450a46515" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403709 1074 "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(2,-1)$ and passes through the point $(-2,3).$\n\nThe general standard equation of an up- or down-opening parabola with vertex $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $(h,k)=(2,-1)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2} & =4p(y+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(-2,3),$ we substitute $x=-2$ and $y=3$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2-2)^{2} & =4p(3+1) \\\\ 16 & =4p(4) \\\\ p & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2} & =4(y+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2} & =4(0+1) \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =4 \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm \\sqrt{4} \\\\ x & =\\pm 2+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts are $0$ and $4.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403710 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403711 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403710 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403712 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403710 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403713 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403710 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403714 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403710 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403715 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403710 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403710 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403710 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403714 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403710 1080 #uuid "199aaf87-46d2-5438-b5f3-ee557ec29887" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403711 1081 "$0$  and $\\sqrt{5}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403711 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403711 1084 #uuid "544b7ae8-40b2-5ec8-83d6-d19730e6b5a3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403712 1081 "$0$ and $5$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403712 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403712 1084 #uuid "2316f0bc-0936-5acf-bd1b-fe6117ca3155" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403713 1081 "$0$ and $3$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403713 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403713 1084 #uuid "1bacfa54-8104-51a9-b2bd-c3c2a3c703ad" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403714 1081 "$0$ and $4$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403714 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403714 1084 #uuid "019cfb67-fa2a-5255-b2d3-9c68213d29fc" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403715 1081 "$0$ and $2\\sqrt{5}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403715 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403715 1084 #uuid "8cdd38f7-11c0-5b67-b2ce-d02618e9c7a7" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403716 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403717 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403716 1069 "q-73860" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403716 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403716 1071 "At which points on the surface $z={x}^{3}-3x+{y}^{2}+2y$ is the tangent plane horizontal?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403716 1072 #uuid "14749651-a6a1-55fa-b209-fec427b8a368" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403716 1074 "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhere $⟨\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),-1⟩$ represents a normal vector to the tangent plane.\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}-3x+{y}^{2}+2y) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}-3 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{3}-3x+{y}^{2}+2y) \\\\  & =2y+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nHence, the normal vector to the tangent plane is \n\n$$\n⟨3{x}^{2}-3,\\,2y+2,\\,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nNote that the tangent plane is horizontal if and only if the normal vector is vertical. This means that the $x$- and $y$-components of the vector must be $0:$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=0 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-3=0 \\\\ 2y+2=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFrom the first equation, we get $x=\\pm 1$ while the second equation gives $y=-1.$ \n\nFinally, substituting $x=-1$ and $y=-1$ into our function, we get\n\n$$\nz=(-1)^{3}-3(-1)+(-1)^{2}+2(-1)=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=1$ and $y=-1$ into our function, we get\n\n$$\nz=(1)^{3}-3(1)+(-1)^{2}+2(-1)=-3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points where the tangent plane is horizontal are $(-1,-1,1)$ and $(1,-1,-3).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403717 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403718 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403717 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403719 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403717 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403720 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403717 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403721 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403717 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403722 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403717 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403717 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403717 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403718 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403717 1080 #uuid "29a46a2f-b76d-5223-bfa0-caee05f36438" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403718 1081 "$(-1,-1,1)$ and $(1,-1,-3)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403718 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403718 1084 #uuid "90f4afcf-4af1-5320-a876-c7e43193b7cc" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403719 1081 "$(1,-1,-3)$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403719 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403719 1084 #uuid "aaeb48d9-f69d-5b9e-9626-640bfefc395e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403720 1081 "$(1,1,0)$ and $(-1,1,2)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403720 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403720 1084 #uuid "98696df4-b0fb-53ef-a177-bce372e2f606" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403721 1081 "$(1,-1,2)$ and $(-1,-1,0)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403721 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403721 1084 #uuid "1cffc4be-00ee-57b7-9ac9-95e61bc1ca5c" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403722 1081 "$(-1,-1,1)$  only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403722 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403722 1084 #uuid "479f131a-35b5-598d-93be-4ae6e4b42f61" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403723 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403724 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403723 1069 "q-73866" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403723 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403723 1071 "For the elliptic paraboloid $\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}=z+5$, the section in the plane $\\sqrt{3}x-2y=2\\sqrt{3}$ is a parabola. \nFind the vertex of the projection of this parabola onto $xz$-plane." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403723 1072 #uuid "cc9a60c0-9b27-537d-8f7e-b89ae32845f5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403723 1074 "Since we want to find the projection onto the $xz$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $y.$ First, we solve for $y$ in the equation of the plane, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{3}x-2y=2\\sqrt{3}\\,⟹\\,y=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}(x-2)}{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expression for $y$ into the equation of the paraboloid, we obtain: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{4}+{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}(x-2)}{2})}^{2} & =z+5 \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{3(x-2)^{2}}{4} & =z+5 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}+4x+4}{4}+\\frac{3{x}^{2}-12x+12}{4} & =z+5 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}-8x+16}{4} & =z+5 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x+4 & =z+5 \\\\ z & ={x}^{2}-2x-1 \\\\ z & =({x}^{2}-2x+1)-2 \\\\ z & ={(x-1)}^{2}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the vertex of the projection onto $xz$-plane is $(1,-2).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403724 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403725 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403724 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403726 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403724 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403727 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403724 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403728 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403724 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403729 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403724 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403724 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403724 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403725 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403724 1080 #uuid "635cbbf9-c9f6-5df5-ac89-d0b4c298244a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403725 1081 "$(1,-2)$ in the $xz$-plane" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403725 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403725 1084 #uuid "b46c7ae5-0a46-59a6-bf83-e94f8ccd0940" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403726 1081 "$(-1,5)$ in the $xz$-plane" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403726 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403726 1084 #uuid "9566cc47-e8d9-5640-b0dc-201689f1ab94" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403727 1081 "$(1,-5)$ in the $xz$-plane" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403727 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403727 1084 #uuid "2357d2af-705d-5e3c-9928-fdd9ee85001e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403728 1081 "$(1,0)$ in the $xz$-plane" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403728 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403728 1084 #uuid "761cef9d-c588-526d-a20b-157cfe62168e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403729 1081 "$(-1,2)$ in the $xz$-plane" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403729 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403729 1084 #uuid "27a115d9-7ebe-5bc3-87bb-45cfdc28a5ef" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403730 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403731 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403730 1069 "q-73869" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403730 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403730 1071 "At which points on the surface $z=x{e}^{y}+{y}^{2}$ is the tangent plane perpendicular to the vector  $v\\,=\\,⟨-2,4,2⟩?$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403730 1072 #uuid "4dda47ef-07a9-5b66-b0c0-061f88baf1dd" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403730 1074 "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhere $⟨\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),-1⟩$ represents a normal vector to the tangent plane.\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{e}^{y}+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & ={e}^{y} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{e}^{y}+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =x{e}^{y}+2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the normal vector to the tangent plane is \n\n$$\n⟨{e}^{y},\\,x{e}^{y}+2y,\\,-1⟩\n$$\n\nOur tangent plane should be perpendicular to $⟨-2,4,2⟩.$ So, the normal vector of that plane must be parallel to that vector. In other words, for some constant $c$, we must have\n\n$$\nc\\cdot ⟨{e}^{y},\\,x{e}^{y}+2y,\\,-1⟩=⟨-2,4,2⟩.\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding coordinates, we obtain the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}c{e}^{y}=-2 \\\\ cx{e}^{y}+2cy=4 \\\\ -c=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $c=-2.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n-2{e}^{y}=-2\\,⟹\\,y=0.\n$$\n\nAnd substituting $c=-2$ and $y=0$ into the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n-2x{e}^{0}+2(-2)(0)=4\\,⟹\\,x=-2.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=-2$ and $y=0$ into our function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =x{e}^{y}+{y}^{2} \\\\  & =(-2){e}^{0}+{0}^{2} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent plane is perpendicular to the vector $v$ at $(-2,0,-2).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403731 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403732 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403731 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403733 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403731 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403734 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403731 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403735 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403731 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403736 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403731 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403731 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403731 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403735 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403731 1080 #uuid "72aa1076-cce3-53b6-97d2-101a723b64a3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403732 1081 "$(-1,0,-1)$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403732 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403732 1084 #uuid "c645d1ad-7209-5343-8f48-3586d833b4f1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403733 1081 "$(-1,0,-1)$ and $(1,0,1)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403733 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403733 1084 #uuid "d2196f73-bb73-51d9-8fdd-442f665c7869" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403734 1081 "$(2,0,2)$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403734 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403734 1084 #uuid "af9a2b62-523f-5ba8-b214-6d70686e54b9" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403735 1081 "$(-2,0,-