 at the point $(-2,1).$ For this, we need to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ which means we first need to find the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=4{t}^{3}-6t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=6{t}^{2}-1.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{6{t}^{2}-1}{4{t}^{3}-6t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=1,$  the slope $m$ of the tangent line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={\\frac{dy}{dx}|}_{t=1} & =\\frac{6(1)^{2}-1}{4(1)^{3}-6(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{-2} \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{5}{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope ${m}_{n}$ of the normal line, we take the negative reciprocal of $m$:\n\n$$\n{m}_{n}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{(\\,-\\frac{5}{2}\\,)}=\\frac{2}{5}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the equation of the normal, we use point-slope form with the point $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(-2,1)$ and the slope ${m}_{n}=\\frac{2}{5}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-1 & =\\frac{2}{5}(x+2) \\\\ y & =\\frac{2}{5}(x+2)+1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403829 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403830 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403829 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403831 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403829 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403832 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403829 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403833 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403829 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403834 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403829 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403829 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403829 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403832 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403829 1080 #uuid "bbc1b61e-03fa-5261-ae12-a9f784057a88" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403830 1081 "y=\\frac{2}{5}(x+2)-1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403830 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403830 1084 #uuid "d5eb255