45500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403848 1084 #uuid "cc1a32ca-3acb-5d7d-b8ad-8a49ebecf6c4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403849 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403850 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403849 1069 "q-7642" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403849 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403849 1071 "Calculate the points where the ellipse \n$\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{6}=1$ intercepts the $y$-axis." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403849 1072 #uuid "c9bca935-b9bf-540f-a535-f5de3e3b987f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403849 1074 "To calculate the $y$-intercept, we need to substitute $x=0$ in the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $y.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{6} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(0-1)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{6} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{6} & =1 \\\\ 4+6(y+2)^{2} & =36 \\\\ 6(y+2)^{2} & =32 \\\\ 3(y+2)^{2} & =16 \\\\ (y+2)^{2} & =\\frac{16}{3} \\\\ y+2 & =\\pm \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ y & =-2\\pm \\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $y$-axis at the points $(0,-2-\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{3})$ and $(0,-2+\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{3}).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403850 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403851 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403850 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403852 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403850 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403853 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403850 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403854 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403850 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403855 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403850 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403850 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403850 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403851 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403850