y=0$ into the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $x.$ We do this and solve the resulting equation by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}-36x+16y & =-16 \\\\ 9{x}^{2}+4(0)^{2}-36x+16(0) & =-16 \\\\ 9{x}^{2}-36x & =-16 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4x & =-\\frac{16}{9} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}-{2}^{2} & =-\\frac{16}{9} \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =-\\frac{16}{9}+4 \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =-\\frac{16}{9}+\\frac{36}{9} \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =\\frac{20}{9} \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3} \\\\ x & =2\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $x$-axis at $(2-\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3},0)$ and $(2+\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3},0).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403857 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403858 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403857 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403859 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403857 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403860 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403857 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403861 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403857 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403862 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403857 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403857 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403857 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403861 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403857 1080 #uuid "e32446d2-a32e-554b-89ca-512e15fbc942" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403858 1081 "(1\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},0)" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403858 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403858 1084 #uuid "19a9a2f6-bd42-5579-a2ff-e314a223a8b1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403859 1081 "(1\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3},0)" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403859 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403859 1084 #uuid "85bc7d3a-2417-530a-983c-0a9380f5af4e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [1759