ons of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $g(x)={2}^{1/{x}^{2}}$ is not defined at $x=0,$ hence, it is not continuous at \n$x=0,$ and so it is not continuous on $[-4,4].$ Therefore, $g(x)$ does not satisfiy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $h(x)=\\sqrt{x+4}$ is continuous on $[-4,\\infty )$ and differentiable on $(-4,\\infty ).$ In particular, it is continuous on $[-4,4]$ and differentiable on $(-4,4).$ Therefore, $h(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\nTherefore, only the functions I and III satisfy the conditions for the mean value theorem over the interval $[-4,4].$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403926 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403927 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403926 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403928 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403926 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403929 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403926 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403930 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403926 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403931 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403926 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403926 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403926 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403928 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403926 1080 #uuid "8b1b4626-8500-573c-8ccc-0601d1a1fa54" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403927 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403927 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403927 1084 #uuid "57a0952d-7db5-57ee-878c-0528fe98cbc2" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403928 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403928 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403928 1084 #uuid "d248d05c-c26d-5279-a4c9-650778c4adfc" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403929 1081 "I only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186403