8 17592186045585 true] [17592186404071 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404071 1071 "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n(x+1)\\frac{dy}{dx}=2{y}^{1/2}(x+1)^{3}+2y,\\,y(0)=\\frac{1}{4},\\,x>-1.\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the fact that the given differential equation can be transformed into the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{1}{x+1}\\,z=(x+1)^{2}\n$$\n\nusing the substitution $z={y}^{1/2}.$*" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404071 1072 #uuid "c2213d2c-5fa6-5310-a52f-41ff5bbd4ec5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404071 1074 "The substitution $z={y}^{1/2}$ transforms the given equation into the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{1}{x+1}\\,z=(x+1)^{2},\n$$\n\nwith the initial condition\n\n$$\nz(0)=\\sqrt{y(0)}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,.\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\nP(x)=-\\frac{1}{x+1},\\,Q(x)=(x+1)^{2}\\,.\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-\\int 1/(x+1)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)^{-1}} \\\\  & =(x+1)^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nunder the condition that $x>-1.$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)=(x+1)^{-1}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{x+1}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{1}{x+1}\\,z) & =\\frac{1}{x+1}\\cdot (x+1)^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x+1}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{1}{(x+1)^{2}}\\,z & =x+1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{x+1}\\,z) & =x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{x+1}\\,z)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,z & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+x+C \\\\ z & =(x+1)(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+x+C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we determine the value of $C$ that satisfies the initial condition $z(0)=\\frac{1}{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z(0) & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ (0+1)(\\frac{1}{2}{0}^{2}+0+C) & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ C & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have \n\n$$\nz=(x+1)(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+x+\\frac{1}{2})\\,.\n$$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by substituting the solution into $z={y}^{1/2}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{1/2} & =(x+1)(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+x+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ y & =(x+1)^{2}{(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404072 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404073 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404072 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404074 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404072 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404075 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404072 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404076 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404072 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404077 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404072 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404072 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404072 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404075 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404072 1080 #uuid "b5400590-876e-51ce-80d8-59c049ac6615" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404073 1081 "y={(x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}{({x}^{2}+1)}^{2}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404073 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404073 1084 #uuid "25a3eb10-2e29-538b-8e42-ae99c94ac32f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404074 1081 "y=(x+\\frac{1}{4})(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+x)" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404074 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404074 1084 #uuid "7cb2d24f-0cf5-5987-8f28-2e07f5e68a80" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404075 1081 "y=(x+1)^{2}{(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}" 13194139533478 17592