9533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404134 1071 "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda $ of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404134 1072 #uuid "ba3b9cc6-841d-5636-9777-0bc1e8c24e7f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404134 1074 "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is given by $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st row, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}+6\\lambda +5)-(-1-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}+7\\lambda +6 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}-7\\lambda -6 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to solve this equation. We find the first root by testing some values. According to the rational zeros theorem, a list of good first guesses consists of all divisors of $6:$ \n\n$$\n\\pm 1,\\pm 2,\\pm 3,\\pm 6\n$$\n\n- Let's pick $x=1.$ Substituting to the characteristic equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1)^{3}-7(1)-6 & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $\\lambda =1$ is not a root of the equation.\n\n- Let's pick $x=-1.$ Substituting to the characteristic equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)^{3}-7(-1)-6 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $\\lambda =-1$ is a root of the equation.\n\nSo, we can factor $(\\lambda +1)$ out of ${\\lambda }^{3}-7\\lambda -6$ using synthetic division:\n\n| $-1$ | $1$ | $0$ | $-7$ | $-6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $↓$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $6$ |\n|  | $1$ | $-1$ | $-6$ | $0$ |\n\nSo, we obtain the following factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda +1)({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -6) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1,$ $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-2,\\,$ and $\\,{\\lambda }_{3}=3.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404135 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404136 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404135 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404137 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404135 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404138 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404135 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404139 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404135 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404140 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404135 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404135 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404135 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404139 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404135 1080 #uuid "135ac5a3-acd1-57d7-85af-ac59d7bb8214" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404136 1081 "\\lambda \\in {1,-6}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404136 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404136 1084 #uuid "8d3a6e5c-6b63-525d-b4d4-f7578f8a390f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404137 1081 "\\lambda \\in {-1,2,-3}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404137 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404137 1084 #uuid "be0e2c11-87fe-59eb-9698-32afe60aafab" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404138 1081 "\\lambda \\in {2,-3}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404138 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404138 1084 #uuid "fdd9bbcf-ec11-5649-bcb8-ae71202883ad" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404139 1081 "\\lambda \\in {-1,-2,3}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404139 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 175921860