  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{{x}^{2}})}{(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}+4-2x)}{(1-\\frac{1}{x})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, when $x$ is very large, the terms $\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}$ and $\\frac{1}{x}$ become very small. Therefore, as $x\\to \\infty ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{(\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}+4-2x)}{(1-\\frac{1}{x})} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{0+4-2x}{1-0} \\\\  & =4-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is not a constant, which means that $y=f(x)$ does not have a horizontal asymptote." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404149 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404150 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404149 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404151 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404149 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404152 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404149 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404153 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404149 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404154 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404149 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404149 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404149 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404152 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404149 1080 #uuid "235aadc5-963f-5fda-85cc-68d107673c61" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404150 1081 "y=3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404150 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404150 1084 #uuid "d098974e-26ed-5d31-b1cd-a3dbc06e5513" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404151 1081 "y=4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404151 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404151 1084 #uuid "f4a92768-6f32-5589-8651-0b25ea1a112b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404152 1081 "No horizontal asymptotes" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404152 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404152 1084 #uuid "7bd5d749-fe1e-50cd-8a40-2be69a0ab8d2" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404153 1081 "y=-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404153 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404153 1084 #uuid "f8fb75dc-1ab6-5d98-9700-9f4e9f0bef00" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404154 1081 "y=-2" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404154 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404154 1084 #uuid "eb5c324b-f42d-5122-b7c3-fe01bb4516cf" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404155 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404156 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404155 1069 "q-81236" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404155 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404155 1071 "Find the eigenvectors of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $T$ given that \n\n$$\nT[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404155 1072 #uuid "811972db-6534-593a-aa1e-100258f3cf1f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404155 1074 "Notice that the matrix $[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]$ appears on both sides of the equation. Since this matrix is invertible (its determinant is not zero), right-multiplying the equation by the inverse gives the following expression for $T:$\n\n$$\nT={{[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{P}{{[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{D}{{{[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}}_{⏟}}_{{P}^{-1}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $T$ is diagonalizable. The eigenvalues of $T$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-1$ and the corresponding eigenvectors are the columns of the matrix $P:$\n\n$\\,$ ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404156 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404157 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404156 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404158 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404156 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404159 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404156 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404160 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404156 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404161 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404156 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404156 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404156 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404161 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404156 1080 #uuid "630df7f3-d3b0-52b1-a138-2b8c01a3e3ed" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404157 1081 "$[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ \\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404157 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404157 1084 #uuid "f64437bc-258f-57d6-8252-86408694ed54" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404158 1081 "$[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404158 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404158 1084 #uuid "e9fce00d-d8dc-5d30-b228-f50bd9f70fa5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404159 1081 "$[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404159 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404159 1084 #uuid "ea65c7ad-6c2b-58e5-8658-7ac9d1dfed34" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404160 1081 "$[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404160 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404160 1084 #uuid "06abf95b-dbcf-5d63-a7e2-6b9ef8e25083" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404161 1081 "$[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404161 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404161 1084 #uuid "163ea62e-033a-5464-9c63-6deea7d57755" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404162 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404163 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404162 1069 "q-81273" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404162 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404162 1071 "Find the locations of all of the critical points of $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}\\,\\,v \\\\ u+{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404162 1072 #uuid "82fb995e-103e-58b4-a8e9-4c6b2963c1a3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404162 1074 "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTo find the locations of the critical points of $T,$ we need to solve \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)={u}^{2}\\,\\,v$ and $y(u,v)=u+{v}^{2}.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =2uv & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & ={u}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =2v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2uv & {u}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 2v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2uv\\cdot 2v-{u}^{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4u{v}^{2}-{u}^{2} \\\\  & =u(4{v}^{2}-u).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.$ So, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =0 \\\\ u(4{v}^{2}-u) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equation $u(4{v}^{2}-u)=0$ defines a pair of intersecting curves in the $uv$-plane: the line $u=0$ and the parabola $u=4{v}^{2}.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404163 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404164 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404163 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404165 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404163 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404166 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404163 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404167 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404163 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404168 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404163 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404163 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404163 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404168 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404163 1080 #uuid "3dd706ed-a6fa-5777-8fba-b9aa9ded06db" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404164 1081 "The critical points lie on the lines $u=v$ and $u=-v.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404164 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404164 1084 #uuid "5a499ca4-07df-5c8d-b83c-a9910cc2fe6f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404165 1081 "The critical points lie on the lines $u=0$ and $u=v.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404165 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404165 1084 #uuid "2cf255f1-3d51-5826-98c1-93901517d605" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404166 1081 "The critical points lie on the parabola $u={v}^{2}.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404166 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404166 1084 #uuid "5da5054c-581f-5f31-9886-dad4f588043d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404167 1081 "The critical points lie on the lines $u=0$ and $u=-v.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404167 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404167 1084 #uuid "6060e83f-92e8-5d62-986a-7a4aa49b2792" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404168 1081 "The critical points lie on the line $u=0$ and on the parabola $u=4{v}^{2}.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404168 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404168 1084 #uuid "1669bc78-1efd-58f9-91e9-a08a66025cf0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404169 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404170 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404169 1069 "q-81279" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404169 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404169 1071 "Find the locations of all of the critical points of $T,$ where $T$ is defined as \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}+3{v}^{2} \\\\ u-2v\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404169 1072 #uuid "59e9bc67-c967-5c58-a234-d26582651fa3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404169 1074 "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the locations of the critical points of $T,$ we need to solve \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)={u}^{2}+3{v}^{2}$ and $y(u,v)=u-2v.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =2u & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =6v \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2u & 6v \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2u\\cdot (-2)-6v\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-4u-6v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.$ So, we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =0 \\\\ -4u-6v & =0 \\\\ 2u+3v & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $2u+3v=0$ defines a line in the $uv$-plane." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404170 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404171 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404170 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404172 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404170 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404173 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404170 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404174 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404170 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404175 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404170 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404170 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404170 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404172 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404170 1080 #uuid "e87074f0-9d22-553d-826e-78e5774760d7" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404171 1081 "The critical points lie on the line $v=\\frac{2}{3}.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404171 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404171 1084 #uuid "27dd60f7-0060-5908-af95-4c108c3b1718"