rential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2yx+y{x}^{2}$ that satisfies $y(1)=1.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404237 1072 #uuid "177e97c5-b0fe-5fdf-abe1-80b42d3faf53" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404237 1074 "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2yx+y{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y(2x+{x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x+{x}^{2} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ y & =\\pm {e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ y & =K{e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=1$ to find $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =1 \\\\ K{e}^{{1}^{2}+{1}^{3}/3} & =1 \\\\ K{e}^{4/3} & =1 \\\\ K & ={e}^{-4/3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2yx+y{x}^{2}$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-4/3}\\cdot {e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3}={e}^{({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-4)/3}\\,.\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404238 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404239 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404238 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404240 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404238 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404241 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404238 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404242 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404238 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404243 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404238 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404238 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404238 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404243 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404238 1080 #uuid "5399864b-fdb6-560a-bb1c-eadfa2e8485b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404239 1081 "y={e}^{3{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-1}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404239 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404239 1084 #uuid "aa22294c-97df-59d3-a2ef-bb723379bd93" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404240 1081 "y={e}^{({x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-2)/3}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404240 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404240 1084 #uuid "05c76659-9ee2-5ea1-9921-4c61064bc47c" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404241 1081 "y={e}^{(2{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-1)/3}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404241 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404241 1084 #uuid "d957c339-7d86-5b49-bfb4-f34772448576" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404242 1081 "y={e}^{{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404242 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404242 1084 #uuid "59acccda-8ad0-5671-8d3b-1eba77285637" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404243 1081 "y={e}^{({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-4)/3}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404243 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404243 1084 #uuid "08886f8e-1110-502c-b6b0-62359e9dd0d0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404244 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404245 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404244 1069 "q-83217" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404244 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404244 1071 "Use the first two non-zero terms of the Taylor expansion of ${x}^{-1/2}$ about $x=9$ to approximate the value of ${8}^{-1/2}.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404244 1072 #uuid "f750b509-3c63-5fc0-8993-9bde234b6a4e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404244 1074 "We use Taylor's formula in the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(a)}{2!}(x-a)^{2}+⋯,\n$$\n\nwith $a=9.$ \n\nCalculating the necessary derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={x}^{-1/2} \\\\ f(9) & ={9}^{-1/2}=\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-3/2} \\\\ {f}^{′}(9) & =-\\frac{1}{2}(9)^{-3/2}=-\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 27}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Taylor series is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{-1/2} & =\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 27}(x-9)+⋯ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{x-9}{54}+⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute $x=8$ into the above to approximate ${8}^{-1/2}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{8}^{-1/2} & ≈\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{8-9}{54} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{54} \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{54}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404245 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404246 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404245 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404247 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404245 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404248 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404245 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404249 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404245 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404250 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404245 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404245 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404245 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404246 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404245 1080 #uuid "62f9d6d4-3621-5ba8-8abe-069970462f3e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404246 1081 "{8}^{-1/2}≈\\frac{19}{54}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404246 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404246 1084 #uuid "01db7ff6-6460-5d8d-ade8-71a8e02c2a81" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404247 1081 "{8}^{-1/2}≈\\frac{17}{81}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404247 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404247 1084 #uuid "d8373422-756d-5371-80d9-489591080546" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404248 1081 "{8}^{-1/2}≈\\frac{8}{27}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404248 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404248 1084 #uuid "635cb5d7-7f18-5bb2-a15b-2282c9accf79" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404249 1081 "{8}^{-1/2}≈\\frac{5}{12}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404249 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404249 1084 #uuid "4da8621d-de59-5cf2-8a08-783a60173651" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404250 1081 "{8}^{-1/2}≈\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404250 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404250 1084 #uuid "064bd6fd-ada7-5cba-9a3e-93099a992f58" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404251 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404252 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404251 1069 "q-83429" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404251 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404251 1071 "Find the first three non-zero terms of the Maclaurin expansion of ${x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404251 1072 #uuid "83cee5be-d033-528b-aa1a-c2f13225ee96" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404251 1074 "The standard Maclaurin expansion for $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5!}-⋯ \\\\  & =x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{120}-⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get an expansion for ${x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ we multiply this series by ${x}^{2}.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & ={x}^{2}(x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{120}-⋯) \\\\  & ={x}^{3}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{6}+\\frac{{x}^{7}}{120}-⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404252 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404253 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404252 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404254 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404252 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404255 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404252 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404256 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404252 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404257 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404252 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404252 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404252 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404257 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404252 1080 #uuid "38f38032-483e-5ebe-a2ba-4fc05febd614" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404253 1081 "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-{x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{6}-\\frac{{x}^{6}}{120}+⋯" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404253 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404253 1084 #uuid "e6684cb3-66f7-5670-a618-240321438de8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404254 1081 "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x={x}^{3}+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{12}+\\frac{{x}^{7}}{60}+⋯" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404254 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404254 1084 #uuid "d8eb2141-deaf-5745-8f39-c0df69c4795f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404255 1081 "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=1-x+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}-⋯" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404255 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404255 1084 #uuid "c8f058db-10d3-5127-a407-810a87d6f495" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404256 1081 "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x={x}^{3}-\\frac{{x}^{6}}{24}+\\frac{{x}^{9}}{96}-⋯" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404256 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404256 1084 #uuid "6537e3c8-b8ab-55e5-9855-26f836f4373a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404257 1081 "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x={x}^{3}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{6}+\\frac{{x}^{7}}{120}-⋯" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404257 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404257 1084 #uuid "1ccc3d10-6b2b-5fed-b615-462c22afdb65" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404258 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404259 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404258 1069 "q-83479" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404258 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404258 1071 "![](images/8c/8ce943f8a77fe5756fdaf77185d8b59493ef0da95da3605f1f2416786f9ec394.png)\n\nFind the global extrema of the function $f(x,y)=xy-4$ on the closed region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 4},$ shown above." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404258 1072 #uuid "74b4ac53-7bdb-5efd-8618-b21e911d16f3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404258 1074 "Since $f(x,y)$ is continuous on the closed, bounded region $D,$ the function attains a global maximum and minimum on $D.$\n\nTo find the extreme values, we follow three steps.\n\n**Step 1.** Find the critical points of $f$ inside the region. \n\nTo determine the critical points, we solve ${f}^{′}=0.$ Computing the derivative gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}y,\\,x\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe derivative exists at each point inside $D,$ and it equals zero when\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0,\\,y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us a single point $(0,0).$ Since the point $(0,0)$ does not belong to the interior of $D,$ we do not yet include it in the list of candidates for extrema (it lies on the boundary of $D,$ so we will consider it in the next step).\n\n**Step 2.**  Find the points on the boundary of $D$ that could give rise to extreme values. \n\nTo find the points on the boundary that could give rise to extreme values, we parametrize each part of the boundary:\n\n- The line connecting $(-2,4)$ and $(2,4)$ can be parametrized as\n\n$$\nr=⟨t,4⟩,\\,t\\in (-2,2).\n$$\n\nThe values of $f$ on this boundary are given by the function\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(t) & =f(x(t),y(t)) \\\\  & =f(t,4) \\\\  & =(t)(4)-4 \\\\  & =4t-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the derivative of $F(t)$ is constant. So, $F(t)$ does not have critical points in the open interval $t\\in (-2,2).$\n\n- The parabola connecting $(-2,4)$ and $(2,4)$ can be parametrized as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨t,{t}^{2}⟩,\\,t\\in (-2,2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe values of $f$ on the boundary are given by the function\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(t) & =f(x(t),y(t)) \\\\  & =f(t,{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =(t)({t}^{2})-4 \\\\  & ={t}^{3}-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nTo find the critical points of $F(t)$ on the open interval $t\\in (-2,2),$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{′}(t) & =0 \\\\ ({t}^{3}-4)^{′} & =0 \\\\ 3{t}^{2} & =0 \\\\ t & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final equation gives one solution $t=0$ inside the interval $t\\in (-2,2).$\nEvaluating the corresponding values of $x$ and $y$ on the boundary, we obtain one candidate point, $(0,0).$\n\nAlso, we have to include the corner points of the region as candidates for extrema. So, in total we obtain three candidates:\n\n$$\n(0,0),\\,(2,4),\\,(-2,4)\n$$\n\n**Step 3.** Evaluate $f(x,y)$ at each of the candidate points, and compare their values. \n\nEvaluating $f(x,y)$ at each of the points mentioned above, we get the following: \n\n| $(x,y)$ | $(0,0)$ | $(2,4)$ | $(-2,4)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x,y)$ | $-4$ | $4$ | $-12$ |\n\nTherefore, on the closed region $D,$ we have that \n\n- $f$ attains the global minimum of $-12$ at the point $(-2,4)$ and\n\n- $f$ attains the global maximum of $4$ at the points $(2,4).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404259 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404260 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404259 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404261 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404259 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404262 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404259 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404263 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404259 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404264 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404259 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404259 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404259 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404264 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404259 1080 #uuid "24e0c5a8-3acd-57db-aba7-34b3ec30ab80" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404260 1081 "${f}_{min}=-10$ and ${f}_{max}=5$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404260 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404260 1084 #uuid "cccc9be8-40ad-59d1-85aa-0c32e8379a16" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404261 1081 "${f}_{min}=-4$ and ${f}_{max}=0$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404261 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404261 1084 #uuid "ec57171d-50ae-555b-9220-9f9b5b798b9f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404262 1081 "${f}_{min}=0$ and ${f}_{max}=12$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404262 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404262 1084 #uuid "097476c4-4c40-568d-90a8-2be9e9dfcb7d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404263 1081 "${f}_{min}=-4$ and ${f}_{max}=4$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404263 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404263 1084 #uuid "ae56b583-e6d7-5084-af2a-bd8d9b194ce6" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404264 1081 "${f}_{min}=-12$ and ${f}_{max}=4$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [175921864