 [17592186404279 1069 "q-83710" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404279 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404279 1071 "Consider the matrix $A$ for which ${\\lambda }_{1}=1,$ ${\\lambda }_{2}=2,$ ${\\lambda }_{3}=3$ are eigenvalues, and \n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nare the respective eigenvectors. Find the matrices $P$ and $D$ such that $PD{P}^{-1}=A,$ where $D$ is a diagonal matrix." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404279 1072 #uuid "c42e4814-ec50-5416-8161-bbb51b0ed62b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404279 1074 "Since the eigenvalues of the matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=1,$ ${\\lambda }_{2}=2,$ ${\\lambda }_{3}=3,$ we construct the diagonal matrix $D$ by writing the eigenvalues in the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, to construct the matrix $P,$ we simply write the respective eigenvectors as columns: \n\n- the $1$st column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{1}=1,$\n\n- the $2$nd column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{2}=2,$ and\n\n- the $3$rd column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{3}=3.$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404280 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404281 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404280 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404282 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404280 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404283 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404280 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404284 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404280 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404285 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404280 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true]