 $(0,0)\\in D,$ which we include in the list of candidates for the extrema.\n\n**Step 2.**  Find the points on the boundary of $D$ that could give rise to extreme values. \n\nTo find the boundary points that could give rise to extreme values, we parametrize the bounding ellipse ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=9.$ This gives\n\n$$\nr=⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nThe values of $f$ on the boundary are given by the function\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(t) & =f(x(t),y(t)) \\\\  & =f(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =1-4(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =1-18\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\  & =1-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTo find the critical points of $F(t)$ on the open interval $t\\in (0,2\\pi ),$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{′}(t) & =0 \\\\ (1-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))^{′} & =0 \\\\ -18\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final equation gives four solutions, namely\n\n$$\nt=\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\,\\frac{5\\pi }{4},\\,\\frac{7\\pi }{4}\\in (0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nWe also have to check the endpoint of the interval $t=0.$ Therefore, the only values of $t$ that can give rise to extreme values are \n\n$$\nt=0,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\,\\frac{5\\pi }{4},\\,\\frac{7\\pi }{4}.\n$$\n\nEvaluating the corresponding values of $x$ and $y$ on the boundary, we obtain five candidate points:\n\n$$\n(3,0),\\,(\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4}),\\,(-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4}),\\,(-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4}),\\,(\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4})\n$$\n\n**Step 3.** Evaluate $f(x,y)$ at each of the candidate points, and compare their values. \n\nEvaluating $f(x,y)$ at each of the points mentioned above, we get the following: \n\n| $(x,y)$ | $(0,0)$ | $(3,0)$ | $(\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4})$ | $(-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4})$ | $(-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4})$ | $(\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4})$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x,y)$ | $1$ | $1$ | $-8$ | $10$ | $-8$ | $10$ |\n\nTherefore, on the closed region $D,$ we have that \n\n- $f$ attains the global minimum of $-8$ at the points $(\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4})$ and $(-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4}),$ and\n\n- $f$ attains the global maximum of $10$ at the points $(-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4})$ and $(\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4}).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404371 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404372 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404371 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404373 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404371 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404374 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404371 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404375 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404371 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404376 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404371 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404371 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404371 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404372 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404371 1080 #uuid "20a29c76-a92d-5a15-9982-689804fc2dba" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404372 1081 "${f}_{min}=-8$ and ${f}_{max}=10$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404372 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404372 1084 #uuid "233ac657-1b6c-5153-ae47-c73f6a18839b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404373 1081 "${f}_{min}=1$ and ${f}_{max}=10$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404373 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404373 1084 #uuid "1398af4c-7ac7-570a-a8f9-3e7b4fb50230" 13194139533478 17592186045585 tr