he extrema.\n\n**Step 2.** Find the points on the boundary that could give rise to extreme values.\n\nIn this case, we are *given* the points on the boundary of our region that could potentially be global extrema for $f.$ These are\n\n$$\n(-2,0),\\,(2,0).\n$$\n\n**Step 3.** Evaluate $f(x,y)$ at each of the candidate points, and compare their values. \n\nEvaluating $f(x,y)$ at each of the points mentioned above, we get the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2,0) & =(-2)^{2}-6(-2)+(0)^{2}+1 \\\\  & =17 \\\\ f(2,0) & =(2)^{2}-6(2)+(0)^{2}+1 \\\\  & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, on the closed region $D,$ we have that \n\n- $f$ attains the global minimum of $-7$ at the point $(2,0),$ and\n\n- $f$ attains the global maximum of $17$ at the point $(-2,0).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404378 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404379 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404378 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404380 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404378 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404381 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404378 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404382 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404378 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404383 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404378 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404378 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404378 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404381 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404378 1080 #uuid "6009c72a-9f51-5ad2-ae87-7dc2fbcb6754" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404379 1081 "${f}_{min}=-1$ and ${f}_{max}=16$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404379 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404379 1084 #uuid "bf37b4ad-f1a1-5a13-8dd8-d35dc56030e2" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404380 1081 "${f}_{min}=-11$ and ${f}_{max}=-1$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404380 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404380 1084 #uuid "5980b150-496c-55d6-8d60-52afa76e9b6b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404381 1081 "${f}_{min}=-7$ and ${f}_{max}=17$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404381 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404381 1084 #uuid "d5651eb6-a478-51ea-b582-8eee402be230" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404382 1081 "${f}_{min}=0$ and ${f}_{max}=17$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404382 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404382 1084 #uuid "e56bac34-6636-58da-9694-caed75b4198b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404383 1081 "${f}_{min}=-11$ and ${f}_{max}=16$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404383 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404383 1084 #uuid "08b74c80-69bd-5d43-8f58-45d6f43cbc2f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404384 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404385 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404384 1069 "q-86758" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404384 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404384 1071 "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda $ of the matrix \n$O=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404384 1072 #uuid "8b75d1ac-303a-511c-86a2-e86c1eaa7201" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404384 1074 "First, we find the matrix $\\,O-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nO-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is given by $det(O-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st row, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(O-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 1 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1-\\lambda  \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}+1)+(\\lambda +1) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda +2 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to solve this equation. We find the first root by testing some values. According to the rational zeros theorem, a list of good first guesses consists of all divisors of $2:$ \n\n$$\n\\pm 1,\\pm 2\n$$\n\nLet's pick $x=1.$ Substituting to the characteristic equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1)^{3}+2(1)^{2}-(1)-2 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $\\lambda =1$ is a root of the equation. So, we can factor $(\\lambda -1)$ out of ${\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -2$ using synthetic division:\n\n| $1$ | $1$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $-2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $↓$ | $1$ | $3$ | $2$ |\n|  | $1$ | $3$ | $2$ | $0$ |\n\nSo, we obtain the following factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda -1)({\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda +2) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda +1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=1,$ $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-2,\\,$ and $\\,{\\lambda }_{3}=-1.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404385 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404386 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404385 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404387 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404385 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404388 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404385 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404389 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404385 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404390 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404385 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404385 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404385 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404389 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404385 1080 #uuid "e326b9f3-50f4-5bf4-9fe5-a7fbee316948" 13194139533478 