e complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}(x)=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe particular solution of the inhomogeneous equation cannot be of the form $\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x$ because this is already included in the complementary function. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x} & =(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)+4x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x) \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =8(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x)+16x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n8(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x)+16x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)+16x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)\\,=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n-8\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+8\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}\\beta =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x) \\\\ -8\\alpha =4\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-\\frac{1}{2}$, $\\beta =0.$\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny={y}_{c}+{y}_{p}=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x.\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404447 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404448 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404447 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404449 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404447 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404450 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404447 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404451 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404447 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404452 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404447 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404447 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404447 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404449 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404447 1080 #uuid "9dec29b5-6835-594f-89d3-a76d54e5866b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404448 1081 "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404448 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404448 1084 #uuid "5e77e8eb-4f76-565b-b3a2-5c91767ba39f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404449 1081 "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404449 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404449 1084 #uuid "de87823a-03c0-572e-9778-3d0e131e7ba6" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404450 1081 "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404450 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404450 1084 #uuid "edee0d23-5e90-53e9-9a9b-3e624f83441e"