2186404461 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404460 1069 "q-89821" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404460 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404460 1071 "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{10}{(s-2)(s+3)}.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404460 1072 #uuid "c32439a8-2f0a-52f2-ba4c-04ee07df7da8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404460 1074 "First, we write $F(s)$ as a sum of partial fractions, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\frac{10}{(s-2)(s+3)}=\\frac{2}{s-2}-\\frac{2}{s+3}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{2t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-2},\\,s>2 \\\\ L{{e}^{-3t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+3},\\,s>-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the addition property of the Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{s-2}-\\frac{2}{s+3}} & =2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}}-2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+3}} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t}-2{e}^{-3t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the inverse Laplace transform of $F(s)=\\frac{10}{(s-2)(s+3)}$ is $f(t)=2{e}^{2t}-2{e}^{-3t}.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404461 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404462 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404461 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404463 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404461 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404464 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404461 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404465 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404461 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404466 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404461 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404461 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404461 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404465 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404461 1080 #uuid "aea651d3-f2f0-5676-bbf4-bf4713440432" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404462 1081 "{L}^{-1}{F(s)}=2{e}^{2t}+3{e}^{-3t}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404462 1083 #edb/ref 175921