s line in slope-intercept form, we have\n\n$$\ny=-x+3.\n$$\n\nNow, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\"  inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>-x+3,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\nx+y>3.\n$$\n\nNow consider the line $y=2x.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict.  Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>2x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+y>3 \\\\ y>2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404468 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404469 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404468 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404470 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404468 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404471 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404468 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404472 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404468 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404473 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404468 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404468 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404468 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404473 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404468 1080 #uuid "8c5be21f-60e7-597b-83dc-3c20339aa469" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404469 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}x+y<3 \\\\ y>2x\\end{aligned}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404469 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404469 1084 #uuid "c7c2a5d4-298c-5631-a9d7-aba5b729e118" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404470 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}x+y\\le 3 \\\\ y\\ge 2x\\end{aligned}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404470 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404470 1084 #uuid "01bc8bf9-9741-5be3-bf6c-963968a707d0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 