ties that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y<4x+3 \\\\ y>\\frac{1}{4}x-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404475 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404476 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404475 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404477 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404475 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404478 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404475 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404479 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404475 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404480 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404475 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404475 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404475 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404477 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404475 1080 #uuid "94914b35-e16f-5398-9a50-4baddb153e6e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404476 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le 4x+3 \\\\ y>\\frac{1}{4}x-2\\end{aligned}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404476 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404476 1084 #uuid "57e3339b-5c2d-5e02-8e56-922ef2cb88bc" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404477 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y<4x+3 \\\\ y>\\frac{1}{4}x-2\\end{aligned}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404477 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404477 1084 #uuid "b2167803-87c2-5c4e-aa85-d576aac9cc32" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404478 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y>4x+3 \\\\ y\\ge \\frac{1}{4}x-2\\end{aligned}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404478 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404478 1084 #uuid "aa93daa1-24f9-58db-9545-6bf0487628c5" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404479 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y>4x+3 \\\\ y<\\frac{1}{4}x-2\\end{aligned}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404479 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404479 1084 #uuid "ecf061e8-e3ee-5abf-a78a-299067a79064" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404480 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y>4x+3 \\\\ y>\\frac{1}{4}x-2\\end{aligned}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404480 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404480 1084 #uuid "6051d13a-7c7c-5804-88c5-53711a5cb6ab" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404481 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404482 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404481 1069 "q-90327" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404481 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404481 1071 "![](images/76/762e53967ddb3ccddfa1c9b7a2aa303d66fc1b761c9be8f409c0b91ecb0201de.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities represents the shaded region shown in the graph above?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404481 1072 #uuid "3e5e2c49-2afd-5324-972b-43974f8bfdd9" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404481 1074 "Consider the line $y=x+2.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\le x+2.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=-x+2.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>-x+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y\\le x+2 \\\\ y>-x+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404482 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404483 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404482 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404484 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404482 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404482 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404486 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404482 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404482 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404482 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404482 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404482 1080 #uuid "f86fe5f2-d23c-5598-bb24-07f9f597ec1a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404483 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le x+2 \\\\ y\\ge -x+2\\end{aligned}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404483 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404483 1084 #uuid "daea2326-2376-5164-b217-f74ca9ead6c8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404484 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y>x+2 \\\\ y\\le -x+2\\end{aligned}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404484 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404484 1084 #uuid "8b73faca-4331-5468-aa5b-5f3ece1295f6" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404485 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le x+2 \\\\ y>-x+2\\end{aligned}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404485 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404485 1084 #uuid "83a1c4b0-cc77-5dcc-8de0-37f06af0e319" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404486 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge x+2 \\\\ y<-x+2\\end{aligned}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404486 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404486 1084 #uuid "b45d0b54-a0ec-5724-b49e-549e13b6d4d6" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404487 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y<x+2 \\\\ y\\ge -x+2\\end{aligned}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404487 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404487 1084 #uuid "3d2a88ff-6f4a-5ac9-a039-72c31f12f559" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404488 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404489 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404488 1069 "q-90493" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404488 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404488 1071 "Consider the following differential equation:\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+5{y}^{4}{e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nGiven that the differential equation is exact, which of the following functions could be $P(x,y)?$\n\nI. $10{y}^{5}{e}^{x}+4$\nII. $2{y}^{5}{e}^{2x}-y$\nIII. $2{y}^{5}{e}^{2x}+{e}^{-x}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404488 1072 #uuid "8fa44e0d-f47d-55dc-9787-703e1dcaa8bd" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404488 1074 "A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're given $Q(x,y)=5{y}^{4}{e}^{2x}.$ \n\nFirst, let's differentiate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(5{y}^{4}{e}^{2x})=10{y}^{4}{e}^{2x}\n$$\n\nNow, let's apply $\\frac{∂}{∂y}$ to each of the given options:\n\n- First, we check $P(x,y)=10{y}^{5}{e}^{x}+4.$ This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(10{y}^{5}{e}^{x}+4)=50{y}^{4}{e}^{x}\\ne \\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=10{y}^{5}{e}^{x}+4$ does *not* give an exact equation.\n\n- Next, we check $P(x,y)=2{y}^{5}{e}^{2x}-y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{y}^{5}{e}^{2x}-y)=10{y}^{4}{e}^{2x}-1\\ne \\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=2{y}^{5}{e}^{2x}-y$ does *not* give an exact equation.\n\n- Finally, we check $P(x,y)=2{y}^{5}{e}^{2x}+{e}^{-x}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{y}^{5}{e}^{2x}+{e}^{-x})=10{y}^{4}{e}^{2x}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=2{y}^{5}{e}^{2x}+{e}^{-x}$ gives an exact equation." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404489 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404490 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404489 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404491 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404489 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404492 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404489 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404489 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404494 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404489 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404489 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404489 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404492 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404489 1080 #uuid "210542c5-de8c-5b63-a6a2-7bc9744e8618" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404490 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404490 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404490 1084 #uuid "97ea3ae4-022f-5830-abec-118a76a06fce" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404491 1081 "I only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404491 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404491 1084 #uuid "536feed6-9dfe-5307-aec5-0edb198d16a9" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404492 1081 "III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404492 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404492 1084 #uuid "20fcb72e-c053-5056-a323-074281dda331" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404493 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404493 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404493 1084 #uuid "51bc6cbd-e4d3-52a7-a0e3-484410623715" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404494 1081 "II only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404494 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404494 1084 #uuid "e96fb37a-ec85-52be-af50-069c63122601" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404495 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404496 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404495 1069 "q-90580" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404495 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404495 1071 "Which of the following polynomials are homogeneous?\n\nI. $f(x)=7{x}^{7}$\nII. $g(x,y)=x+y$\nIII. $h(x,y,z)={x}^{2}z-2xyz+x{z}^{2}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404495 1072 #uuid "056f268e-6f23-5cca-ba50-28679fda2fed" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404495 1074 "Let's go through each of the options.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is homogeneous of degree $7.$  It is a polynomial of degree $7,$ with no terms of degree other than $7.$\n\n- The function $g(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $1.$ It is a polynomial of degree $1,$ and all of its terms are of degree $1.$\n\n- The function $h(x,y,z)$ is  homogeneous of degree $3.$ It is a polynomial of degree $3,$ and all of its terms are of degree $3.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404496 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404497 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404496 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404498 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404496 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404496 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404496 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404501 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404496 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404496 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404496 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404497 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404496 1080 #uuid "fa88942a-1208-5ce3-a956-2912d19d6e95" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404497 1081 "I, II, and III" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404497 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404497 1084 #uuid "67cf3cc3-3635-5acb-a7ed-452bb9111c1d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404498 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404498 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404498 1084 #uuid "45d32fb4-03c1-5310-b998-78f449edc9a2" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404499 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404499 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404499 1084 #uuid "497b8fa1-01e8-5353-b89a-f5299641c340" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404500 1081 "None" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404500 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404500 1084 #uuid "dbb2a7c0-0bcf-56f1-9412-5bbd52e46ef8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404501 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404501 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404501 1084 #uuid "52739661-1a40-5904-b3b8-993cc50b384a" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404502 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404503 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404502 1069 "q-90706" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404502 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404502 1071 "Consider the equation ${y}^{″}-{y}^{′}-6y=0$ where $y=y(x).$ If $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ is a solution, then $\\lambda =$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404502 1072 #uuid "a8bfd769-670f-5f6b-bec7-13134d36de0b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404502 1074 "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}-6{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -6) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -6 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -3)=0,\n$$\n\nand so the solutions of the auxiliary equation  are $\\lambda =-2$ or $\\lambda =3.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404503 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404504 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404503 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404505 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404503 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404506 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404503 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404507 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404503 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404508 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404503 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404503 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404503 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404508 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404503 1080 #uuid "117667a9-4c0a-559e-becf-2c255a4fa945" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404504 1081 "$-1$ or $6$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404504 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404504 1084 #uuid "0c59fbbc-2dc0-562b-b432-ce3c7f59dad3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404505 1081 "$-4$ or $2$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404505 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404505 1084 #uuid "c01408ce-3680-5eb5-8582-5d15eb08699d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404506 1081 "$-6$ or $1$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404506 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404506 1084 #uuid "0e45d023-bccd-58f6-9704-f559be5f8da8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404507 1081 "$-3$ or $2$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404507 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404507 1084 #uuid "1b463397-33ab-5e64-907b-e8904f8a0935" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404508 1081 "$-2$ or $3$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404508 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404508 1084 #uuid "d6e036bd-fcc3-5ff2-9e88-b80ab4086884" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404509 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404510 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404509 1069 "q-90725" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404509 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404509 1071 "Given that $y=y(x)$ satisfies the equation ${y}^{″}+8{y}^{′}+15y=0,$ which of the following **cannot** be $y(x)?$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404509 1072 #uuid "ec0270d1-70c2-5347-87eb-345d880dbd64" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404509 1074 "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+8\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+15{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +15) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +15 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda +5)=0,\n$$\n\nand so the solutions of the auxiliary equation  are $\\lambda =-3$ or $\\lambda =-5.$\n\nTherefore, any linear combination of the functions ${e}^{-3x}$ and ${e}^{-5x}$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only ${e}^{5x}$ is not a solution." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404510 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404511 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404510 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404512 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404510 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404513 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404510 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404514 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404510 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404515 1