17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404644 1071 "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)=9{x}_{1}^{2}-18{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+16{x}_{2}^{2}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n\\boxed{}\\,{y}_{1}^{2}+7{y}_{2}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what is missing from the blank spaces?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404644 1072 #uuid "106b083d-c143-5f48-8526-3cd804d072e3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404644 1074 "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and factor out the coefficient of ${x}_{1}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =9{x}_{1}^{2}-18{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+16{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =(9{x}_{1}^{2}-18{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+16{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =9({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+16{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+16{x}_{2}^{2} & =9([{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}]-{x}_{2}^{2})+16{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =9(({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2})+16{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9(({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2})+16{x}_{2}^{2} & =9({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}-9{x}_{2}^{2}+16{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =9({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}+7{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n9{y}_{1}^{2}+7{y}_{2}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}={x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ $9\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404645 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404646 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404645 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404647 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404645 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404648 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [175921864046