(t)+{x}_{2}\\cdot {p}_{2}(t)=0.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404732 1072 #uuid "f3490611-7455-53f0-adf9-bb4a980b5cf3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404732 1074 "If the set is linearly dependent, then there exist ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ not both zero such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)=0.\n$$\n\nOtherwise, if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0,$ the set is linearly independent.\n\nSubstituting the given expressions for ${p}_{1}(t)$ and ${p}_{2}(t)$ into the above equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(2+{t}^{2})+{x}_{2}(1+t+{t}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ (2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2})+({x}_{2})t+({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}){t}^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final equation is true for every $t$ if and only if \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we obtain ${x}_{2}=0.$ Substituting this into the third equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=0.$ \n\nTherefore, ${{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ is linearly independent." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404733 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404734 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404733 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404735 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404733 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404736 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404733 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404737 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404733 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404738 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404733 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404733 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404733 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404736 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404733 1080 #uuid "e16bcf78-6512-5a7c-8045-63540d96f2c8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404734 1081 "2" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404734 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404734 1084 #uuid "34273254-8aaf-5d1e-940e-1dde3326290a" 13194