}^{-1},$ which of the following could be matrices $D$ and $P?$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404932 1072 #uuid "2c18b01b-5fe3-525e-a48a-1bfa359e69d8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404932 1074 "Notice that $A=PD{P}^{-1}$ is a diagonalization of the matrix $A.$ So let's apply the diagonalization algorithm to $A.$\n\n**Step 1.** We need to find the eigenvalues of $A.$ Since $A$ is a triangular matrix, its eigenvalues are the entries on the main diagonal. Therefore, the eigenvalues are \n\n$\\,$ ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\lambda }_{2}=-3\\,$ and $\\,{\\lambda }_{3}=0.$\n\n**Step 2.** Now, we need to find an eigenvector basis of $A.$\n\n- Consider $\\lambda =-3.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-(-3)I & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]+3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are two pivot columns (the $1$st and the $2$nd). This implies that we will have $3-2=1$ linearly independent eigenvector corresponding to the current eigenvalue. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({V}_{-3})=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A$ is *not* diagonalizable, since \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({V}_{0})+\\text{dim}({V}_{-3})=1+1=2\\ne 3.\\,\\times \n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404933 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404934 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404933 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404935 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404933 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404936 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404933 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404937 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404933 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404938 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404933 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404933 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404933 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404938 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404933 1080 #uuid "6f28aa99-06f1-5424-8ad8-144ce8c8f37f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404934 1081 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ and $P=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404934 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404934 1084 #uuid "a2dd8f07-48f6-51da-8357-4d18430cf33f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404935 1081 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $P=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404935 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404935 1084 #uuid "f4c972a6-4f1d-52d6-a963-a9daadedf261" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404936 1081 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ and $P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404936 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404936 1084 #uuid "9d90f352-8134-5420-ae6b-5ce885859da6" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404937 1081 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ and $P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404937 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404937 1084 #uuid "5524bf59-8618-5814-b344-b4194f375a26" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404938 1081 "$A$ is not diagonalizable" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404938 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404938 1084 #uuid "e1685bf8-f4c4-527f-9a5c-f2a1148bd6f1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404939 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404940 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404939 1069 "q-97720" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404939 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404939 1071 "Find the center and radius of the osculating circle to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $P(0,4)$ where $t=1,$ given that $‖{r}^{′}(1)‖=3\\pi ,$ and the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ to the curve is\n\n$$\nT(t)=⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi {t}^{2}}{2}),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi {t}^{2}}{2})⟩.\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404939 1072 #uuid "fd2936d9-6a40-5af8-901d-a96142d64a90" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404939 1074 "Since we are given both the value of $‖{r}^{′}(1)‖$ and the unit tangent $T(t),$ we will use the following formula for the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNotice that $r(1)=⟨0,4⟩,$  since the point $P(0,4)$ is at the tip of $r(1).$ \n\nNow, we find ${T}^{′}(t),$ ${T}^{′}(1)$ and $‖{T}^{′}(1)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi {t}^{2}}{2})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi {t}^{2}}{2}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\pi t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi {t}^{2}}{2}),-\\pi t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi {t}^{2}}{2})⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(1) & =⟨-\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})⟩=⟨0,-\\pi ⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-\\pi )^{2}}=\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the radius of curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(1) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{3\\pi }{\\pi }=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal normal vector at $t=1$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(1) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(1)}{‖{T}^{′}(1)‖}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }⟨0,-\\pi ⟩=⟨0,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the center of the osculating circle is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(1)+R(1)N(1) & =⟨0,4⟩+3⟨0,-1⟩=⟨0,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404940 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404941 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404940 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404942 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404940 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404943 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404940 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404944 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404940 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404945 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404940 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404940 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404940 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404944 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404940 1080 #uuid "77606255-ab40-56b2-a453-f732ee8398aa" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404941 1081 "The center is $(0,-1)$ and the radius $3$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404941 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404941 1084 #uuid "8215fc14-563c-5e9c-b543-3b181532b76e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404942 1081 "The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius $3$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404942 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404942 1084 #uuid "42923454-cf65-5ffa-b13a-8454aab9fce9" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404943 1081 "The center is $(0,\\pi )$ and the radius $\\frac{1}{3}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404943 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585