}^{2}+6)-(2x+1)\\cdot 2x}{({x}^{2}+6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}+12-4{x}^{2}-2x}{({x}^{2}+6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12-2x-2{x}^{2}}{({x}^{2}+6)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to find the critical points:\n\n- First, we compute the points where ${f}^{′}(c)=0.$ We set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{12-2x-2{x}^{2}}{({x}^{2}+6)^{2}} & =0 \\\\ 12-2x-2{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+x-6 & =0 \\\\ (x+3)(x-2) & =0 \\\\ x & =-3,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has stationary points at $x=-3$ and $x=2.$\n\n- Second, we note that ${f}^{′}(x)$ exists for all values of $x$ in the domain of $f(x).$ So $f(x)$ has no non-stationary critical points.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the critical points of $f(x)$ are $x=-3$ and $x=2.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404988 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404989 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404988 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404990 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404988 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404991 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404988 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404992 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404988 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404993 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404988 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404988 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404988 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404990 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404988 1080 #uuid "6da6d1b2-a92b-5381-b98b-6a6c794e9358" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404989 1081 "$x=-\\frac{1}{2}$ only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404989 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404989 1084 #uuid "e62997e2-1f0c-5d4b-9eb1-4b41bb6ab374" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404990 1081 "$x=-3$ and $x=2$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186404990 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [1759218640499